0 @I6000000109116519823@ INDI
1 NAME Isabelle /Le Portier de Marigny/ Vicomtesse d'Auge
2 GIVN Isabelle
2 SURN Le Portier de Marigny
2 NSFX Vicomtesse d'Auge
2 _MARNM de Marigny
1 SEX F
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1339
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Her possible marriage to Geoffroy Marcel de Longueuil is not listed in Cawley's bio, below.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/normacre.htm#IsabelleMarignyM1GuillaumeTancarville
2 CONT
2 CONT ISABELLE de Marigny (before 1302-after 1323).  Philippe IV King of France confirmed the marriage contract between “Johanna domina de Tanquarvilla mater Guillelmi de Tanquarvilla filii quondam Roberti cambellani domini de Tanquarvi
2 CONC lla...dicti Guillelmi” and “Ysabellem filiam...Ingerranni domini de Marrignyaco militis et cambellani nostri...qui ont ja passé sept ans”, naming “...monseigneur Drieu de Mellou pour lui et pour son pere, monseigneur Regnaut vidam
2 CONC e d’Amiens, monseigneur Girart et Ferris ses freres, monseigneur Jehan Malet seigneur de Guerarville, Jehan et Guillaume ses fieus, Robert Bertran, monseigneur Guillaume Bertran...” as present for the marriage contract 23 Oct 1309
2 CONC , by charter dated 18 Nov 1309[657].  Her age indicated in this contract suggests that Isabelle could have been from either her father’s first or second marriage.  Philippe IV King of France confirmed the marriage in another chart
2 CONC er dated Feb 1310[658].  Her second marriage is recorded by Père Anselme[659].  Anselme records that Isabelle de Marigny “demandoit sa dot sur la terre de Tancarville en 1323”[660].  The primary source on which this information is
2 CONC  based has not been identified.  
2 CONT
2 CONT m firstly (contract 23 Oct 1309, before Feb 1310) GUILLAUME [VI] de Tancarville, son of ROBERT de Tancarville & his wife Jeanne Mauvoisin (before 1302-[1310/23].  
2 CONT
2 CONT m secondly HUGUES d’Auxy Seigneur de Dompierre, son of JEAN Seigneur d’Auxy & his wife Isabelle de Craon (-after 1337). 
