1 NAME Isabeau /de Clermont/
2 GIVN Isabeau
2 SURN de Clermont
2 _MARNM de Clermont
2 NICK Isabeau de St. Martin
1 NAME Isabeau //
2 GIVN Isabeau
2 SURN de Sant Martin le Gallard
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1310
2 ADDR
3 CITY Saint-Martin-le-Gaillard
3 STAE Duché de Normandie
3 CTRY Framce
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Hija y sucesora del Barón de Saint Martin le Gaillard, descendiente de Guillaume Martel, aliado de Guillermo el Conquistador. 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Isabeau de St. Martin24,18,7,12,18 was also known as Anne Isabeau de Clermont.17 She was also known as Anne Isabelle de Clermont.18 She was also known as Izabel de Saint Martin.20 She was also known as Isabelle de Saint Martin Le 
2 CONC Gaillard.7 She was also known as Izabel de São Martinho.25 She was also known as Isabeau de Clermont.9 She was also known as Isabeau de Saint-Martin.10 She was also known as Anne Izabeau.12 She was born circa 1310 at Saint-Martin-
2 CONC le-Gaillard, Eu, Dieppe, Seine-Maritime, France; Barony of St. Martin.18
2 CONT
2 CONT (Monsieur Pierre Cleret has presented a different genealogy for this line. He states that the wife of Jehan (Jean) de St. Martin, Isabeau's father, was not Isabeau de Harcourt, but Isabelle Martel de Basqueville. Her ancestor was 
2 CONC Guillaume de Basqueville who was married to the great-granddaughter of Herfaut, brother of Duchess Gonor, wife of Richard Sans Peur, 3d Duke of Normandy. Guillaume de Basqueville was the son of Nicolas de Basqueville, whose father
2 CONC , Baldric le Teuton, married a niece of Gilbert de Brionne, who was the grandson of Richard Sans Peur, son of Guillaume Longue Épée, son of Rollon, 1st Duke of Normandy. Nicolas married Albreda, great-granddaughter of Harfaut, sis
2 CONC ter of Guillaume Fitzaubert).26,27,11 She married an unknown person in 1338 at France.28
2 CONT
2 CONT After 1353 Isabeau sold or pretended to sell her inherited castle at Saint-Martin to Mathieu de Braquemont.29 She married Mathieu de Braquemont, son of Regnault de Braquemont (I), after 1357 at France.17,23 Before 1360 in the divi
2 CONC sion of her father's property, the castle must have fallen to Isabeau and, in this way, by the said sale or by her second marriage, passed to the possession of Mathieu de Braquemont. In it then lived Mathieu with his wife and prob
2 CONC ably their children. It followed, however, that meanwhile, war broke out between the King of France and Charles the Bad, King of Navarre, the Braquemonts taking the side of the latter. For this reason, the King of France ordered t
2 CONC hat the castle belonging to Mathieu be seized, and Pierre d'Auxy was charged with the task. Pierre was the son of Hugues d'Auxy, Lord of Dompierre, and his wife Isabeau de Marigny who was descended from the ancient barons of Saint
2 CONC -Martin; he was, therefore, cousin once removed of Isabeau de Saint-Martin. She was still young and attractive. Pierre fell in love with her and sequestered her, perhaps with her consent. An illegitimate child appears to have been
2 CONC  born from this adulterous affair, taking the name of Dompierre and is presumed to be the nobleman of this name who accompanied Jean (IV) in the expedition to the Canary Islands. Enraged by the seizure and by the sequestration and
2 CONC  adultery of his wife, Mathieu killed Pierre, later begging pardon for this crime from the King.30 In 1376 Isabeau put in motion proceedings against various people, including her sisters, proceedings in which she complains of havi
2 CONC ng been wronged in the division of her father's property.29
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Jean de Bethencourt (II) and Isabeau de St. Martin all born at Normandy, France, were as follows:
2 CONT
2 CONT * + 9 i. Jean de Bethencourt (III) was born circa 1339. He married Marie de Bracquemont, daughter of Regnault de Braquemont (I), at the instigation of her brother (Jean's step-father), Mathieu de Braquemont in Jun 1358 at Normandy
2 CONC .
2 CONT
2 CONT * + 10 ii. Jeanne de Bethencourt (I) was born after 1339. She married Pierre de Neuville circa 1355 at France. She married Eustache de Erneville in 1362 at France.
2 CONT
2 CONT * 11 iii. Daughter 2 Bethencourt31,31,31 was born circa 1340.31 She was married in Auge or Angles, producing from this marriage the Demoiselle d'Espreville, the Lords of Vipars (Vipari) and of Maillot (Mailos), and the wife of the
2 CONC  Lord of Angles. According to some, this sister of Jean (III), of unknown name, was the mother of Georges, Henri, and Maciot de Bethencourt.
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Bettencourts 1200-2000 - Generation Five. Disp. em: http://web.meganet.net/bettenco/bett0005.htm#id19940
2 CONT
