1 NOTE Aude was in possession of the castle of Saint-Martin and drew up a deed in which she ceded it and other lands to her sister Jeanne and her nephew Jean (III) for an annual rent of 200 libras torneses (100 paid by each)and the pledg
2 CONC e that, when she died, the buyers would make a payment of 100 libras (50 each) to whom she would indicate in her will. Since Jean died soon after (1364), he was not long in possession of the castle. His son Jean (IV) did not inher
2 CONC it it and it became part of the feudal lands which it had been associated with previously
