2 CONT
2 CONT the year his father died
2 CONT
2 CONT he visited his brother Jean de Bethencourt at Grainville-la-Teinturière when Jean was home on a short visit from the Canary Islands
2 CONT
2 CONT he pledged fealty to King Henry V of England after the English had conquered most of Normandy
2 CONT
2 CONT Regnault was sent as Ambassador to Spain to persuade King Henry III to render obedience to the Pope at Avignon
2 CONT
2 CONT he received, in payment for his services, a house
2 CONT
2 CONT As vassal of the Kings of England and of France, he performed the duties of Chief Treasurer of Normandy (1423) and Commander of the night watch of the streets of Paris (1424), a duty which he lost when the city returned to the pos
2 CONC session of the French in 1436
2 CONT
2 CONT Regnault's goods were increased by the gift which Jean (IV) made him of all his personal fortune
2 CONT
2 CONT Regnault was granted the fief of Béthencourt as well as 500 libras from the revenues of the lands of Granville which were awarded to Aldonce de Bracquemont and her husband Pierre de Rouville
2 CONT
2 CONT a certificate in Latin issued in Paris in favor of Reynaldo de Bettencourt by King Henry VI, King of England who held Paris at that time, refers to his brother as King and Lord of the Canaries
2 CONT
2 CONT he inherited all his brother's goods
