1 NAME Guillaume d'Estouteville, seigneur de Torcy
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1379
1 DEAT
2 DATE 19 NOV 1449
1 OCCU Chevalier, grand maître des arbalêtriers de France, grand maître enquêteur et général réformateur des Eaux et Forêts de France (en 1406 et 1408
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ====FMG: [https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/normacre.htm#GuillaumeEstTorcydied1449 Normandy: Aumâle, Rouen, Eu]
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. '''GUILLAUME d’Estouteville''' ([1379]–19 Nov 1449, bur Torcy). Père Anselme records his parentage, his date of death and place of burial, noting documents dated 1406, 1416 and 1419 in which he was named (no source citations)[7
2 CONC 64]. ''Europäische Stammtafeln'' indicates his birth in 1379[765]. As noted above, documents dated 1411 record Guillaume as Seigneur de Blainville, in the absence of his brother Charles. A document dated 4 Aug 1415 records “''mess
2 CONC ire Louys d’Estouteville chevalier banneret''” at Harfleur with “''ses cousins...les deux fils de Torcy Charles sgr de Blainville et son cadet Guillaume''”[766]. '''Seigneur de Torcy, de Blainville, d’Estoutemont et de Beyne. Gran
2 CONC d-maître et général réformateur des eaux et forêts de France'''.  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' firstly (1400) '''MARIE de Chalon''' Dame de Laignes et de Grisselles, daughter of LOUIS [I] d’Auxerre “''le chevalier vert''” Comte de Tonnerre & his first wife Marie de Parthenay (–[1400/03?]). ''Europäische Stammtafeln'
2 CONC ' records her parentage and marriage[767]. The primary source which confirms the information has not been found.  She is not mentioned by Père Anselme.  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' secondly ([1403?]) as her second husband, '''JEANNE de Doudeauville''' Dame de Garences, de Ponches, de Nouvion et de Caumartin, widow of RAOUL de Raineval, daughter of JEAN “Mansart” du Bois Seigneur de Raincheval [Fienne
2 CONC s] & his wife Jeanne de Créquy ([1380/85?]–[after 14 Feb 1451?]). Père Anselme records her parentage and two marriages[768]. Her Bois/Fiennes family origin is confirmed by the 4 Jul 1444 marriage contract of her daughter Jeanne, c
2 CONC ited below. The age of her son Colart recorded in 1420 suggests the date of her marriage. A register of the Parlement de Paris dated 1404 records a lawsuit brought by “''Guillelmus de Estoutevilla dominus de Blainvilla ac Joanna d
2 CONC e Dondeauvilla eius uxor''” against “''Nicolaum de Dondeauvilla dictum Gadifer scutiferum''”, relating to the successions following the death 30 Nov 1343 of “''defunctus Ioannes dominus de Dondeauvilla''” leaving children “''Ioann
2 CONC em, Nicolaum supradictum, Balduinum et Joannem dictum Gauvain''” and the death 26 Apr 1383 of “''Joannes de Dondeauvilla miles primogenitus''” leaving “''Joanna supradicta filia eius sola''”, noting that the latter married firstly
2 CONC  “''Radulpho de Raineval filio Walerandi de Raineval militis''” by whom she had an only son who died “''post patrem in minori ætate''” and secondly “''Guillelmo præfato''”[769]. ''Europäische Stammtafeln'' records that she died “1
2 CONC 449†”[770]. However, a charter dated 2 Feb 1450 (O.S.?), connected with the marriage contract of her daughter Michelle, records promises made “''feu Messire Guillaume d’Estouteville son…pere et par Madame sa mere, soit par lez de 
2 CONC testament ou autrement''”[771], in which her mother is not “''feue''”, in contrast to her father, suggesting that she may have been living at the time. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Guillaume & his second wife had nine children:'''
2 CONT a) COLART d’Estouteville ([1404?]–[11 Aug 1420/Jul 1427] or [after 1467?])....&c.
2 CONT b) JEAN d’Estouteville ([1405]–Blainville 11 Nov 1494, bur Blainville)....&c.
2 CONT c) MICHELLE d’Estouteville (–[31 May 1476/1480])....&c.
2 CONT d) GUILLAUME d’Estouteville (–after Apr 1449)....&c.
2 CONT e) ESTOUT d’Estouteville (–13 Dec 1476, bur Charlemesnil Sainte-Catherine)....&c.
2 CONT f) ROBERT d’Estouteville (–Paris 3 Jun 1479)....&c.
2 CONT g) JEANNE d’Estouteville (–Gent 5 Sep 1476, bur Bruges Sœurs grises)....&c.
2 CONT h) RAOUL d’Estouteville (–1462)....&c.
2 CONT i) JEANNE d’Estouteville (–1506). Nun 1449.  Prioress of Poissy 1497....&c.
