1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [https://www.myheritage.com/research/record-1-297649311-1-504192/mathieu-ier-ou-ii-de-marly-de-montmorency-dorleans-du-in-myheritage-family-trees?indId=externalindividual-070d15122268ebf9aa65aef55e5d7a4f&mrid=ff1e9
2 CONC 89fddbc8e572e9f3897ecc9e10e Mathieu De Montmorency Seigneur De Marly 1135-1201 08 27]
2 CONT
2 CONT {{https://sites-cf.mhcache.com/t/649/311/297649311/501/501587_168998fbw85iw4f6b2dda4_W_87x128/9BIrLKTjBBNH4NYssPnLfBL_PKY=/.jpg}}
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ''G.      SEIGNEURS de MARLY''
2 CONT https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/parcorroc.htm#MathieuMarlydied1204
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''MATHIEU de Montmorency''', son of MATHIEU [I] Seigneur de Montmorency & his first wife Alix [of England] (-Constantinople 27 Aug 1203, bur Constantinople church of Knights Hospitallers).  "Matheus de Montemorenciaco" donated pr
2 CONC operty to the abbaye du Val, with the consent of "filii mei Buchardus, Theobaldus, Matheus", by charter dated 1160[900].  "Bucardus de Monte Morenciaco" donated money to Notre-Dame des Vaux de Cernay by charter dated to [1160/77],
2 CONC  witnessed by "Teobaldo fratre meo, Matheo fratre meo…"[901].  His parentage is confirmed by the donation to Port-Royal dated Dec 1227 by "Matheus dominus Montismorenciaci" which names "bone memorie Matheus de Monte Morenciaco pat
2 CONC ruus noster et…consanguinei nostri Buchardus et Malliaco filii eiusdem Mathei"[902].  Seigneur de Marly et d'Attichy.  "Matheus dominus Marleii" donated property to Notre-Dame des Vaux de Cernay by charter dated to [1177], witness
2 CONC ed by "Milone de Nielpha…"[903].  “Matheus de Montemorenciaco Marlei dominus” granted exemptions to Bon Port Notre-Dame in “castro nostro Marlei et in terra nostra Mellentii”, with the consent of “uxoris mee Matildis”, by charter 
2 CONC dated 1190[904].  "Matheus de Montemorenciaco dominus Marliaci", leaving on crusade, instructs "Matildis uxor mea" for a pious foundation by charter dated to before 1204[905].  The necrology of Port-Royal records the death "VI Kal
2 CONC  Sep" of "mons. Mathieu de Marly"[906].  Geoffroy de Villehardouin records the death of “Mathius de Monmorenci...uns des meillors chevaliers del roiaume de France” from illness and his burial “à une yglise de monseignor Saint Joha
2 CONC n de l’Hospital de Jerusalem”[907].  This passage immediately precedes the record of an expedition led by “l’empereres Alexis” [Alexios IV Angelos, crowned co-emperor 1 Aug 1203] and well before the narrative of the crusaders’ cap
2 CONC ture of Constantinople in early 1204.  Mathieu’s death can therefore be dated to 1203. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' ( [1189/90] ) as her second husband, MATHILDE de Garlande, widow of HUGUES de Gallardon Seigneur de Gallardon, daughter of GUILLAUME de Garlande & his wife Idoine de Chaumont (-16 Mar 1224).  “Matheus de Montemorenciaco Ma
2 CONC rlei dominus” granted exemptions to Bon Port Notre-Dame in “castro nostro Marlei et in terra nostra Mellentii”, with the consent of “uxoris mee Matildis”, by charter dated 1190[908].  "Matildis filia Willelmi de Garlanda et Idonee
2 CONC  uxoris sue et uxor domini Mathei de Montemorenciaco" founded the priory of Notre-Dame de Gournay on the anniversary of her father by charter dated after Jul 1191[909].  A charter dated Mar 1193 (O.S.) records an agreement between
2 CONC  Notre-Dame de Josaphat and “dominam Mathildim uxorem domini Mathei de Montemorenciaco” concerning “molendino de Galardone...in loco...Richebort” acquired by “Hugo de Galardone et predicta M. quondam eius uxor”, and the confirmati
2 CONC on by Mathilde and her second husband, with the consent of “filiis eorum Burchardo, Matheo, Guillelmo” of a donation made by “sepedictus H. de Galardone”[910].  "Domina Matildis de Maliaco, Buchardus filius eius et Matheus frater 
2 CONC eius" witnessed a donation to Port-Royal by "dominus Paganus de Ursinis" by charter dated Aug 1204[911].  The Historia Albigensium of Pierre de Vaux-Cernay records that "mater Buchardi de Marliaco" escaped from "Minerbam" after th
2 CONC e castle surrendered to Raymond VI Comte de Toulouse in 1210[912].  "Bucherius Malliaci dominus…et M uxor mea et domina M mater mea" donated property to Port-Royal by charter dated 1218[913].  "Matildis de Marleio" noted a donatio
2 CONC n to Port-Royal by "dominus et maritus noster Matheus de Montemorenciaco" by charter dated Feb 1223/24[914]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT   Matthieu & his wife had four children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.         BOUCHARD ([1190]-11/13 Sep 1226, bur Port-Royal).  m (before Jun 1209) MATHILDE de Châteaufort
2 CONT 2.         MATHIEU ([1191/92]-2 Apr [1249]).  m (before 1212) MABILIE de Châteaufort Dame de Mondeville, 
2 CONT 3.         GUILLAUME ([1192/93]-28/29 Aug [1220]).  Canon at Paris. 
2 CONT 4.         MARGUERITE (-7 Aug [1230]). m ([before 8 Mar 1218] or [Oct 1221/Jul 1223]) as his [third] wife, AIMERY [III] Vicomte de Narbonne
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mathieu_Ier_de_Montmorency
2 CONT
2 CONT Mathieu Ier de Marly (de), il hérite la seigneurie de Marly de son frère Thibaud et devient l'auteur de la branche de Montmorency-Marly ; croisé des troisième et quatrième croisades ; époux de Mathilde de Garlande, il est père de 
2 CONC Bouchard de Marly (dont la fille Isabelle transmet Marly à son mari Guy III de Lévis), et de Marguerite qui épouse Aymeri III de Narbonne.
2 CONT
2 CONT > Mathieu I de Marly inherited the lordship of Marly from his brother Thibaud and became the founder of the Montmorency-Marly branch; a crusader in the Third and Fourth Crusades; husband of Mathilde de Garlande, he was the father 
2 CONC of Bouchard de Marly (whose daughter Isabelle passed Marly on to her husband, Guy III de Lévis) and of Marguerite, who married Aymeri III de Narbonne.
2 CONT
2 CONT See also: https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maison_de_Montmorency
