1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1165
2 ADDR
3 CTRY Cyprus
1 DEAT
2 DATE ABT JUN 1216
1 OCCU Princesse, de Sidon, de Toron, Dame, de Tyr
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} -https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Helvis_of_Ibelin
2 CONT
2 CONT ------
2 CONT
2 CONT -http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/JERUSALEM%20NOBILITY.htm#HelvisIbelinM1RenaudSidonM2GuyMonfort
2 CONT
2 CONT 4.         HELVIS Ibelin ([1182]-before 1 Jun 1216).  The Lignages d'Outremer name (in order) "une fille…Heloys, et un fiz Johan et une autre fille Marguerite, et un fiz Phelippe" as children of "Belleem de Ybelin" & his wife, sta
2 CONC ting that "Heloys" was wife firstly of "Renaut seignor de Seete" and secondly of "Gui de Monfort"[915].  The Chronicle of Alberic de Trois-Fontaines names "uxorem Renaldi de Sidone" as the daughter of "Bethuliani de Guibelin" & hi
2 CONC s wife and her second husband "Guido de Monteforti", but does not name her[916].  The Chronicle of Ernoul records the arrival of "li quens Simons de Montfort, et Guis ses freres" in Palestine [in 1204] and that "Guis prist à feme 
2 CONC le dame de Saiete"[917].  "Guido de Monteforti" donated property to "ecclesiæ de Pruliano", with the consent of "uxoris Alicis Sidoniæ dominæ", by charter dated 1 Jun 1216[918].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' firstly ([1195]) as his second wife, RENAUD Garnier Lord of Sidon, son of GERARD Garnier Lord of Sidon & his wife Agnes of Bures-Tiberias (-[Nov 1200/1204]).  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' secondly ([1204]) as his first wife, GUY de Montfort Seigneur de la Ferté-Alais et de Castres-en-Albegeois, son of SIMON [IV] Sire de Montfort & his wife Amicie of Leicester (-killed in battle Vareilles near Pamiers 31 Jan
2 CONC  1228, bur Abbaye de Haute-Bruyère). 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------
2 CONT
2 CONT The family of Guy de MONTFORT and Helvise d'YBELIN
2 CONT
2 CONT [129213] MONTFORT (de), Guy (Simon II & Amicie de LEYCESTRE [133902]), seigneur de Castres et de La Ferté-Alais
2 CONT
2 CONT * married 1202 fin
2 CONT
2 CONT YBELIN (d'), Helvise (Balian II d'IBELIN & Marie COMNÈNE [132085])
2 CONT
2 CONT       1) Philippe Ier, seigneur de Castres en Albigeois, de la Ferté-Aleps en Beauce et de Tyr en Levant, married about 1225 Éléonore de COURTENAY, married about 1230 Marie d'ANTIOCHE
2 CONT
2 CONT Bibliographie : Histoire de la maison royale de France (Père Anselme); Mémoires (Société généalogique canadienne-française) 
