1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ====FMG: England Earls Created [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/ENGLISH%20NOBILITY%20MEDIEVAL.htm#AmicieBreteuilLeicesterdied1215 1067-1122]
2 CONT * 4. '''AMICE''' (–3 or 10 Sep 1215, bur Abbaye de Haute-Bruyère). A history of the foundation of St Mary’s abbey, Leicester names “''Amiciam primogenitam…et Margaritam juniorem''” as the two daughters of “''Robertus''” and his wi
2 CONC fe “''Petronillam filiam Hugonis de Grantmenyl''”, adding that Amice married “''domino Symoni de Monteforti''”[1724]. The Chronicle of Alberic de Trois-Fontaines refers to the mother of "''comes Symon Montisfortis et Guido frater 
2 CONC eius"'' as "''Guilelmum comitem Licestrie…sorore''" but does not name her[1725]. "''Simon de Monte Forti''" donated money from "''Rochefort''" to Notre-Dame des Vaux de Cernay, with the consent of "''Amicia uxore mea''", by charte
2 CONC r dated to [1180][1726]. A charter dated Feb 1199 recalls a donation to the leprosery of Grand-Beaulieu near Chartres by "''Amauricus de Monteforti''", with the consent of "''Amauricus parvus filius eiusdem Amaurici, qui erat sub 
2 CONC custodia Amaurici de Mestenon''", confirmed after his death by "''Simon frater eius et successor''", and a later donation by "''Simon iste comes Ebroicensis et Mahaudis'' [presumably an error for ''Amicia] uxor eius''"[1727]. She 
2 CONC styled herself Ctss of Leicester after the death of her brother Robert. She surrendered Breteuil to Philippe II King of France in 1206 in return for other lands[1728]. Her second marriage is confirmed by the necrology of the Prieu
2 CONC ré de Fontaines which shows that she had a daughter by her second husband when it records the death "23 Dec" of "''domina Ameza…monacha, Willelmi de Barris et comitisse Montis Fortis filia''"[1729]. The necrology of Chartres cathe
2 CONC dral records the death "''IV Id Sep''" of "''Amicia…comitissa Liecestrie et domina Montisfortis''"[1730]. The necrology of Haute-Bruyère lists members of the Montfort family who are buried in the abbey, including "…''comte Simon…e
2 CONC t de sa femme la contesse Amicie''…"[1731]. 
2 CONT * '''m''' firstly (before [1170] ) [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/NORMANDY%20NOBILITY.htm#SimonIVEvreuxB '''SIMON''' {IV} '''de Montfort'''], son of SIMON [III] de Montfort Seigneur de Montfort et de Rochefort & his wife Mathild
2 CONC e —– (–before 13 Jan 1188, bur Abbaye de Haute-Bruyère). He succeeded his father in 1181 as Seigneur de Montfort-l'Amaury.  
2 CONT * '''m''' secondly (before 13 Jan 1188) [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/parcorroc.htm#GuillaumeIIBarresRochefortdied1234 '''GUILLAUME''' {II} '''des Barres'''] Comte de Rochefort, Seigneur d’Oissery et de la Ferté-Alais, son of G
2 CONC UILLAUME [I] des Barres Seigneur d’Oissery-les-Meaux et de Saint-Pathus[1732] & his first wife —– (–Fontaine-les-Nonnes 23 Mar 1234, bur Fontaine-les-Nonnes).
