2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/NORMAN%20NOBILITY.htm#SimonIVEvreuxB
2 CONT
2 CONT (-1187 or before, bur Abbaye de Haute-Bruyère).  Robert of Torigny records the death in 1182 of "Simon comes Ebroicensis" and the succession "in comitatu Ebroicensis in Normannia" of "Amalricus filius eius" and "in comitatu de Roc
2 CONC ha et in terra Francie" of "Simon alter filius eius"[1632].  He succeeded his father in 1181 as Seigneur de Montfort-l'Amaury.  A charter dated Feb 1199 recalls a donation to the leprosery of Grand-Beaulieu near Chartres by "Amaur
2 CONC icus de Monteforti", with the consent of "Amauricus parvus filius eiusdem Amaurici, qui erat sub custodia Amaurici de Mestenon", confirmed after his death by "Simon frater eius et successor", and a later donation by "Simon iste co
2 CONC mes Ebroicensis et Mahaudis [presumably an error for Amicia] uxor eius"[1633].  The necrology of Haute-Bruyère lists members of the Montfort family who are buried in the abbey, including "…comte Simon…et de sa femme la contesse Am
2 CONC icie…"[1634].  
2 CONT
2 CONT m (before [1170]) as her first husband, AMICIE of Leicester, daughter of ROBERT de Breteuil Earl of Leicester & his wife Pernelle de Grantmesnil (-3 or 10 Sep 1215, bur Abbaye de Haute-Bruyère).  The Chronicle of Alberic de Trois-
2 CONC Fontaines refers to the mother of "comes Symon Montisfortis et Guido frater eius" as "Guilelmum comitem Licestrie…sorore" but does not name her[1635].  A history of the foundation of St Mary´s abbey, Leicester names “Amiciam primo
2 CONC genitam…et Margaritam juniorem” as the two daughters of “Robertus” and his wife “Petronillam filiam Hugonis de Grantmenyl”, adding that Amice married “domino Symoni de Monteforti”[1636].  "Simon de Monte Forti" donated money from 
2 CONC "Rochefort" to Notre-Dame des Vaux de Cernay, with the consent of "Amicia uxore mea", by charter dated to [1180][1637].  A charter dated Feb 1199 recalls a donation to the leprosery of Grand-Beaulieu near Chartres by "Amauricus de
2 CONC  Monteforti", with the consent of "Amauricus parvus filius eiusdem Amaurici, qui erat sub custodia Amaurici de Mestenon", confirmed after his death by "Simon frater eius et successor", and a later donation by "Simon iste comes Ebr
2 CONC oicensis et Mahaudis [presumably an error for Amicia] uxor eius"[1638].  She married secondly (before 13 Jan 1188) Guillaume [II] des Barres Comte de Rochefort, by whom she had a daughter as shown by the necrology of the Prieuré d
2 CONC e Fontaines which records the death "23 Dec" of "domina Ameza…monacha, Willelmi de Barris et comitisse Montis Fortis filia"[1639].  She styled herself Ctss of Leicester after the death of her brother Robert.  She surrendered Brete
2 CONC uil to Philippe II King of France in 1206 in return for other lands[1640].  The necrology of Chartres cathedral records the death "IV Id Sep" of "Amicia…comitissa Liecestrie et domina Montisfortis"[1641].  The necrology of Haute-B
2 CONC ruyère lists members of the Montfort family who are buried in the abbey, including "…comte Simon…et de sa femme la contesse Amicie…"[1642].  
2 CONT
2 CONT Simon & his wife had three children
2 CONT
