1 NOTE {geni:about_me} "Guillaume Bertrand (died 19 May 1356) was a French prelate of the 14th century.
2 CONT -Biography-
2 CONT Coming from the Bertrand family, he was the son of Robert VI Bertrand de Bricquebec, Baron de Bricquebec, and Ide de Clermont-Nesle, and the brother of Marshal Robert VII Bertrand de Bricquebec.
2 CONT Guillaume Bertrand was canon at Beaune and bishop of Noyon from 1331 to 1338, then bishop of Bayeux (1338-1347) and bishop of Beauvais (1347-1356).
2 CONT In 1346 he defended the Chateau de Caen, where the king established him commander when the king of England besieged it."
2 CONT [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Guillaume_Bertrand]
