1 NOTE {geni:about_me} from MEDLANDS 
2 CONT
2 CONT ROBERT [VI] d’Estouteville, son of ROBERT [V] Seigneur d’Estouteville & his wife Alix Bertrand (-after 1330).  Seigneur d’Estouteville et de Vallemont. 
2 CONT
2 CONT m MARGUERITE de Hotot Dame de Hotot, de Berneval et de Vasqueil, daughter of NICOLAS Seigneur de Hotot & his wife Isabelle de Ferrières Dame de Saint-Martin-le-Gaillard.  Père Anselme records her parentage and marriage without cit
2 CONC ing any source on which this information is based[377].  Robert [VI] & his wife had children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.         ROBERT [VII] d’Estouteville (-[11 Jul] 1396).  Seigneur d’Estouteville et de Vallemont.  m (contract Paris Jan 1352, 30 Nov 1356) MARGUERITE de Montmorency, daughter of CHARLES [I] Seigneur de Montmorency & his second w
2 CONC ife Jeanne de Roucy Dame de Blason et de Chimeliers-en-Anjou (after 1339-after 21 Sep 1406).  Robert [Vii] & his wife had children:  a)         JEAN [II] d’Estouteville (-[1436]).  Seigneur d’Estouteville, de Vallemont et de Hotot
2 CONC .  m MARGUERITE d’Harcourt Dame de Longueville et de Plaines, daughter of JEAN [VI] Comte d’Harcourt & his wife Catherine de Bourbon (Harcourt 11 Apr 1377-).  Jean [II] & his wife had children:  i)          LOUIS d’Estouteville (-
2 CONC 21 Aug 1464)).  Seigneur d’Estouteville, de Vallemont et de Hotot.  Grand bouteiller de France.  -         see below.  ii)         GUILLAUME d’Estouteville (-Rome 22 Dec 1483, bur Rome St. Augustine’s convent).  Archbishop of Roue
2 CONC n.  Cardinal.  b)         GUILLAUME d’Estouteville (-after 1394).  Bishop of Evreux.   c)         ISABELLE d’Estouteville (-after 28 Oct 1438).  Her parentage and second marriage are confirmed by the following document: [her son] 
2 CONC “Robert de Bethune chevalier seigneur de Marueil en Brie, d’Hostel et de Baye” and “madame Isabel de Bethune sa seur femme...de...Iacques seigneur de Hans et des Armoises chevalier” agreed the succession of “monseigneur Iehan de B
2 CONC ethune chevalier iadis seigneur desdits lieux...et madame Isabel d’Estouteville leurs pere et mere”, noting property inherited from “feuë madame Marguerite de Montmorency dame d’Estouteville” by “ladite madame Isabel d’Estoutevill
2 CONC e sa fille...”, by charter dated 29 May 1441[378].  m firstly GAUTHIER de Vienne Seigneur de Mirebel, son of JEAN de Vienne & his wife --- ([1378]-killed in battle Nikopolis 1396).  m secondly (contract 8 Nov 1401) JEAN de Béthune
2 CONC  Seigneur de Locres et de Mareuil, son of JEAN de Béthune Seigneur de Vendeuil & his first wife Jeanne de Coucy (-killed in battle Agincourt 25 Oct 1415).  m thirdly (after 1415) as his second wife, HENRI [III] Seigneur de Hans, s
2 CONC on of HENRI [II] Seigneur de Hans & his wife Beatrix de Commercy (-after 1436. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 2.         COLART d’Estouteville (-after 16 Nov 1346).  Seigneur d’Aussebosc.  m (16 Mar 1338) as her third husband, JEANNE de la Tournelle Dame de Tournelle, de Raulot, de Montdesir et de Mainvilliers, widow firstly of JEAN [I] d
2 CONC e Montmorency Seigneur de Beausault, de Breteuil, and secondly of FLORENT de Varennes Seigneur de Grandville, daughter of ROBERT Seigneur de la Tournelle & his wife Marie de Ferrières (-27 May [1373], bur Valmont).  Père Anselme n
2 CONC ames her as wife of Louis d’Harcourt but cites no source on which the information is based[379].  She married fourthly Louis d’Harcourt Vicomte de Châtellerault.  Colart & his wife had children:  -        SEIGNEURS d’AUSSEBOSC[380
2 CONC ]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 3.         RAOUL d’Estouteville (-Cocherel 1383).  Seigneur de Rames.  m as her second husband, MARGUERITE d’Harcourt, widow of ROBERT de Boulainvilliers Seigneur de Chepoy, daughter of [JEAN [IV] Seigneur d’Harcourt & his wife Is
2 CONC abelle de Parthenay].  Père Anselme states that Marguerite was daughter of Jean [II] Seigneur d’Harcourt & his wife Jeanne Vicomtesse de Châtellerault and records her marriages, but provides no source citation[381].  Considering t
2 CONC he marriages of her second husband’s brothers dated 1352 and 1338, it is chronologically impossible for the wife of Raoul d’Estouteville to have been the daughter of Jean [II] d’Harcourt.  If Marguerite was a member of the Harcour
2 CONC t family, it is possible chronologically that she was the daughter of Jean [IV].  Raoul & his wife had children:  a)         ROBERT d’Estouteville .  Père Anselme records his parentage[382].  Seigneur de Rames.  -        SEIGNEURS
2 CONC  de RAMES[383].  b)         JEANNE d’Estouteville (-after 1391).  La Roque (citing “Monsieur le President Bigot en ses Memoires“) says that “Robert d’Estouteville Seigneur de Remmes” consented to “Jeanne d’Estouteville sa sœur fil
2 CONC le de Raul d’Estouteville Seigneur de Remmes et femme de Jean de Harcourt Sire de Charentonne son beau-frere” retaining revenue from “la terre de Remmes” due under their marriage contract[384].  La Roque (citing “Registrum manuale
2 CONC  placitorum et negociorum Scacarii Normanniæ“ dated [29 Sep] 1390 at Rouen) records “Pierre Mauvoisin escuier” claiming against the chapter of Evreux and “dame Jeanne d’Estouteville iadis femme de feu monsieur Jean de Harcourt che
2 CONC valier”[385].  La Roque (citing “Eschiquier de Pasques l’an 1391“) records “madame Jeanne d’Estouteville veufve de messire Jean de Harcourt jadis chevalier et dame de Charentonne, messire Jean Dacy dit petit Galois chevalier et he
2 CONC ritier de messire Jean de Harcourt jadis chevalier”[386].  m JEAN d’Harcourt Seigneur de Charentonne, son of RAOUL [II] d’Harcourt Seigneur de Charentonne & his wife Eléonore [Jeanne?] de Sacquenville (-[1387/Sep 1390]). 
2 CONT
2 CONT 4.         NICOLAS d’Estouteville (-1361 or before).  Seigneur du Bouchet.   -        SEIGNEURS du BOUCHET[387].  —————————————————
2 CONT
2 CONT  Bibliography 
2 CONT
