2 CONT GUILLAUME [III] de Tancarville, son of GUILLAUME [II] de Tancarville....  "Willelmus camerarius de Tancharvilla, filius Rabelli" confirmed the purchase of land at Bretteville from the church of Bayeux, with the consent of "Willelm
2 CONC um filium meum", by charter dated to [1182/1205][841].  The dating clause of a charter of Guillaume [III] records “primo anno in quo Philippus rex Francorum habuit dominium Normanniæ...MCCIV”[842].  "Guillaume Chambellan de Tancar
2 CONC ville" donated land "à Iz" to the priory of Sainte-Barbe, at the request of "Alix sa femme", by undated charter witnessed by "Guillaume de Séran, frère de la dite Alix"[843]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT m ALIX de Serans, daughter of ---.  "Guillaume Chambellan de Tancarville" donated land "à Iz" to the priory of Sainte-Barbe, at the request of "Alix sa femme", by undated charter witnessed by "Guillaume de Séran, frère de la dite 
2 CONC Alix"[844].  Philippe II King of France confirmed the marriage contract between “Guillelmus cambellanus de Tancarvilla...Isabella filia sua” and “Adæ filio...Galterii junioris camerarii nostri” by charter dated 1205, which provide
2 CONC d for an increase in the dowry if Guillaume de Tancarville had no male heir “ex Alliz uxore sua” and if “Marsilia sororia ipsius” died[845]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Guillaume [III] & his wife had two children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.         ISABELLE de Tancarville (-[1214]).  Philippe II King of France confirmed the marriage contract between “Guillelmus cambellanus de Tancarvilla...Isabella filia sua” and “Adæ filio...Galterii junioris camerarii nostri” by
2 CONC  charter dated 1205, which provided for an increase in the dowry if Guillaume de Tancarville had no male heir “ex Alliz uxore sua” and if “Marsilia sororia ipsius” died[846].  m (1205) as his first wife, ADAM [I] de Villebéon, son
2 CONC  of GAUTHIER [II] Seigneur de Villebéon & his wife Elisabeth --- ([1183/85]-28 Jan 1235, bur Jard). 
2 CONT
2 CONT 2.         RAOUL [III] de Tancarville (after 1205-).  Raoul was born after 1205, the date of his sister’s marriage contract which specifies that her father had no male heir (see above).  The primary source which confirms his paren
2 CONC tage has not been identified.  m ---.  The name of Raoul’s wife is not known.  Raoul [III] & his wife had one child: 
2 CONT
2 CONT >a)         GUILLAUME [IV] de Tancarville (-after 1268).  The primary source which confirms his parentage has not been identified.  He is named as deceased in the 1283 charter of his son Guillaume [V] (see below).  m AUDE, daughte
2 CONC r of --- (-before 1283).  She is named as deceased in the 1283 charter of her son Guillaume [V] (see below).  Guillaume [IV] & his wife had four children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT >>i)          RAOUL [IV] de Tancarville (-[21 Sep 1275/1283]).  Raoul [IV] donated property to Saint-Georges de Bocherville by charter dated 21 Sep 1275[847].  He is named as deceased in the 1283 charter of his brother Guillaume [
2 CONC V] (see below). 
2 CONT
2 CONT >>ii)         GUILLAUME [V] de Tancarville (-after 1283).  Guillaume [V] donated property to Saint-Georges de Bocherville, for the souls of “sa mère Aude, de son père Guillaume et de son frère Raoul chevaliers décédés” by charter 
2 CONC dated 1283[848]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT >>iii)        ROBERT de Tancarville (-killed in battle Courtrai 11 Jul 1302).  The primary source which confirms his parentage has not been identified.  Robert confirmed donations of “la dîme des forêts de Fécamp, de Lillebonne, d
2 CONC e Tancarville et de Montebourg...celle du manoir de Saint-Martin sous Tancarville [et] la dîme du port de Tancarville” to Saint-Georges de Bocherville by charter dated 1297[849].  The Chronique Artésienne records “li camberlens de
2 CONC  Tancarvile” among those killed at the battle of Courtrai 11 Jul 1302[850].  m JEANNE Mauvoisin, daughter of GUY [VII] Mauvoisin Seigneur de Mello & his wife Isabelle de Mello (-after Feb 1310).  She is named in the marriage contr
2 CONC act of her son:  Philippe IV King of France confirmed the marriage contract between “Johanna domina de Tanquarvilla mater Guillelmi de Tanquarvilla filii quondam Roberti cambellani domini de Tanquarvilla...dicti Guillelmi” and “Ys
2 CONC abellem filiam...Ingerranni domini de Marrignyaco militis et cambellani nostri...qui ont ja passé sept ans” by charter dated 18 Nov 1309[851].  Her family origin is indicated in the following document:  Philippe IV King of Francer
2 CONC  granted “le bailh et toute la garde des enfans de Robert jadis chambellane de Tanquarville chevalier”, noting specifically “[le] mariage de Guillaume ainzné fieus dudit Robert”, to “Engerran de Marreigni nostre...chevalier et cha
2 CONC mbellene”, reserving the assets of “Jehanne de Roony, femme jadis dudit Robert”, by charter dated Feb 1310[852].  Thomas indicates her precise parentage, adding that she was her father’s oldest daughter[853].  Robert & his wife ha
2 CONC d two children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>(a)       JEANNE de Tancarville (-before 1327).  The primary source which confirms her parentage and marriage has not been identified.  m ([1316]) as his first wife, JEAN [I] Vicomte de Melun, son of ADAM de Melun Seigneur de M
2 CONC ontreuil-Belloy & his wife Jeanne de Sully (-1350, bur Jard). 
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>(b)       GUILLAUME [VI] de Tancarville (before 1302-[1310/23]).  Philippe IV King of Francer granted “le bailh et toute la garde des enfans de Robert jadis chambellane de Tanquarville chevalier”, noting specifically “[le] mari
2 CONC age de Guillaume ainzné fieus dudit Robert”, to “Engerran de Marreigni nostre...chevalier et chambellene”, reserving the assets of “Jehanne de Roony, femme jadis dudit Robert”, by charter dated Feb 1310[854].  m (contract 23 Oct 1
2 CONC 309, before Feb 1310) as her first husband, ISABELLE de Marigny, daughter of ENGUERRAND [II] Seigneur de Marigny, Chambellan de France & his [first wife Jeanne ---/second wife Hawise [Alix] de Mons[-sur-Seine]] (before 1302-after 
2 CONC 1323).  Philippe IV King of France confirmed the marriage contract between “Johanna domina de Tanquarvilla mater Guillelmi de Tanquarvilla filii quondam Roberti cambellani domini de Tanquarvilla...dicti Guillelmi” and “Ysabellem f
2 CONC iliam...Ingerranni domini de Marrignyaco militis et cambellani nostri...qui ont ja passé sept ans”, naming “...monseigneur Drieu de Mellou pour lui et pour son pere, monseigneur Regnaut vidame d’Amiens, monseigneur Girart et Ferri
2 CONC s ses freres, monseigneur Jehan Malet seigneur de Guerarville, Jehan et Guillaume ses fieus, Robert Bertran, monseigneur Guillaume Bertran...” as present for the marriage contract 23 Oct 1309, by charter dated 18 Nov 1309[855].  P
2 CONC hilippe IV King of France confirmed the marriage in another charter dated Feb 1310[856].  She married secondly Hugues d’Auxy Seigneur de Dompierre.  Her second marriage is recorded by Père Anselme[857].  Anselme records that Isabe
2 CONC lle de Marigny “demandoit sa dot sur la terre de Tancarville en 1323”[858].  The primary source on which this information is based has not been identified. 
2 CONT
2 CONT >>iv)       AUDE (-after 1267).  Guillaume [IV] granted revenue “à prendre sur la prévôté de Saint-Romain” to “sa fille Aude” by charter dated 1267[859]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
