1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Jeanne de Fayel32,100,100 was also known as Jeanne du Fayel.9 She was born after 1370 at Champagne, France.32,135 Her dowry was relatively modest. It consisted of the fief and lands of Saclas in the region of Béauc
2 CONC e, near Éstampes, and an annual rent of 200 pounds which she had inherited from her maternal grandfather, the Count of Porcin. Perhaps because of the difficulty of maintaining those estates, situated far from his home, her husband
2 CONC  Jean sold them after three years.100 She died before 1425.149,148
2 CONT
2 CONT There were no children of Jean de Bethencourt (IV) and Jeanne de Fayel.
2 CONT
2 CONT Dona Maria de Ayala e Vargas150 was born circa 1370 at Seville, Spain.150
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Jean de Bethencourt (IV) and Dona Maria de Ayala e Vargas were:
2 CONT
2 CONT * 21 i. Floridas Bethencourt150,150,150 was born illegitimate circa 1405 at Seville, Spain.150 After being acknowledged by his father, he was brought to the Canary Islands.150
2 CONT
2 CONT Françoise de Calletot136 was born circa 1375 at France.136
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Jean de Bethencourt (IV) and Françoise de Calletot were:
2 CONT
2 CONT * 22 i. Jacques de Bethencourt136,136,136 was born circa 1410 at France.136 He married Marie d' Estoutteville-Villebon at France.136
2 CONT
2 CONT Marie d' Estoutteville-Villebon136 was born circa 1410 at France.136
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Bettencourts 1200-2000 - Generation Seven. Dsip. em: http://web.meganet.net/bettenco/bett0007.htm#id19335
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Guillaume de Fayel foi um nobre do Reino de França onde foi Visconde de Breteuil na localidade francesa, situada no Departamento francês de Marne na região de Champagne-Ardenne.
2 CONT
2 CONT Relações familiares
2 CONT
2 CONT Foi casado com Margarida de Chatillon de quem teve:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Philippote Fayel, foi senhora de Troyes (Troyes, Bretanha, França, 1370 -?) casou em 14 de julho de 1422 com Regnault de Bettencourt IV (1365 – 1443). [1]
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Jeanne de Fayel casada em Paris, a 30 de abril de 1392 com Jean de Bettencourt (Héricourt-en-Caux, Grainville-la-Teinturière, Ducado da Normandia, (1362 - 1425), nomeado rei das ilhas Canárias.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Wikipédia, a enciclopédia livre. Disp.em: http://pt.wikipedia.org/wiki/Guillaume_de_Fayel
