1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Peter II of Alençon
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT On October 10, 1371, he married Marie Chamaillart, Viscountess of Beaumont-au-Maine (d. Argentan November 18, 1425). They had eight children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Marie of Alencon (29 March 1373–1417), married 1390 in Paris John VII of Harcourt, Count of Harcourt and Aumale (d. 1452).
2 CONT
2 CONT Peter (1374–1375)
2 CONT
2 CONT John (1375–1376)
2 CONT
2 CONT Marie (1377)
2 CONT
2 CONT Jeanne (1378–1403, Argentan)
2 CONT
2 CONT Catherine (1380, Verneuil – June 25, 1462, Paris), married 1411 in Alençon Peter d'Évreux, Infante of Navarre and Count of Mortain (1366–1412), married October 1, 1413 in Paris Louis VII, Duke of Bavaria-Ingolstadt (1365–1447)
2 CONT
2 CONT Marguerite (1383 – aft. 1400), became a nun at Argentan
2 CONT
2 CONT John I of Alençon (1385–1415)
