1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Alix/Alice/Aline fitzRoy (d'Angleterre)
2 CONT
2 CONT From Medlands:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/ENGLAND,%20Kings%201066-1603.htm#_Toc272564016
2 CONT
2 CONT '''ALIX [Aline (-before 1141)'''  Guillaume de Jumièges records one illegitimate daughter of King Henry I as wife of "Matthieu fils de Burchard de Montmorency"[240].  m (1126) as his first wife, MATHIEU [I] de Montmorency, son of 
2 CONC BOUCHARD [III] Sire de Montmorency & his first wife Agnès de Beaumont-sur-Oise (-1160).  He succeeded his father as Sire de Montmorency in [1130/32].  Constable of France.  
2 CONT
2 CONT ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
2 CONT
2 CONT Mathieu [I] & his first wife had [five] children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.         [HENRI (-24 Jul before 1160).  The necrology of the abbey of Notre-Dame du Val records the death "IX Kal Aug" of "Henricus de Montemorenciaco"[632].  Duchesne names Henri as oldest son of Mathieu [I] Seigneur de Montmor
2 CONC ency, citing only this necrology entry which gives no indication either of his parentage or the time-frame during which he lived[633].] 
2 CONT
2 CONT 2.         BOUCHARD [IV] (-Jerusalem 1189, bur Abbaye du Val).  The Chronicon Hanoniense names "nobili Buchardo de Montemorenciaco…filium Matheum et filiam Rogerus, Reinaldi de Roseto frater…comitis Hanoniensis consobrinus"[634]. 
2 CONC  "Matheus de Montemorenciaco" donated property to the abbaye du Val, with the consent of "filii mei Buchardus, Theobaldus, Matheus", by charter dated 1160[635].  Seigneur de Montmorency, Seigneur de Conflans-Sainte-Honorine et d'H
2 CONC érouville.  "Bucardus de Monte Morenciaco" donated money to Notre-Dame des Vaux de Cernay by charter dated to [1160/77], witnessed by "Teobaldo fratre meo, Matheo fratre meo…"[636].  Seigneur d'Ecouen 1183.  "Buccardus de Montemor
2 CONC enciaco" confirmed donations made by "Guibertus de Tauerni…" to l’abbaye du Val, with the consent of "fratres mei Theobaldus et Matheus et Herveus clericus, uxorque mea Laurentia et filius meus Matheus et filia mea Eva", by undate
2 CONC d charter[637].  The necrology of the abbey of Notre-Dame du Val records on "XVI Kal Dec" that "Bucardus avus, Bucardus, Theobaldus de Montemorenciaco" died in Jerusalem[638], although it is not clear to which of the three deaths 
2 CONC the date relates.  m (1173) as her second husband, LAURETTE de Hainaut, widow of DIRK van Aalst, daughter of BAUDOUIN IV Comte de Hainaut & his wife Alix de Namur (-9 Aug 1181, bur Abbaye du Val).  The Chronicon Hanoniense names (
2 CONC in order) "Yolandem, Agnetem, Lauretam" as the daughters of "Alidis comitissa Hanonensis …cum viro Balduino comite", specifying that Laurette married "Theodericus de Alost, Iwani de Gandavo et Laurete filius" and secondly "in Fran
2 CONC cia Bucardo de Monte Morenciaco…filium Matheum", recording in a later passage that her second marriage took place "1173 post atavam epiphanie"[639].  The Chronicle of Alberic de Trois-Fontaines names (in order) "comitem Balduinum,
2 CONC  Henricum de Sebu rgo et quatuor sorores" as children of "comiti Balduini de Haynaco", naming one daughter (third among those listed) "Loreta [uxor] Buchardo de Montinorencei" by whom she had "Matheum in curia Francie nominatissim
2 CONC um et comitissam Montisfortis matrem comitis Almarici"[640].  The necrology of the abbey of Notre-Dame du Val records the death "V Id Aug" of "domina Laureta de Montemorenciaco"[641].  Bouchard [IV] & his wife had five children:  
2 CONC a)         MATHIEU [II] "le Grand" (-24 Nov 1230).  The Chronicle of Alberic de Trois-Fontaines names "Matheum in curia Francie nominatissimum et comitissam Montisfortis matrem comitis Almarici" as children of "Loreta [de Haynaco]
2 CONC  [uxor] Buchardo de Montinorencei"[642].  Seigneur de Montmorency, d'Ecouen, de Conflans-Sainte-Honorine et d'Attichy.  Connétable de France 1194.  -        see below.  b)         EVA .  "Buccardus de Montemorenciaco" confirmed do
2 CONC nations made by "Guibertus de Tauerni…" to l’abbaye du Val, with the consent of "fratres mei Theobaldus et Matheus et Herveus clericus, uxorque mea Laurentia et filius meus Matheus et filia mea Eva", by undated charter[643].   c) 
2 CONC         THIBAUT .  The primary source which confirms his parentage has not been identified.   He is not mentioned by Duchesne.  [1220].  d)         ALIX (-25 Feb 1221, bur Abbaye de Haute-Bruyère).  The Chronicle of Alberic de Tro
2 CONC is-Fontaines names "Matheum in curia Francie nominatissimum et comitissam Montisfortis matrem comitis Almarici" as children of "Loreta [de Haynaco] [uxor] Buchardo de Montinorencei"[644].  "Symon comes Leycestrie dominus Montisfor
2 CONC tis…Biterrenensis et Carcasonensis vicecomes" donated property to Notre-Dame de la Trappe with the consent of "A comitissa uxore mea et filiis nostris A et G" by charter dated Jul 1212[645].  The necrology of Port-Royal records th
2 CONC e death "V Kal Jan" of "Alix comtesse de Montfort"[646].  The necrology of Haute-Bruyère lists members of the Montfort family who are buried in the abbey, including "…conte Simon…qui mourut en Albigeois et de la contesse Alix sa f
2 CONC emme…"[647].  m ([1190]) SIMON [V] Seigneur de Montfort, son of SIMON [IV] Seigneur de Montfort & his wife Amicie of Leicester ([1170]-killed in battle Toulouse 25 Jun 1218, bur Abbaye de Haute-Bruyère).  Earl of Leicester.  Duc d
2 CONC e Narbonne, Comte de Toulouse.  e)         JEANNE .  The primary source which confirms her parentage has not been identified.   She is not mentioned by Duchesne.  [1220]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 3.         THIBAUT (-Jerusalem after 1189).  "Matheus de Montemorenciaco" donated property to the abbaye du Val, with the consent of "filii mei Buchardus, Theobaldus, Matheus", by charter dated 1160[648].  "Theobaldi domini castri
2 CONC  de Marli" confirmed donations made by "avo suo Bucardo" to "ecclesiæ S. Eugenii de Diogillo", by charter dated 1160, witnessed by "domino Bucardo fratre suo"[649].  "Bucardus de Monte Morenciaco" donated money to Notre-Dame des V
2 CONC aux de Cernay by charter dated to [1160/77], witnessed by "Teobaldo fratre meo, Matheo fratre meo…"[650].  Seigneur de Marly.  "Theobaldus Marliensis dominus" donated property to Notre-Dame des Vaux de Cernay by charter dated 15 A
2 CONC ug 1173[651].  He joined the crusade in 1173: "Theobaldus dominus Marliaci", on the point of leaving for Jerusalem on pilgrimage, donated property "apud Gunnessam et apud Montem Morenciacum Herveo fratri meo" to Notre-Dame de Pari
2 CONC s, with the consent of “dominus Bucardus frater meus”, by charter dated 1173[652].  He became a Cistercian monk at Notre-Dame du Val in [1177].  The necrology of the abbey of Notre-Dame du Val records on "XVI Kal Dec" that "Bucard
2 CONC us avus, Bucardus, Theobaldus de Montemorenciaco" died in Jerusalem[653], although it is not clear to which of the three deaths the date relates. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 4.         HERVE (-25 Mar 1192).  "Theobaldus dominus Marliaci", on the point of leaving for Jerusalem on pilgrimage, donated property "apud Gunnessam et apud Montem Morenciacum Herveo fratri meo" to Notre-Dame de Paris, with the 
2 CONC consent of “dominus Bucardus frater meus”, by charter dated 1173[654].  "Burchardus dominus Montismorenciaci" confirmed the grant of property made by "frater meus Theobaldus de Marliaco, assumpto peregrinationis Hierosolimitane" t
2 CONC o "Herveo fratri meo" by charter dated 1173[655].  Abbot of Saint-Martin de Montmorency 1174.  Deacon at Paris 1184.  The necrology of Paris Notre-Dame records the death "VIII Kal Apr" of "de domo Sancte Marie...Herveus decanus et
2 CONC  sacerdos", his donations of “prata apud Viri...terram...apud Gonessiam”, and the donation made by “Matheus de Marli frater eiusdem Hervei” for his soul[656]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 5.         MATHIEU (-Constantinople 27 Aug 1204).  "Matheus de Montemorenciaco" donated property to the abbaye du Val, with the consent of "filii mei Buchardus, Theobaldus, Matheus", by charter dated 1160[657].  "Bucardus de Monte
2 CONC  Morenciaco" donated money to Notre-Dame des Vaux de Cernay by charter dated to [1160/77], witnessed by "Teobaldo fratre meo, Matheo fratre meo…"[658].  Seigneur de Marly et d'Attichy. 
