2 CONT 2.       '''  IDOINE de Gisors''' (-[1208]).  A charter dated 1150 records that Louis VII King of France exiled "Theobaldum de Gisortio" who went to “villam suam...Beeleium” with “Willelmum abbatem” who took them to the church of 
2 CONC Saint-Martin de Pontoise, and that while at Le Bellay "Robertus de Relhi" donated “decimam” with the support of “ipsum Theobaldo uxor eius Rohaidis et sororia ejus Mathildis quæ fuerat uxor Hugonis de Gisortio fratris Theobaldi et
2 CONC  filius eiusdem Mathildis Johannes nepos Theobaldi et soror Johannis Idonea”[584].  Her parentage and marriage are indicated by an undated charter under which “Johannes de Gysorcio” donated revenue from “furno meo de Chars” to Liv
2 CONC ry, for the soul of “Anselli nepotis mei”, witnessed by “Guillelmus de Garlanda, Odo de Gysorcio...”[585].  “Guillelmus de Garlanda” donated land “de nemore Talebot et medietatem nemoris de Genesvilla” to Jumièges, with the consen
2 CONC t of “Ydonie uxoris mee et Guillelmi filii mei primogeniti”, by charter dated 26 Aug 1188[586].  “Idonea” donated property to Livry, for the soul of “Vuillelmi de Garlanda quondam viri mei et...filiorum meorum maxime pro anima fil
2 CONC ii mei Theobaldi pro quo abbatia constructa est”, with the consent of “Vuillelmi filii mei”, by charter dated Sep 1205[587].  
2 CONT
