1 NAME Philippe I /de Lévis/ vicomte de Lautrec
2 GIVN Philippe I
2 NSFX vicomte de Lautrec
2 _MARNM de Lévis
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1279
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1304
1 OCCU Vicomte de Lautrec
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} -http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/toulcentw.htm#PhilippeLevisdied1304
2 CONT
2 CONT PHILIPPE de Lévis, son of GUY [III] de Lévis Maréchal de Mirepoix & his wife Isabelle de Marly [Montmorency] (-after 15 Mar 1305).  “Dominus Iohannes de Levis dominus Mirapiscis...cum...domino Theobaldo, Petro, Philippo, Eustachio
2 CONC  et Francisco fratribus” settled a dispute with the inhabitants of Mirepoix concerning the cutting of wood from the forest of Bélène by charter dated 20 Mar 1301[416].  Seigneur de Florensac.  Seigneur de Lévis.  Vicomte de Lautre
2 CONC c.  A charter dated 15 Mar 1304 (O.S.?) ratified a settlement agreed between arbitrators (the convent of Avignon Sainte-Claire and “Petri de Mirapicio dicti de Levis domini de Vilanova”) and “Philippe de Lévis sgr de Florenciaco e
2 CONC t vicomte de Lautrec” concerning “l’hérédité de feu Sic. Alaman chevalier et de Sic. son fils”, claimed by “sororis Magarite Alamanne monache dicti monasterii filieque dicti Sicardi sororisque Sicardii filii condam”[417]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' (contract 19 Sep 1296, Papal dispensation 3 Jun 1297, before 28 Jul 1298) as her first husband, BEATRIX de Lautrec Vicomtesse de Lautrec, daughter of BERTRAND Vicomte de Lautrec & his wife Alasie de Nargeac (-after 21 Mar 
2 CONC 1336).  The marriage contract between “Gui de Lévis sgr de Mirepoix...son fils Philippe de Levis” and “Beatrix vicomtesse de Lautrec...sa mère Aladays”, noting her previous betrothal to “Mathieu de Lévis” and subject to Papal disp
2 CONC ensation, is dated 10 Sep 1296[418].  Pope Boniface VIII issued the dispensation for the marriage 3 Jun 1297, referring to her earlier contract to marry “quondam Matheus de Levis miles frater tuus fili Philippe”[419].  “Alazia fil
2 CONC le de feu...Guill. B. de Najac veuve de Bertr. vic de Lautrec” granted her rights in “castrum nostrum de Savinhaco” to “Beatrix notre fille aînée et héritière universelle dud. Bertr.” by charter dated 30 Jun 1297[420].  She marrie
2 CONC d secondly (before 11 Mar 1311) Bertrand de Goth, who succeeded his father as Vicomte de Lomagne et d’Auvillars.  The date of her second marriage is estimated from the following document: a charter dated 11 Mar 1310 (O.S.) records
2 CONC  a dispute between “Bertrandi de Guto militis vicecomitis Lautricensis” and “dominam A. de Monteforti comitissam Vindocinensem” concerning “loca de Cabanesio”[421].  A charter dated Nov 1313 recorded payment by the convent of Avig
2 CONC non Sainte-Claire to “Bertr. de Guto vicomte de Lomagne et d’Auvillars et...sa demme Béatrix épouse de feu Phil. de Lévis”[422].  "Béatrix de Lautrec" bequeathed money for her future marriage to her daughter Regine, by her testame
2 CONC nt dated 30 Jul 1315[423].  Jean I Comte d´Armagnac, acting for his wife "fille et heritière de feu Bertrand de Goth vicomte de Lomagne et d´Auvillars", assigned a pension to "Béatrix de Lautrec, veuve de Bertrand de Goth" by char
2 CONC ter dated 10 Jun 1324[424].  "Regina de Gutto comitissa Armaniaci Fesenciaci et Ruthenensis vicecomitissaque Leomaniæ et Altavillaris", under her testament dated 12 Aug 1325, appointed "dominæ Beatrici vice-comitissæ Lautricensi m
2 CONC atri suæ…Rogerio de Armaniaco et Domino Amanevo de Lebreto" as her executors[425].  “Beatrix vicomtesse de Lautrec” promised not to dispose of her assets without the consent of “ses fils...Philippe et Bertrand de Lévis”, with the 
2 CONC consent of “...vicomte Guillaume cousin de lad. dame”, by charter dated 28 Nov 1326, and committed to pay certain sums to her sons “pro custodia castri [de La Focz]” where she was living by charter dated 29 May 1327[426].  “Beatri
2 CONC x vic. de Lautrec” ordered her subjects to swear allegiance to “nos fils Philippe et à Bertrand” by charter dated 21 Mar 1335 (O.S.)[427]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT   Philippe & his wife had two children: 
