1 NOTE {geni:about_me} The family of Philippe II de MONTFORT and Jeanne de LEVIS-MIREPOIX
2 CONT
2 CONT [126598] MONTFORT (de), Philippe II (Philippe Ier & Éléonore de COURTENAY [126599]), seigneur de la Ferté-Aleps en Beauce
2 CONT
2 CONT * married before 1245, from .. (France)
2 CONT
2 CONT LEVIS-MIREPOIX (de), Jeanne (Guy Ier & Guiburge de MONTFORT [129214])
2 CONT
2 CONT       1) Éléonore, married about 1270 Jean V de VENDÖME
2 CONT
2 CONT       2) Jeanne, married about 1270 Guigues VI de LACHAMBRE, married France ? (France) 1278 Louis Ier de SAVOIE
2 CONT
2 CONT Bibliographie : Histoire de la maison royale de France (Père Anselme); Traité de généalogie (René Jetté); Europaische Stammtafeln; Histoire de Bresse et de Bugey; CEGRA-Informations 
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.francogene.com/quebec--genealogy/126/126598.php
2 CONT
2 CONT -----------
2 CONT -http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/toulcentw.htm#PhilippeMontfortdied1270<br/>
2 CONT PHILIPPE [II] de Montfort, son of PHILIPPE de Montfort Lord of Tyre & his first wife Eléonore de Courtenay (-Tunis 24 Sep 1270, bur Castres).  The Lignages d'Outremer name "Phelippe qui fu nom Coton" as son of "Phelippe de Monfort
2 CONC " and "la fille au comte d'Ausseure", stating that Philippe "morut"[263].  Seigneur de Castres et de la Ferté-Alais.  "Symon de Monteforti comes Lincestrie" granted his proxy to administer the county of Bigorre to "dominum Philipp
2 CONC um de Monteforti…consanguineum nostrum" by charter dated 9 Apr 1259[264].  The testament of "Philippus de Monteforti", dated 1 Apr 1271, names "uxoris nostre Johanne"[265].  A fragment written by Bernard Guidonis records the death
2 CONC  "IV Kal Oct" in 1270 of "dominus Philippus de Monte Forti junior, filius Philippi senioris" and his burial "ad fratres Castrenses"[266]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' JEANNE de Levis, daughter of GUY [II] de Levis Maréchal de Mirepoix & his wife Jeanne --- (-30 May 1284, bur Castres).  A fragment written by Bernard Guidonis names "dominæ Johannæ" as widow of "dominus Philippus de Monte 
2 CONC Forti junior, filius Philippi senioris"[267].  A charter dated 15 May 1295 included in the cartulary of Notre-Dame de la Roche records the partition of property of Montfort and Castro, agreed by "Joannes de Monteforti comes Squlla
2 CONC cii et Montis-Caviosi ac regni Siciliæ camerarius, Bernardus de Convenis miles…et domicella Elienore de Monteforti" which names their parents "bonæ memoriæ D Philippi de Monteforti patris et D Joannæ de Leviers matris nostrum pred
2 CONC ictorum Joannis, Lauræ et Elienoris"[268].  A fragment written by Bernard Guidonis records the death "III Kal Jun" in 1284 of "domina Johanna uxor quondam...domini Philippi...filia domini Mirapicis"[269]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT  Philippe [II] & his wife had five children: 
