2 CONT
2 CONT ====FMG ''(3 Dec 2025)'' England, Earls Created [https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/ENGLISH%20NOBILITY%20MEDIEVAL.htm#RobertBeaumontLeicesterdied1190 1067-1122]
2 CONT * '''ROBERT de Beaumont''' "''ès Blanchemains''", son of ROBERT de Beaumont Earl of Leicester & his wife Amicie de Gaël (–Acre or Durazzo 31 Aug 1190)....He succeeded his father in 1168 as Earl of Leicester....'''m''' (before [115
2 CONC 5/59] ) '''PERNEL''' [Petronille], daughter GUILLAUME —– & his wife —– (–1 Apr 1212)....Earl Robert & his wife had seven children:...
2 CONT ** 5. '''MARGARET''' ([before 1172][1733]–[12/15] Jan or 12 Feb 1235).  A history of the foundation of St Mary’s abbey, Leicester names “''Amiciam primogenitam…et Margaritam juniorem''” as the two daughters of “''Robertus''” and h
2 CONC is wife “''Petronillam filiam Hugonis de Grantmenyl''”, adding that Margaret married “''Sayero de Quincy''”[1734]. "''Seherus de Quency comes Wintonie''" donated "''ecclesiam de Gasc''" to Inchaffray Abbey, for the souls of "''pat
2 CONC ris nostri bone memorie Roberti de Quency et…matris nostre Orable et…Roberti de Quency primogeniti nostri et…Margarete uxoris nostre''" by charter dated to [1210/13][1735]. A charter of King Edward I confirmed donations to Garendo
2 CONC n Abbey among which by “''Margareta…comitissa Wyntoniæ, soror Roberti comitis Leycestriæ''”[1736]. The necrology of the monastery of Ouche records the death "12 Jan" of "''Margarita comitissa Wintonyæ''"[1737]. The necrology of Ga
2 CONC rendon abbey (Leicestershire) records the death “''XVIII Kal Feb''” of “''Margareta comitissa Wintonie et mater...Rogeri de Quyncy''”[1738]. 
2 CONT ** '''m''' (before 1190) [https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/ENGLISH%20NOBILITY%20MEDIEVAL2.htm#SaherQuincydied1219 '''SAHER''' {IV} '''de Quincy'''], son of ROBERT de Quincy & his first wife Orabilis —– (–Damietta 3 Nov 1219, bur A
2 CONC cre). He was created Earl of Winchester before 10 Feb 1207.
2 CONT ** '''Saher [IV] & his wife had [eight] children:...''' {Please click Saher [IV] de Quincy above for children born of the couple.}
2 CONT '''<nowiki>—————————————————————————————————————————</nowiki>'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret, Countess of Winchester, was also called Margaret de Harcourt.
2 CONT
2 CONT She married Saher III de Quency the Surety, 1st Earl of Winchester, son of Robert de Quency, circa 1173 in England.
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret died on 12 January 1236 (or she died before 12 Feb 1245?).
2 CONT
2 CONT See "My Lines" 
2 CONT
2 CONT ( http://homepages.rootsweb.ancestry.com/~cousin/html/p391.htm#i6935 ) 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT By his wife Margaret de Beaumont, Saer de Quincy had three sons and three daughters:
2 CONT * Lorette who married Sir William de Valognes
2 CONT * Arabella who married Sir Richard Harcourt
2 CONT * Robert (d. 1217), before 1206 he married Hawise of Chester, Countess of Lincoln, sister and co-heiress of Ranulf de Blundeville, Earl of Chester.
2 CONT * Roger, who succeeded his father as earl of Winchester (though he did not take formal possession of the earldom until after his mother's death);
2 CONT * Robert de Quincy (second son of that name; d. 1257) who married Helen, daughter of the Welsh prince Llywelyn the Great;
2 CONT * Hawise, who married Hugh de Vere, 4th Earl of Oxford.
2 CONT '''<nowiki>—————————————————————————————————————————</nowiki>'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT http://familytrees.genopro.com/azrael/default.htm?page=deBeaumont-Margaret-ind07150.htm
2 CONT http://freepages.genealogy.rootsweb.com/~hwbradley/aqwg644.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT Saher IV de QUINCY Earl of Winchester was born 1155 in Winchester, Hampshire, England. He died 3 Nov 1219 in Damietta, Egypt. Saher married Margaret de BEAUMONT Countess of Winchester on 1170 in Winchester, Hampshire, England.
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret de BEAUMONT Countess of Winchester was born 1158 in Leicester, Leicestershire, England. She died 12 Jan 1235 in Brackley, Northamptonshire, England. Margaret married Saher IV de QUINCY Earl of Winchester on 1170 in Winche
2 CONC ster, Hampshire, England.
2 CONT
2 CONT They had the following children:
2 CONT
2 CONT F 	i 	Lorette de QUINCY was born 1177.
2 CONT M 	ii 	Sir Robert de QUINCY Knight was born 1179 and died 1217.
2 CONT M 	iii 	Sir Roger de QUINCY Earl of Winchester was born 1184 and died 25 Apr 1264.
2 CONT M 	iv 	Sir Robert de QUINCY Knight was born 1190 and died Aug 1257.
2 CONT F 	v 	Hawise de QUINCY was born 1195 and died 3 Feb Aft 1273.
2 CONT F 	vi 	Orabella de QUINCY was born 1198.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT MARGARET de Harcourt de BEAUMONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ABT 1155 - 12 Jan 1234
2 CONT
2 CONT ID Number: I18339
2 CONT
2 CONT * RESIDENCE: England
2 CONT * BIRTH: ABT 1155, Hampshire, ENG
2 CONT * DEATH: 12 Jan 1234
2 CONT * BURIAL: Brackley, England [S2721]
2 CONT * RESOURCES: See: [S590] [S1033] [S2195] [S2222] [S2458] 
2 CONT
2 CONT Father: ROBERT III "Blanchmains" Harcourt de BEAUMONT 3rd Earl of Leicester
2 CONT Mother: PETRONELLA de GRANTMESNIL
2 CONT
2 CONT Family 1 : SAIRE IV de QUINCEY 1st Earl of Winchester
2 CONT
2 CONT * MARRIAGE: BEF 1173 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.  ORABELLA de QUINCEY
2 CONT 2. +LORETTE de QUINCEY
2 CONT 3. +HAWISE de QUINCEY
2 CONT 4.  REGINALD de QUINCEY
2 CONT 5. +ROGER de QUINCEY 2nd Earl of Winchester 
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT Aka: HARCOURT, Margaret b. ABT 1156 Hampshire, England d. 12 JAN 1235/36
2 CONT
2 CONT Father: HARCOURT, Robert "Blanchmains" Earl of LEICSTER
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother: GRENTMESNIL, Petronille de
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert de Beaumont, 3rd Earl of Leicester married Petronilla[1], who was either a granddaughter or great-granddaughter of Hugh de Grandmesnil. They had five children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert, who succeeded his father as Earl of Leicester;
2 CONT Roger, who became Bishop of St Andrews in 1189;
2 CONT William, who was a leper;
2 CONT Amicia, who married Simon III de Montfort, and whose son Simon subsequently became Earl of Leicester;
2 CONT Margaret, who married Saer de Quincy, later 1st Earl of Winchester.
2 CONT
2 CONT Saer de Quincy's immediate background was in the Scottish kingdom: his father was a knight in the service of king William the Lion, and his mother was the heiress of the lordship of Leuchars in Fife (see below). His rise to promin
2 CONC ence in England came through his marriage to Margaret, the younger sister of Robert de Beaumont, 4th Earl of Leicester: but it is probably no coincidence that her other brother was the de Quincys' powerful Fife neighbour, Roger de
2 CONC  Beaumont, Bishop of St Andrews. In 1204, Earl Robert died, leaving Margaret as co-heiress of the vast earldom along with her elder sister. The estate was split in half, and after the final division was ratified in 1207, de Quincy
2 CONC  was made Earl of Winchester.
2 CONT
2 CONT By his wife Margaret de Beaumont, Saer de Quincy had three sons and three daughters:
2 CONT
2 CONT Lorette who married Sir William de Valognes
2 CONT
2 CONT Arabella who married Sir Richard Harcourt
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert (d. 1217). Some sources say he married Hawise, sister and co-heiress of Ranulf de Blundeville, earl of Chester. However, it is more likely Hawise married Saer's brother Robert II;
2 CONT
2 CONT Roger, who succeeded his father as earl of Winchester (though he did not take formal possession of the earldom until after his mother's death);
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert de Quincy (second son of that name; d. 1257) who married Helen, daughter of the Welsh prince Llywelyn the Great;
2 CONT
2 CONT Hawise, who married Hugh de Vere, 4th Earl of Oxford.
