1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ====FMG: England, Earls Creates [https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/ENGLISH%20NOBILITY%20MEDIEVAL.htm#RobertBeaumontLeicesterdied1190 1067-1122]
2 CONT * 2. GUILLAUME de Breteuil (–[1189/90]). The history of the foundation of St Mary’s abbey, Leicester names “''Robertum…Willielmum leprosum, secundum…et Galfridum''” as the three sons of “''Robertus''” and his wife “''Petronillam f
2 CONC iliam Hugonis de Grantmenyl''”[1717]. He is named before his brother Robert in charters, the last dated in 1189 at '''Nuneaton'''[1718]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ====Notes
