2 CONT Simon III de Montfort, comte de Évreux, was Count of Évreux in Normandy between 1140 and March 1181. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Simon married Maud circa 1150 in France.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a vassal of both the King of France and of the King of England (who was also Duke of Normandy), whose position was embarrassing when his two suzerains were at war. He adhered to England and handed over his castles of Rochef
2 CONC ort, Montfort, and Epernon to Henry II, which forced the French king, Louis, to make a truce by cutting his communications between Paris, Orleans, and Etampes in 1159.
2 CONT
2 CONT Simon married Amicia de Beaumont, daughter of Robert III de Beaumont, 3rd Earl of Leicester and Petronilla de Grentesmesnil, between 1166 and 1169.
2 CONT
2 CONT Simon died on 12 March 1180/81 at or 13th.
2 CONT
