1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Alix de Montmorency
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Alix de Montmorency, died Feb 24, 1220-1221. Her parents were Bouchard III de Montmorency and Countess of Hainaut Laurence.
2 CONT
2 CONT Early life
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1190 she married Simon de Montfort, 5th Earl of Leicester (1160 – June 25, 1218), son of Simon III de Montfort, who descended from the lords of Montfort l'Amaury near Paris, France.
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit]Children of Alix and Simon
2 CONT
2 CONT They left three sons: Their French estates passed to their eldest son, Amaury de Montfort, while their younger son, Simon, eventually gained possession of the earldom of Leicester and played a major role in the reign of Henry III 
2 CONC of England. Another son, Guy, was married to Petronille, Countess of Bigorre, on 6 November 1216, but died at the siege of Castelnaudary on 20 July 1220. Their daughter, Petronilla, became an abbess at the Cistercian nunnery of St
2 CONC . Antoine's. Another daughter, Amicia, founded the nunnery at Montargis and died there in 1252.
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit]Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT ^ Chanson de la Croisade Albigeoise laisse 205.
2 CONT
2 CONT ^ Chanson de la Croisade Albigeoise laisse 206; Peter of les Vaux-de-Cernay, Historia Albigensis 615.
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit]Sources
2 CONT
2 CONT J. R. Maddicott, Simon de Montfort, 1996
2 CONT
2 CONT Jonathan Sumption, The Albigensian Crusade, 2000
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit]See also
2 CONT
2 CONT Simon IV de Montfort
