1 NOTE {geni:about_me} death after 1290
2 CONT
2 CONT https://genealogics.org/getperson.php?personID=I00291426&tree=LEO
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------
2 CONT
2 CONT -http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/chamdampjo.htm#GeoffroyJoinvilledied1290
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.         GEOFFROY de Joinville ([1245/47]-before 11 Dec 1290).  "Jean de Joinville", with the consent of "sa femme Alix et de ses fils Geoffroy et Jean", sold "la grange de Bailly..." to Ecurey abbey, by charter dated 19 Oct 126
2 CONC 6[444].  Mabile de Lezinnes Dame de Nanteuil acknowledged having received property from “Erars de Lesines doyen d’Auxerre et de défunt Guillaume de Lesignes ses frères” on her marriage, ratified by “Joiffroiz de Joingville son mar
2 CONC i”, by charter dated 1270[445].  Seigneur de Briquenay.  "Geoffroy de Joinville seigneur de Briquenay fils aîné de Jean de Joinville" made an agreement with Thibaut Comte de Bar concerning Apremont by charter dated Jan 1270 (O.S.?
2 CONC )[446].  “Jofroi de Joinville seigneur de Briquenay et Mabile dame de Nanteuil sa femme” requested Henri III Comte de Champagne to ratify an agreement under which they received “des biens à Lappiou et une rente due par le comte de
2 CONC  Roucy” from “le seigneur de Commercy”, in return for property “à Lirey, Villetart et Assencières”, by charter dated Jun 1273[447].  A charter dated Apr 1274 records freedoms granted to Ampilly-le-Sec by “Goffroy de Joinville chev
2 CONC alier seigneur de Seantholiot...de...Mabile sa femme et...Gauchis fils de la dessus dite Mabile”[448].  He is named as deceased in the charter dated 11 Dec 1290 quoted below.  "Jean de Joinville sénéchal de Champagne" declared hav
2 CONC ing relinquished revenue “sur la maison de Sommermont”, which he had granted to the “seigneur de Briquenay lorsque celui-ci était parti pour la Pouille”, to “ses petit-fils Jean de Joinville s. de Venafro maréchal de Sicile et Gui
2 CONC llaume tous deux fils de feu Geoffroy s. de Nanteuil et de Briquenay, ainsi qu’aux enfants d’un autre Geoffroy leur frère”, with the consent of “ses fils Jean de Joinville s. d’Ancerville, Anseau s. de Reynel chevaliers, André de 
2 CONC Joinville s. de Bonney écuyer”, by charter dated 9 Jun 1304[449].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' (contract May 1270) as her second husband, MABILE de Lezinnes, widow of ERARD [I] de Nanteuil Seigneur de Nanteuil-la-Fosse, daughter of GUILLAUME de Villehardouin Seigneur de Lezinnes & his wife Marguerite de Mello (-[128
2 CONC 6/Dec 1290]).  Mabile de Lezinnes Dame de Nanteuil acknowledged having received property from “Erars de Lesines doyen d’Auxerre et de défunt Guillaume de Lesignes ses frères” on her marriage, ratified by “Joiffroiz de Joingville s
2 CONC on mari”, by charter dated 1270[450].  “Jofroi de Joinville seigneur de Briquenay et Mabile dame de Nanteuil sa femme” requested Henri III Comte de Champagne to ratify an agreement under which they received “des biens à Lappiou et
2 CONC  une rente due par le comte de Roucy” from “le seigneur de Commercy”, in return for property “à Lirey, Villetart et Assencières”, by charter dated Jun 1273[451].  A charter dated Apr 1274 records freedoms granted to Ampilly-le-Sec
2 CONC  by “Goffroy de Joinville chevalier seigneur de Seantholiot...de...Mabile sa femme et...Gauchis fils de la dessus dite Mabile”[452].  
2 CONT
2 CONT   Geoffroy & his wife had children:  
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------
2 CONT
2 CONT -http://www.genmarenostrum.com/pagine-lettere/letterai/ianvilla.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT   A1. Goffredo (+ prigioniero degli aragonesi, 1285/1290), 
2 CONT
2 CONT con il padre ed i fratelli seguì Carlo d’Angiò nella conquista  del Regno di Napoli; Signore di Calvi e della Rocca di Mondragone, nella provincia di Terra di Lavoro; ebbe, per il suo  servizio e la sua fedeltà, da Carlo I d’Angiò
2 CONC , 400 once di rendita sui fiscali di Mondragone e Carinola. 
2 CONT
2 CONT        = 5-1270 Mabille de Villehardouin, figlia di Guillaume Signore di Lézinnes e di Marguerite de Mello (+ 1307).
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------
