1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''TIPHAINE de Husson Dame de Ducey (-[6 Sep 1390/1391])''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT d/o FRASLIN de Husson Seigneur de Ducey, de Champeservon et de Cherancé &  Clémence du Guesclin (-[6 Sep 1390/1391]). 
2 CONT
2 CONT x GUY de Laval “Brumor” Seigneur de Chaloyau (-[1382/83])
2 CONT *FOULQUES de Laval (-[1398/1403])
2 CONT *GUY de Laval (-[29 Oct 1415/early 1416], bur Buzay abbey) x MARIE de Craon
2 CONT
2 CONT xx (1383) Raoul [V] de Meulan Seigneur de Corseulles.
2 CONT *JEAN de Meulan ([1385]-[1414]). x MARGUERITE le Servain Dame de Saint-Pois, de Martigny, des Abbayes et de Sermentot
2 CONT *JEANNE de Meulan ([1385/90?]-) x GUILLAUME de Briqueville Seigneur de Laune xx HENRI Carbonnel Seigneur de Brévands et Saint-Denis-le-Gast
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT GUY de Laval “Brumor” (-[1382/83]).  Duchesne records his parentage, noting “surnommé Brumor par sobriquet de guerre” and the battles in which he fought[335].  Seigneur Chaloyau, de Blason et de Chemillé.  m firstly (Paris 29 Sep 
2 CONC 1358) JEANNE de Montmorency Dame de Damville, daughter of CHARLES Seigneur de Montmorency & his second wife Jeanne de Roucy (-[1364/68]).  Duchesne records her parentage, marriage, marriage date and place, noting her dowry “les te
2 CONC rres de Blason et de Chemilier en Anjou, venues du costé de sa mere; bien qu’au traité de son mariage eust esté convenu qu’elle auroit la Seigneurie de Damville en Normandie”, and her death “quelque temps apres...sans enfants” (no
2 CONC  date stated)[336]. '''m secondly as her first husband, TIPHAINE de Husson Dame de Ducey, daughter of FRASLIN de Husson Seigneur de Ducey, de Champeservon et de Cherancé & his wife Clémence du Guesclin (-[6 Sep 1390/1391]).  She m
2 CONC arried secondly (1383) as his second wife, Raoul [V] de Meulan Seigneur de Corseulles.  Duchesne records that “Guy de Laval dit Brumor Seigneur de Chalouyau, de Blason et de Chemilier” married secondly “Tiphaine de Husson autremen
2 CONC t dite Estiennette, dame de Duscé, fille de Fralin de Husson chevalier seigneur de Duscé, de Champ-Seruon et de Charancé en Normandie et de Clémence du Guesclin seur de Bertrand du Guesclin connestable de France“, who in 1383 marr
2 CONC ied secondly “Raoul de Meullent chevalier seigneur de Courceulle”[337].  La Roque records “un acte exercé aux Assises d’Avrenches devant le Bailly de Costentin”, dated 6 Sep 1390, which records a claim by “[les] Chevaliers de Rhod
2 CONC es” against “Raoul de Beauchamp Chevalier et Clemence du Guesclin sa femme, seigneurs de la Fere, de Chevreuse et du Heron” who named “Raoul de Meullent...Chevalier...sire de Courseulles et...mary de Madame Tiphaine de Husson sa f
2 CONC emme” as their guarantor[338].  A register of homage to Marie d’Anjou Queen of Sicily records that “le rachapt de la terre et chastellenie de Blason” reverted to the Duc d’Anjou “ayant le bail et administration des biens de Fouque
2 CONC s de Laval fils aisné de cette Dame” in 1391 “par le deceds de...Tiphaine de Husson...”[339].  Guy & his second wife had two children:
2 CONT '''
2 CONT >i)          FOULQUES de Laval (-[1398/1403]).  A register of homage to Marie d’Anjou Queen of Sicily records that “le rachapt de la terre et chastellenie de Blason” reverted to the Duc d’Anjou “ayant le bail et administration des
2 CONC  biens de Fouques de Laval fils aisné de cette Dame” in 1391 “par le deceds de...Tiphaine de Husson...”[340].  Duchesne records his parentage and death 1398 “sans avoir esté marié”[341].  Europäische Stammtafeln, on the other hand
2 CONC , records his mention “1398/1403”[342]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT >ii)         [https://www.geni.com/people/Guy-II-de-Montmorency-Laval-baron-de-Rais/6000000014329892239?through=6000000014329624719 GUY de Laval], (-[29 Oct 1415/early 1416], bur Buzay abbey).m (before 5 Feb 1404) [https://www.gen
2 CONC i.com/people/Marie-de-Craon/6000000014329642592   MARIE de Craon], daughter of [https://www.geni.com/people/Jean-de-Craon-Dommart-en-Ponthieu-de-Nou%C3%A2tre/6000000003827587630?through=6000000014329642592 JEAN de Craon Seigneur d
2 CONC e la Suze] & his first wife [https://www.geni.com/people/B%C3%A9atrix-de-Rochefort/6000000014329901294?through=6000000003827587630 Beatrix de Rochefort] (-before Oct 1415, bur Buzay abbey). 
2 CONT
2 CONT >>1.         [https://www.geni.com/people/Gilles-de-Montmorency-Laval-baron-de-Rais/6000000014329624719 GILLES de Lava]l ([1404/05]-killed Nantes 24 Oct 1440).  Seigneur de Rays 
2 CONT
2 CONT >>2.         [https://www.geni.com/people/Ren%C3%A9-de-Montmorency-Laval-baron-de-Retz/6000000016700527962?through=6000000014329624719 RENE de Laval] (-1474).  Seigneur de la Suze.  * https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/mainnob.htm#G
2 CONC illesLaval
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT RAOUL [V] de Meulan, son of RAOUL [IV] de Meulan Seigneur de Corseulles & his wife Jeanne Paynell ([1340/45?]-after 3 May 1406, bur Ardayne). '''m secondly (1383) as her second husband, TIPHAINE de Husson Dame de Ducey, widow of G
2 CONC UY de Laval “Brumor” Seigneur de Chaloyau, de Blason et de Chemillé, daughter of FRASLIN de Husson Seigneur de Ducey, de Champeservon et de Cherancé & his wife Clémence du Guesclin (-[6 Sep 1390/1391]). RAOUL [V] & his second wife
2 CONC  had two children:''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT >>6.         JEAN de Meulan ([1385]-[1414]).   m (contract 29 Sep 1404) MARGUERITE le Servain Dame de Saint-Pois, de Martigny, des Abbayes et de Sermentot, daughter of ROBERT le Servain Baron de Saint-Pois [previously named Saint-
2 CONC Paër/Saint-Pair/Saint-Pair-le-Servain] & his wife Beatrix de la Chesse (-after 13 Oct 1435).
2 CONT
2 CONT >>7.         JEANNE de Meulan ([1385/90?]-).  m firstly (contract 3 May 1406) GUILLAUME de Briqueville Seigneur de Laune, son of --- (-[1410?]).  Not enough verified information has been found about the Briqueville family to specu
