1 NOTE {geni:about_me} John VI de Vendôme (died 1365), Count of Vendôme and Castres (1354-1365) was of the House of Montoire and was son of Bouchard VI and Alix de Bretagne.
2 CONT
2 CONT He lived mainly in Castres and fought at Poitiers (1356) where he was captured.[1] In 1362, a troop of Gascon and English took the city and imprisoned Countess Jeanne de Ponthieu. Several attempts to deliver the city by force fail
2 CONC ed, and John VI had to be resolved to pay a ransom for the city.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1342, he married Jeanne de Ponthieu, they had two children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Bouchard VII 
2 CONT
2 CONT Catherine of Vendôme 
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_I,_Count_of_La_Marche
2 CONT
2 CONT John I, Count of La Marche
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
