2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Charles d'Albret
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Family
2 CONT
2 CONT He married, as her third husband, Marie de Sully, daughter of Louis de Sully and Isabel de Craon[2], on 27 January 1400 and had issue:
2 CONT
2 CONT Jeanne d'Albret (1403–1435), married in 1422 Jean I of Foix-Grailly, Count of Foix. They were parents of Gaston IV of Foix.
2 CONT
2 CONT Charles II d'Albret (1407–1471), married Anne of Armagnac (born 1402), the daughter of Bernard VII of Armagnac, Count of Charolais and Bonne of Berry, by whom he had seven children. Queen Jeanne III of Navarre was a notable descen
2 CONC dant.
2 CONT
2 CONT Guillaume d'Albret (d. 1429), Lord of Orval
2 CONT
2 CONT Jean d'Albret
2 CONT
2 CONT Catherine d'Albret, married Jean de Montagu (1363–1409), vidame of Laon and illegitimate son of Charles V of France.
