1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://genealogics.org/getperson.php?personID=I00613128&tree=LEO
2 CONT
2 CONT BIOGRAPHY Jacques de Warignies, seigneur de Blainville, la Potterie et Bléville, was the son of Jean de Warignies, seigneur de Bléville, and Anne de Villetain. With his wife Adrienne Martel, dame de la Potterie, daughter of Charle
2 CONC s Martel, seigneur de Bacqueville, and Marie de Jaucourt, Jacques had at least two sons, Jean and Tanneguy, of whom Tanneguy is recorded with progeny. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Jacques, who belonged to a noble family in Picardy that had acquired the estate of Blainville in the 15th century, was gentleman of the chamber to the duke of Alençon. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Jacques died on 10 November 1589.
