1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://genealogics.org/getperson.php?personID=I00094123&tree=LEO
2 CONT
2 CONT BIOGRAPHY Charles was the son of Nicolas de Coësmes and Madeleine de Chourses. In July 1520 he married Jeanne d'Harcourt, baronesse de Bonnétable, daughter of François d'Harcourt, baron de Bonnétable et de Sailly, and Anne de Sain
2 CONC t-Germain. Jeanne died without issue in 1523. In 1526, under controversial circumstances he married Jeanne's sister Gabrielle. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The marriage was initially disapproved of by King François I as Gabrielle had been abducted by Charles, who was aided by Pierre de Bernay, seigneur de Launay. The couple took refuge at the château de Launay, and subsequent events 
2 CONC are known in great detail including quotes from the angry mother trying to fetch her daughter at night. 
2 CONT
2 CONT By 1527, because of services rendered by Charles to the crown and, some say, because of Gabrielle's remarkable beauty, the couple often joined the court of François I at Amboise and Chambord. Charles' chatellany of Lucé was made i
2 CONC nto a barony. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Charles and Gabrielle had two children, Louis and Renée, both of whom would have progeny. Charles, described by one source as wayward, violent and perverted, died on 7 May 1543
