1 OCCU Sieur, du Hommet, de la Rivière, Baron - Seigneur de Remilly - Connétable de Normandie
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Richard Seigneur du Hommet'''
2 CONT
2 CONT s/o Guillaume du Hommet & Lucie 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===From Medlands:===
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/NORMAN%20NOBILITY.htm#RichardHommetdied1181
2 CONT
2 CONT GUILLAUME du Hommet .  Robert of Torigny names "Guillermum, Enjorannum, Jordanum" as the sons and heirs of "Richardus de Humet constabularius regis" when recording his death[944].  Henry II King of England confirmed the possession
2 CONC s of the abbey of Aunay, including donations by "Richardi de Humetis et Agnetis uxoris sue, filie et heredis predicti Jordani" with the agreement of "Guillelmi de Humetis et Engerranni et Jordani filiorum suorum", by charter dated
2 CONC  to [1181/89][945].  "Guillelmus de Humeto" confirmed the donation to Bayeux of the church of Hérils by "Roberti de Novo Burgo" by charter dated 1166, witnessed by "…Ricardo de Humeto…"[946].  Connétable de Normandie.  Henry II Ki
2 CONC ng of England confirmed "Willelmo de Humetis constabulariam meam" in his office previously held by "Ricardus de Humetis pater suus" by charter dated 1180[947].  The Red Book of the Exchequer, listing scutage payments in [1194/95],
2 CONC  names "Willelmus de Homez" paying "xx s, i militem" in Hampshire[948].  "Willelmus de Humeto constabularius Normanniæ" donated half the church of Louvières to Bayeux, in the presence of "Jordano filio meo episcopo Lexoviensi", by
2 CONC  charter dated to [1202/05], which names "Ricardi patris mei"[949].  “Willielmus de Humeth” donated property to Stanford Nunnery, confirmed by King John by charter dated 22 Nov [1199/1205][950].  m LUCIE, daughter of ---.  "Lucia 
2 CONC de Humetis" donated revenue from land at Bradecroft, near Stamford to Southwick priory, Lincolnshire, for the souls of "domini mei Willelmi de Humetis et Ricardi filii mei", by charter dated to the late 12th century, witnessed by 
2 CONC "Jordano de Humetis, Ricardo de Humetis, Baudewino Wac…Bartholomeo de Mortuo mari..:Willelmo de Sae, Henrico de Humetis fratre suo…"[951].  “Lucia uxor domini Willielmi de Humet constabularii domini regis” donated "terra mea de Br
2 CONC adecrofd" to Stanford Nunnery, with the consent of "domini mei Willielmi et Ricardi filii mei", by undated charter witnessed by "Jordano de Humet, Ricardo de Humet, Willielmo de Sae, Henrico fratre suo…"[952].  Guillaume & his wif
2 CONC e had three children:  
2 CONT
2 CONT (a)       '''RICHARD du Hommet'''
2 CONT  "Lucia de Humetis" donated revenue from land at Bradecroft, near Stamford to Southwick priory, Lincolnshire, for the souls of "domini mei Willelmi de Humetis et Ricardi filii mei", by charter dated to the late 12th century, witne
2 CONC ssed by "Jordano de Humetis, Ricardo de Humetis, Baudewino Wac…Bartholomeo de Mortuo mari..:Willelmo de Sae, Henrico de Humetis fratre suo…"[953].  “Lucia uxor domini Willielmi de Humet constabularii domini regis” donated "terra m
2 CONC ea de Bradecrofd" to Stanford Nunnery, with the consent of "domini mei Willielmi et Ricardi filii mei", by undated charter witnessed by "Jordano de Humet, Ricardo de Humet, Willielmo de Sae, Henrico fratre suo…"[954].  m GILLE de 
2 CONC la Haye, daughter of RICHARD de la Haye & his wife Mathilde [de Vernon].  Bracton records a claim, dated 1231, by "Willelmus Longespei et Idonea uxor eius" against "Oliuero de Ayncurt et Nicholæ uxori eius" concerning "manerium de
2 CONC  Dudingtona", inherited from "Nicholaæ de Haya avie ipsius Idonee cuius heres ipsa est" which names "Gerardum de Kaunuilla et Nicholaam uxorem eius Ricardum de Humaz et Juliam uxorem eius et Willelmum de Rullos et Isabellam uxorem
2 CONC  eius" as "filias et heredes Ricardi de Haya"[955].  
