1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ====Notices
2 CONT # '''Medlands:''' Much information that was once deposited into this overview was updated and will be updated in future years. ''No longer'' does Medlands think of Marie as a certain daughter in the connected family. Its bio-bit b
2 CONC elow is entirely in brackets now with a proviso statement.
2 CONT # '''Please keep genealogically sourced information at the top of Geni Overviews.''' Please limit that content to what's useful for each profile. See, for example, the pared down Medlands information below. Previously, it included
2 CONC  far too much about her parents and siblings—bearing no relevance to Marie de Meulan's life. Removed below was too much was about the lives of her parents and siblings.
2 CONT # '''Please limit historical information to a minimum''' after genealogically sourced information in Geni Overviews. 
2 CONT # '''Please be content to click on links''' if one wishes to read a broad history, especially when websites and webpages will probably remain long-term available.
2 CONT # '''Wikipedia''' now provides five sourced conjectures for whom the poet "Marie de France" may have been, thus making everything about that poet's works irrelevant to this profile. What once was included about those works is now 
2 CONC removed. Limited quoted matter from the article now sits where it belongs: at the bottom of this Overview. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ====FMG ''(update 29 Aug 2025)'': Normandy Nobility: [https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/NORMANDY%20NOBILITY.htm#Walerandied1166B Alençon, Evreux, Meulan, Perche]
2 CONT * '''WALERAN de Beaumont, son of ROBERT de Beaumont-le-Roger Comte de Meulan, Earl of Leicester & his wife Elisabeth de Vermandois [Capet]''' (1104-Préaux 9/10 Apr 1166, bur Préaux, monastery of Saint-Pierre)....'''m''' (1141) AGN
2 CONC ES de Montfort, daughter of AMAURY [III] de Montfort Comte d'Evreux & his second wife Agnès de Garlande (-15 Dec 1181)....
2 CONT * '''Comte Waléran & his wife had nine children:'''  
2 CONT ** 1. ROBERT de Beaumont ([1142/43?]-[16 Aug or 20 Sep] 1208, bur Préaux)....
2 CONT ** 2. WALERAN de Meulan (-after 1181)....
2 CONT ** 3. AMAURY [I] de Meulan ([1145/50?]-[1182/87?])....
2 CONT ** 4.  ROGER de Meulan ([1146/52?]-12 Jul [1221])....
2 CONT ** 6. ETIENNE de Meulan (-after 1165)....
2 CONT ** 7. ISABELLE de Meulan (-10 May 1220, bur Savigny)....
2 CONT ** '''8. [MARIE de Meulan''' ([1145/60?]-).  La Roque names “Marie de Meullent dame de la baronnie de Cleuuille et de Talbot” as second daughter of Waléran de Meulan, in a later passage naming her husband “Huë de Talebot Baron de 
2 CONC Cleuuille”, identifying him as the son of “Godeffroy de Talebot qui s’empara de la ville d’Herford, vivoit l’an 1138”[1847].  The last-named is identified as Geoffrey [II] Talbot (died 22 Aug 1140) in the document ENGLISH LORDS T-
2 CONC Z, but no record has been found of his having a son named Hugh/Hugues.  Morandière records the unnamed father of Jeanne Talbot as the son of "Richard Talebot…compagnon de son voisin Grondebœuf à Hastings"[1848]. '''''The primary s
2 CONC ources which confirms this information have not been identified.  Until such sources emerge, it is suggested that these supposed persons should be treated with caution''.''' '''m''' [https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/ENGLISHNOBILIT
2 CONC YMEDIEVAL3T-Z.htm#HuguesTalbotMMarieMeulan '''HUGUES Talbot'''] Baron de Cleuville Seigneur de Hotot-sur-Mer, son of [RICHARD [I] Talbot & his wife ---].] 
2 CONT ** 9. [AMICIE de Meulan ([1145/60?]-)....] 
2 CONT
