1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ====FMG: Normandy Nobiliy: [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/NORMANDY%20NOBILITY.htm#IsabelleMeulandied1220 Alençon, Évreux, Meulan, Perche]
2 CONT * '''WALERAN de Beaumont''', son of ROBERT de Beaumont-le-Roger Comte de Meulan, Earl of Leicester & his wife Elisabeth de Vermandois [Capet] (1104–Préaux 9/10 Apr 1166, bur Préaux, monastery of Saint-Pierre)....'''m''' (1141) '''
2 CONC AGNES de Montfort''', daughter of AMAURY [III] de Montfort Comte d'Evreux & his second wife Agnès de Garlande (–15 Dec 1181)....Waléran & his wife had [nine] children:...
2 CONT ** 7. '''ISABELLE de Meulan''' (–10 May 1220, bur Savigny). Henry II King of England confirmed a donation to Savigny by "''Ysabell filie Gualerandi comitis de Mellento''", with the consent of "''filiis suis Juhello…filio Gaufridi 
2 CONC de Meduana, et Mauricio et Petro, filiis Mauricii de Creon''", by charter dated to [Apr 1180/Jan 1183][1839]. "''Mauricius de Creon Hugonis filius''" donated property to Roë by charter dated 23 Jun 1191, witnessed by "…''Guillelmo
2 CONC  de Guierchia et Isabel uxore mea et filiis meis Mauricio et Petro''…"[1840]. Her two marriages are confirmed by the undated charter by which her son "''Mauritius dominus Credoni''" confirmed the donation by "Constantia soror mea"
2 CONC  of revenue set by "''dominus Juhellus frater meus''" at "''apud Harperiam''" to the abbey of Clarei, by undated charter, witnessed by "…''domina Isabel matre mea, domina Gervasia''…"[1841]. "''Mauritius de Credone filius Hugonis'
2 CONC '" appointed "''meæ uxoris Isabel''" as guardian of his lands and his children in his undated testament when leaving for Jerusalem[1842]. The ''Gesta Guillelmi Majoris Andegavensis Episcopi'' names “''dominis de Credonio…et Isabel
2 CONC la Domina de Credonio''” among those present at the burial of Bishop Guillaume, undated but stated to be during the reign of Philippe II King of France[1843]. "''Constancia soror domini Amaurici de Credone''" donated property to R
2 CONC oë, with the consent of “...''Isabel matris meæ et Juhel de Meduana et Amauricii de Credone fratrum meorum''”, by charter dated 1217[1844]. The ''Chronicon Savigniacensis Monasterii'' records the death in 1220 of "''Juhellus de Me
2 CONC duana…domina Isabel mater eius''"[1845]. The necrology of Angers Cathedral records the death "''Kal Mai''" of "''Isabellis domina de Credonio''"[1846]. 
2 CONT ** '''m''' firstly {[1161]} as his second wife, [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/mainnob.htm#GeoffroyMayennedied1169 '''GEOFFROY Seigneur de Mayenne'''], son of JUHEL Seigneur de Mayenne & his wife Clémence de Ponthieu (–18 Feb or
2 CONC  25 Jul 1169). 
2 CONT ** '''m''' secondly {[1170]} [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/anjounob.htm#MauriceIICraondied1196B '''MAURICE''' (II) '''Seigneur de Craon'''], son of HUGUES Seigneur de Craon & his second wife Isabelle de Vitré (–12 Jul 1196).
2 CONT ** Geoffroy and his [second] wife had one child:
2 CONT *** c) JUHEL [II] de Mayenne (–killed in battle 12 or 26 Apr, 2 or 4 May 1220, bur Fontaine-Daniel)....&c.
2 CONT ** Maurice [II] & his wife had seven children: 
2 CONT *** 1. AVOISE (–1230)....
2 CONT *** 2. CONSTANCE ([1170/73]–after 1217)....
2 CONT *** 3. AGNES (–1205 or before)....
2 CONT *** 4. RENAUD (–before 1180)....
2 CONT *** 5. MAURICE [III] ([after 1178]–25 Jul 1207, bur Roë)....
2 CONT *** 6. PIERRE (–[1207], maybe [1215/16])....
2 CONT *** 7. AMAURY [I] (–15 May 1226)....
2 CONT
2 CONT ====Wikipediæ ''(as of 22 Mar 2026)''
