2 CONT >9. [AMICIE de Meulan ([1145/60?]-). La Roque names “Amicie de Meullent dame de la baronnie de Ferrieres” as third daughter of Waléran de Meulan, in a later passage naming her husband “Henry sire et Baron de Ferrieres”[1849]. ''Th
2 CONC e primary source which confirms her parentage and marriage has not yet been identified''. The chronology suggests that, if the information is correct, Amicie’s husband would have been Henri son of Walkelin de Ferrers.  '''m HENRI 
2 CONC de Ferrers''' Seigneur de Ferrières, son of WALKELIN de Ferrers & his wife --- (-after 1207).]
