3 CTRY France
1 OCCU Comte, greve av Auvergne, d'Auvergne
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} -https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/AUVERGNE.htm#GuillaumeIXAuvergnedied1246
2 CONT
2 CONT '''GUILLAUME [X] d’Auvergne''', son of GUY [II] Comte d'Auvergne & his wife Petronille de Chambon (-1246, bur Le Bouchet).  The Chronicle of Alberic de Trois-Fontaines records that "iunior comes Alvernie Guilelmus" was son of “com
2 CONC itis Guidonis Alvernie” and his wife "soror abbatis Radulfi…Camboniam"[295].  "Guido comes Claromontensis" donated "Buillonem…et Leez…et Buisseroles…" to "Petronillæ dominiæ Chambonii uxori meæ comitissæ Clarimontensis in dotalici
2 CONC o" on leaving for "partes Albigenses…contra hæreticos", with the consent of "Guillelmus primogenitus meus [ …matri suæ ]", by charter dated 1209[296].  The testament of "Guidonis comitis Arvernorum", dated 27 May 1209, names "Guil
2 CONC lelmo primogenito suo…Hugo secundus natu…Petronillæ uxoris suæ…Guidoni…tertio filio suo"[297].  Comte d'Auvergne.  Henry III King of England recorded a treaty with "W. filium comitis Guidonis de Alvernia et Delfinum Clari Montis e
2 CONC t R. nepotem eius" dated [Oct] 1225[298].  The testament of "Guillermus comes Claromontensis", dated Feb 1245, chooses burial "in monasterio del Boschet in sepulcro bonæ memoriæ patris nostri", appoints "Robertum filium nostrum…su
2 CONC b custodia…Hugonis…episcopi Claromontensis consanguinei nostri" as his heir, names "Guidonem filium nostrum clericum…Guillermum et Godefridum filios nostros…Henricum filium nostrum", provides for the anniversary of "sororis nostræ
2 CONC  et…generis nostri Guillelmo de Ussone" and makes various other donations including to "domui de las Chesas…ad vitam sororis nostræ"[299]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Betrothed''' (Apr 1202) to --- de Montluçon, daughter of ARCHAMBAUD Seigneur de Montluçon & his wife ---.  A charter dated Apr 1202 records an agreement between “Archembaudus dominus Montis Lucii” and “Guidonem comitem Arvernie
2 CONC " for the marriage of "filiam Archembaudi primogenitam" and "Guillelmus filius comitis, vel alter filius", together with "Combralium et comitatum"[300]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Betrothed''' ( [1210] ) to [ELEONORE] de Forez, daughter of GUY [III] Comte de Forez & his second wife Alix ---.  La Mure states that "la troisième et dernière fille de Guy III Comte de Forez et de son épouse Alice de Suilly" w
2 CONC as "Eléonor de Forez" who, in a charter "alléguée par Justel de l’an 1210", was betrothed to "Guillaume fils de Guy II Comte d’Auvergne", that the betrothal was terminated "par le changement des affaires qui survint ès Maisons d’A
2 CONC uvergne et de Forez", and that the same daughter later married "un grand seigneur d’Auvergne nommé Guillaume de Baffie, seigneur de Baffie et de Viveron"[301].  In this way, La Mure conflates the daughter of Comte Guy [III] by his
2 CONC  first marriage, who married Guillaume de Baffie as demonstrated by the charter dated Mar [1241/42] quoted above, with his younger daughter who was betrothed to Guillaume d’Auvergne.  This must be incorrect in light of the source 
2 CONC which names the older daughter, wife of Guillaume de Baffie, as "S" (see SEIGNEURS de BAFFIE, below).  In an earlier passage, La Mure describes the background to this betrothal: Philippe II King of France had dispossessed Guy [II]
2 CONC  of his county in 1210 in reprisal for his persecution of his brother Robert Bishop of Clermont, Guy de Dampierre Seigneur de Bourbon supported the king in this move, while the county of Forez supported the comte d’Auvergne[302]. 
2 CONC  The agreement is confirmed in the undated charter which records that "Reginaldus…primæ Lugdunensis ecclesiæ minister…et pater meus comes Forensis et Guido comes Arverniæ" agreed the marriages, firstly of "G. fratris mei" and "fil
2 CONC ias G. comitis Arverniæ", and secondly of "filius…dicti comitis Arverniæ" and "filiam […reliquæ filiæ fratris mei] fratris mei G. quondam comitis Forensis"[303].  This charter makes it clear that this daughter was the last remaini
2 CONC ng (unmarried) daughter ("reliquæ filiæ") of Comte Guy [III], but the document does not name her.  La Mure gives no indication of the basis on which he names her "Eléonor", but presumably his source was Justel’s Histoire d’Auvergn
2 CONC e (not yet consulted).  No record has been found which indicates that this betrothal was ever finalised into a marriage, although the late date of Guillaume [X]’s recorded marriage suggests that he may have been married before and
2 CONC  remarried only after the death of his earlier wife, who would presumably have died childless. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' (before 3 Feb 1225) as her second husband, ALEIDIS de Brabant, widow of ARNOLD [III] Graf van Looz en Rieneck, daughter of HENRI I Duke of Brabant & his first wife Mathilde de Flandre (-[5 Feb 1261/1267]).  The Genealogia 
2 CONC Ducum Brabantiæ Heredum Franciæ refers to the third of the four daughters of "Henricus dux" as the wife of "comes de Alvernia" and mother of "Robertum comitem Bolonie et Alvernie et fratres eius et sorores"[304].  The Oude Kronik 
2 CONC van Brabant names "Mariam, conthoralem Ottonis Quartus Romanorum imperatoris, Aleydam comitissam Auernie, Margaretam comitissam Gerardi comitis Ghelrie et Mechteldim, primo quidem comitissam Palatinam Rheni, postea…comitissam Holl
2 CONC andie" as the daughters of "Henricus…primus, dux Lotharingie" and his wife "Mechteldim, filiam Mathei Boloniensis comitis"[305].  "Willelmus…comes Arverniæ et Aleydis quondam comitissa de Los" renounced an inheritance from "dominu
2 CONC s dux Lotharingiæ", presumably in connection with their forthcoming marriage although the document does not specify this, by charter dated 1 Feb 1224[306].  She married thirdly ([1247/21 Apr 1251]) as his [second/third] wife, Arno
2 CONC ut [II] Heer van Wesemaal.  "Robertus comes Claremontis et Alverniæ, Aleydis mater eius, et Arnoldus dominus de Wensemale maritus" confirmed agreement concerning property by charter dated 21 Apr 1251[307].  Her third marriage is c
2 CONC onfirmed by a letter dated 1260 from "Ernoul chevalier Sire de Wesemale et Alys que fu contesse d’Auvergne sa femme" granted their rights in the county of Boulogne to "nostre cousine germaine la contesse Mahaut de Boloigne"[308]. 
2 CONC  "Robertus comes Alverniæ" confirmed his agreement with Henri Duke of Brabant that, if “Arnoldum dominum de Wesemale” died before “domina Aleyde comitissa Arverniæ uxore sua”, the latter would be invested with the county of Boulog
2 CONC ne, by charter dated 5 Feb 1260 (O.S.)[309]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT   Guillaume [X] & his wife had six children:  
