1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Jean I de Montfort
2 CONT (c.1228–1249, Cyprus), Count of Montfort from 1241 to 1249, son of Amaury de Montfort, count of Montfort, and of Béatrice of Burgundy.[1] In 1248 he joined Louis IX's crusader fleet.[2] Once the fleet arrived at Limassol, it was s
2 CONC cattered by fierce storms and was forced to wait there to regroup.[2] John died of sickness, while awaiting the rest of Louis's forces in Cyprus.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage
2 CONT In March 1248 he married Jeanne de Châteaudun,[3] Dame of Château-du-Loir, daughter of Geoffrey VI, Viscount of Châteaudun, and of Clémence des Roches. Their only child was:
2 CONT
2 CONT Beatrice de Montfort, Countess of Montfort-l'Amaury († 1312), who in 1260 married Robert IV (died 1282), comte de Dreux,[3] but according to the history he raised the son of John III of Bretagne , Jean Decoud or Decoude
2 CONT References
2 CONT  Maddicott 1995, p. xxvi.
2 CONT  Folda 2005, p. 238.www.celtic-casimir.com
2 CONT
2 CONT JEAN DE MONTFORT Comte de Montfort
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage Information:
2 CONT Jean married Jeanne DE CHÂTEAUDUN Dame de Château-de-Loire, daughter of Geoffroi VI DE CHÂTEAUDUN Vicomte de Châteaudun and Clemence DES ROCHES. (Jeanne DE CHÂTEAUDUN Dame de Château-de-Loire was born about 1227 in <Acre, Palestin
2 CONC e> and died after 1265.)
2 CONT
2 CONT  Pollock 2015, p. 188.www.celtic-casimir.com
2 CONT
2 CONT Jeanne DE CHÂTEAUDUN Dame de Château-de-Loire
2 CONT 	Born: Abt 1227, Acre, Palestine 
2 CONT 	Married (1): 1251 
2 CONT 	Died: After 1265
2 CONT
2 CONT Ancestral File Number: 91SD-B7. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage Information:
2 CONT Jeanne married Jean DE BRIENNE d' Acre, son of Jean DE BRIENNE King of Jerusalem and Berenguela (Berengaria) ALFONSEZ Infanta of Léon and Castile, in 1251. (Jean DE BRIENNE d' Acre was born in 1223 in Acre, Palestine and died in 1
2 CONC 296.)
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage Information:
2 CONT Jeanne also married Jean I DE MONTFORT Comte de Montfort, son of Amaury VI (VII) DE MONTFORT Duke of Narbonne, Comte de Toulouse and Beatrix DE VIENNOIS. 
