1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Arthur II de Bretagne''' (1262-1312)
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/79795273/artus-de-bretagne
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Arthur II, Duke of Brittany'''
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Arthur II (July 2, 1262 – August 27, 1312), of the House of Dreux, was Duke of Brittany from 1305 to his death. He was the first son of '''John II''' and '''Beatrice''', daughter of Henry III of England and Eleanor of Provence.
2 CONT
2 CONT After he inherited the ducal throne, he gave his brother John their father's English earldom of Richmond.
2 CONT
2 CONT As duke, Arthur was independent of the French crown. He divided his duchy into eight "battles": Leon, Kernev, Landreger, Penteur, Gwened, Naoned, Roazhon, and Sant Malou. In 1309, he convoked the first estates general (the ancesto
2 CONC r of the Breton parliament) in Brittany. It was the first time in French history that the third estate was represented.
2 CONT
2 CONT Arthur died at Château de L'Isle and was interred in a marble tomb of the cordeliers of Vannes. The tomb was vandalised during the French Revolution, but repaired and is on display today.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Marriages and children==
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1275, Arthur married '''Mary, Viscountess of Limoges''', daughter of Gui VI, Viscount of Limoges and Margaret, Lady of Molinot. Her maternal grandparents were Hugh IV, Duke of Burgundy and his first wife Yolande of Dreux. They 
2 CONC were parents of three children:
2 CONT
2 CONT John III, Duke of Brittany (March 8, 1286 - April 30, 1341).
2 CONT
2 CONT Guy de Dreux, Count of Penthievre (1287 - 1331). Father of Joanna of Dreux.
2 CONT
2 CONT Pierre de Dreux (1289 - 1312).
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary died in 1291. In May, 1292, Arthur was re-married to '''Yolande de Dreux, Countess of Montfort''', daughter of Robert IV, Count of Dreux and Beatrice de Montfort. They were parents of seven children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Jeanne de Dreux (1294 - 1363). Married Robert, Lord de Cassell.
2 CONT
2 CONT John IV, Duke of Brittany (1295 - September 16, 1345).
2 CONT
2 CONT Beatrice de Dreux (1295 - 1384). Married Guy X, Lord of Laval.
2 CONT
2 CONT Jeanne de Dreux (1296 - 1364). Married Robert, Count of Marle.
2 CONT
2 CONT Alice de Dreux (1297 - 1377). Married Bouchard VI, Count of Vendôme.
2 CONT
2 CONT Blanche de Dreux (born c. 1300). Considered to have died young.
2 CONT
2 CONT Marie de Dreux (1302 - 1371). A nun.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Ancestors==
2 CONT
2 CONT Arthur's ancestors in three generations'
2 CONT
2 CONT Arthur II, Duke of Brittany 	Father:
2 CONT
2 CONT John II, Duke of Brittany	Paternal Grandfather:
2 CONT
2 CONT John I, Duke of Brittany	Paternal Great-Grandfather:
2 CONT
2 CONT Peter I, Duke of Brittany
2 CONT
2 CONT Paternal Great-grandmother:
2 CONT
