2 CONT
2 CONT https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jean_IV_de_Bretagne  - This is not the same person / This his son
2 CONT
2 CONT John IV of Montfort (in Breton Yann Moñforzh, in French Jean de Montfort) (1295 – 16 September 1345 Château d'Hennebon), was duke of Brittany, from 1341 to his death. He was son of Duke Arthur II and Yolande de Dreux, countess of 
2 CONC Montfort, his second wife.
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage and issue
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1322 he succeeded his mother as count of Montfort, and in 1329, he married Joanna of Flanders at Chartres. They had two children:
2 CONT
2 CONT  John V, Duke of Brittany (1339–1399)
2 CONT
2 CONT  Joan of Brittany, Baroness of Drayton (1341 – aft. 20 October 1399), married before 21 October 1385 Ralph Basset, 4th Baron Basset de Drayton
2 CONT
2 CONT Breton War of Succession
2 CONT
2 CONT When his half-brother, duke John III, died with no male heirs in 1341, John IV decided to contest the rights of his niece, Joanna of Penthièvre, and her husband, Charles of Blois, to the duchy of Brittany. This led to the Breton W
2 CONC ar of Succession part of the Hundred Years' War. His patron in this quest was king Edward III of England.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ancestry
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_IV,_Duke_of_Brittany#Ancestry - This not the same person / this is his son
