2 CONT * [http://webcache.googleusercontent.com/search?q=cache:XWH18Gtvi20J:en.wikipedia.org/wiki/House_of_Cro%C3%BF '''House of Croÿ'''] - Wikipedia - English
2 CONT * '''Prince of Chimay and progenitor of the line of Croÿ-Solre'''
2 CONT * '''born''' - ca.1390/95 
2 CONT * '''died''' - 25 Mar 1473, Valenciennes
2 CONT * '''married''' - Marie of Lalaing (1390 - 1474)
2 CONT * '''children''' -
2 CONT # Jaqueline Croÿ, (1430 - 1500)
2 CONT # Philip de Croÿ-Chimay (1430 - 18 Sep 1482), lord of Quievrain
2 CONT # Catherine, (1440 - 1515) Jean II belonged to the powereful House fo Croÿ.  He wa the second surviving son of [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jean_I_de_Cro%C3%BF '''Jean I de Croÿ'''] and Marie de Craon. His elder brother was [http
2 CONC ://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Antoine_I_de_Cro%C3%BF '''Antoine I de Croÿ''']
2 CONT
2 CONT Jean II de Croÿ was a prominent member of the Burgundian court. He governed Hainaut andNamur in the name of the dukes of Burgandy as ''grand bailli de Hainaut''.  His dominions were centered on the town of Chimay, of which he beca
2 CONC me the first count. In 1430, he was made one of the very first '''Knights of the Order of the Golden Fleece'''.
2 CONT
2 CONT He had been godfather to [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Charles_the_Bold '''Charles the Bold'''] in 1433 and to the Dauphin in 1459.  He was also amongst those who took the [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Feast_of_the_Pheasant '''Ban
2 CONC quet of the oath of the Pheasant'''] in 1454. (car)
