1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Petronilla_of_Aquitaine
2 CONT
2 CONT  Sources: 
2 CONT The book, 'Eleanor of Aquitaine'
2 CONT The book, 'An Autobiography of Eleanor'
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Petronilla of Aquitaine
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Petronilla of Aquitaine (c. 1125 – 1193) was the daughter of William X of Aquitaine and Aenor of Châtellerault. She was the sister of Eleanor of Aquitaine, who was Queen consort of France and England. She is variously called Alix 
2 CONC (or Aelith in Occitan) and Petronilla; she typically went by Alix after her marriage, while Petronilla seems to have been her childhood name (she is referred to as such in her father's will).
2 CONT
2 CONT Petronilla accompanied her sister to the French court, where she met the very-married Count Raoul I of Vermandois, a cousin to her brother-in-law Louis VII of France. He repudiated his wife and married her, and they were excommuni
2 CONC cated by the Pope. Pope Innocent II promised to lift the excommunication, but recanted his promise in 1143. Hostilities flared, and Louis VII infamously burned Vitry. Finally the Pope died and his successor Pope Celestine II lifte
2 CONC d the excommunication at Council of Reims in 1144. However, Petronilla and Raoul divorced in 1151, as he remarried the next year. Petronilla remained a member of the French royal court and a constant companion to her sister Eleano
2 CONC r while she was imprisoned by her husband King Henry II in England and Wales. After Henry's death, Eleanor was freed, and Petronilla planned on returning to France. Yet,records of Petronilla after 1189 are scarce. It is believed t
2 CONC hat she came down with a fever on her voyage from England back to France and died in early 1190 before her arrival at port. Together Raoul and Petronilla had three children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth (1141-1151)
2 CONT
2 CONT Isabel Mabile (1143 - 28 March 1183), married Philip, Count of Flanders.
2 CONT
2 CONT Raoul II, count de Vermandois and Valois (1145-1167), married Margaret of Lorraine, later countess of Flanders. Died of leprosy.
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit]In fiction and literature
2 CONT
2 CONT Kristiana Gregory. Eleanor Crown Jewel of Aquitaine: France, 1136. Scholastic Inc. (2002). ISBN 0-439-16484-2. She is mentioned as Petronilla and sometimes just Petra in this fictional diary of her sister, Eleanor.
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit]References
2 CONT
2 CONT Kerrebrouck, Patrick van (2000). Les Capétiens 987-1328.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Sister of Eleanor of Aquitaine
