1 NAME Antoine /de Lalaing/ seigneur de Bugnicourt
2 GIVN Antoine
2 SURN de Lalaing
2 NSFX seigneur de Bugnicourt
2 _MARNM de Lalaing
1 SEX M
1 DEAT
2 DATE 8 JAN 1469
1 OCCU chevalier, seigneur de Bugnicourt (et de Hordaing ?), chambellan du duc de Bourgogne
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT Chevalier, seigneur de Bugnicourt. Chambellan du duc. Tué à la bataille de Granson (2 mars 1476) contre les suisses. Brassart conteste cette fin et le fait décéder le 8 janvier 1469. Il eut des enfants bâtards.
2 CONT Available Sources : F Brassart, 1879, L de Herckenrode, 1868, FV Goethals, 1862.
2 CONT Death
2 CONT Autre date possible: 5 avril 1476. 
2 CONT Autre date 8 janvier 1469. Source : F Brassart, 1879.
2 CONT Autre date de décès 9 janvier 1469. Source : FV Goethals, 1862.
2 CONT Death: L de Herckenrode, 1868.
2 CONT _____
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Antoine de Lalaing''', + 08/01/1470 ns (inh. à Lalaing) 
2 CONT - chevalier (armé au sacre de Louis XI à Reims le 15/08/1461),
2 CONT - seigneur de Bugnicourt (et de Hordaing ?), 
2 CONT - Chambellan du duc de Bourgogne,X à Montlhéry (1465) 
2 CONT
2 CONT ép. Marie de Noyelles-Vion, héritière d’Hangest (ép. 2) Gilles de Waziers, chevalier, seigneur d’Heudincourt) 
2 CONT
2 CONT X) liaison avec Catherine de Couvringhe
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Pattou, Etienne. “Famille & Seigneurs De Lalaing.” Racines et Histoire :''
2 CONT __________
2 CONT '''Antoine de Lalaing''', knight, lord of Bugnicourt, chamberlain of the duke, knighted at the coronation of King Louis XI in Rheims on August 15, 1461; he fought at Monthéry, alongside his brother Philippe (56). He would have mar
2 CONC ried Marie DE NOYELLES Wyon, heiress of Hangest, who married Gilles de Waziers, knight, lord of Heudincourt, according to the genealogists, who are without departure, reg. aux rémissions, B 1727, fo xxvij; in margin: " moiennant f
2 CONC ine ciuille "; it was the " finance " taxed in Lille by the chamber of the counted.
2 CONT
2 CONT It is doubtless more exact here than when they make Antoine de Lalaing die in 1477 under the blows of the Swiss while: he died on January 8, 1469 (old style), lying in the church of Lalaing, in the chapel of Notre-Dame de Sainghin
2 CONC ', where was a beautiful and large stone with its representation and its four quarters, which stone is now preserved in a private property of the village.
2 CONT
2 CONT He had from Catherine de Couvringhe, "for then not married", a bastard:
2 CONT
2 CONT ..A. Rodigue, bastard of Lalaing in 1505, squire and captain of the archers of the body of the archduke Philip the Handsome, king of Castile, legitimized, about this time, by this prince, without financing, "for regard of the virt
2 CONC ues and good deaths are in him, and of the great, leases and pleasant services which he has, all his eaige, faiz to feuz our predecessors, whom God absoille, and, to us, and has fencoires daily" (57). Molinet quotes him several ti
2 CONC mes, about tournaments, military expeditions, etc. He broke with a net a few times. He broke a golden net in a bar (cabinet of titles; genealogical table).
2 CONT He left a daughter:
2 CONT
2 CONT ….a. Jeanne de Lalaing, died on November 28, 1540, - wife of Lambert DE LIGNE, bastard of Barbançon, esquire, who died on November 20, 1555, natural son of Michel de Ligne, lord of Barbançon, who died in 1468, - rested with her hu
2 CONC sband, in the church of Boussu, where their epitaph is (58)
2 CONT In the great genealogical table of the Cabinet des titres, drawn up towards the end of the 16th century, she is mentioned, with her alliance, but without filiation.
2 CONT
2 CONT (57). Les lettres de légitimation furent enregistrées en la chambre des comptes à Lille, vers le mois de décembre 1505, au f°.iijc iiijxx xij vo du 17e reg. des chartes, La fin de ces lettres, notamment leur date, se trouvait sur 
2 CONC le fo. ijc iijxx xiij,qui contenait l'anoblissementdeNicolas le Canonne : cause pour laquelle cefeuillet a été arrachè du registre par les vandales révolutionnaires.
2 CONT (58) P. Anselme, Hist. généalog., Paris, 11733, in-f°, VIII, p. 34 c ; d'après Scohier.—Mémoires de la Société de Tournai, 1859, in-8o, VI, pp. 26 et 27. —Cf. Epitaphier de Malotau, tome IV, écrit en 1740, pp. 321 et 322 ; Ms. 886
2 CONC  de la Bibliothèque publique de Douai.
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Brassart, Felix, Société Académique, editor. Souvenirs De La Flandre Wallonne, Catalogue des Nobels de Nom, de Lalaing, Dix-Septieme, L. Crépin, 1882. un Comite Historique et Archeologique: Memories of Walloon Flanders: pp.45.''
