3 CITY Santpoort-Noord
3 STAE North Holland
3 CTRY The Netherlands
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Notes
2 CONT Available Sources: L de Herckenrode, 1868, F Brassart, 1879, FV Goethals, 1862, A Janse, 2001, FV Goethals, 1850, C Butkens, 1626.
2 CONT _____
2 CONT '''Yolande (Yolente) de Lalaing''' ° ~1422, avant 1448 + 15/08/1497
2 CONT (réside à Brederode en 1492) 
2 CONT
2 CONT ép. après 28/11/1445 Reinald (Renaud) II van Brederode (de la Maison princière de Hollande) heer van Vianen, - - vicomte d’Utrecht, 
2 CONT - chevalier de la Toison d’Or
2 CONT ° ~1414/15 + 16/10/1473 (Vianen) (frère de l’Evêque d’Utrecht)
2 CONT
2 CONT postérité Brederode
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Pattou, Etienne. “Famille & Seigneurs De Lalaing.” Racines et Histoire :''
2 CONT __________
2 CONT '''Yolente de Lalaing''', born around 1422, married to Renaud, sire DE BREDERODE, of the princely house of Holland, knight [of the Golden Fleece; whose posterity.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1492, widowed, she resided at the castle of Brederode (Molinet, IV, page 279).
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Brassart, Felix, Société Académique, editor. Souvenirs De La Flandre Wallonne, Catalogue des Nobels de Nom, de Lalaing, Dix-Septieme, L. Crépin, 1882. un Comite Historique et Archeologique: Memories of Walloon Flanders: pp. 46''
2 CONT __________.
2 CONT * Zie [http://www.historici.nl/Onderzoek/Projecten/DVN/lemmata/data/LalaingYolande '''Historici.nl...''']
2 CONT {{https://www.geni.com/media/proxy?media_id=6000000188915821821&size=large}}
2 CONT Yolande of Lalaing is kneeling before the Virgin Mary. Image from her book of hours, c. 1460 (Bodleian Library, Oxford).
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT LALAING, Yolande van (geb. Lallaing, Frankrijk ca. 1422 – gest. Santpoort 15-8-1497). Dochter van Willem van Lalaing (gest. 1475) en Johanna van Créquy. Yolande van Lalaing trouwde in 1445 (huwelijkse voorwaarden: 28-11) met Reino
2 CONC ud van Brederode (gest. 1473), ridder. Uit dit huwelijk werden ten minste 5 dochters en 2 zoons geboren. Yolande was het tweede kind en de oudste dochter van Willem van Lalaing en zijn Picardische vrouw Johanna van Créquy. Toen ha
2 CONC ar vader in 1433 een functie kreeg aan het hof van Isabella van Portugal, echtgenote van Filips de Goede, nam hij zijn circa twaalfjarige dochter Yolande en haar zusje Isabella mee om hen daar een Bourgondische opvoeding te laten 
2 CONC doorlopen. Haar oudere broer Jacques kreeg zijn leerschool aan het hof van de hertog zelf – hij zou uitgroeien tot een van de bekendste toernooihelden van de vijftiende eeuw. In 1440 verhuisde Yolande naar Den Haag, waar haar vade
2 CONC r was benoemd tot Bourgondisch stadhouder in Holland en Zeeland. Willem raakte er verwikkeld in de partijstrijd tussen Hoeken en Kabeljauwen. Die strijd liep zo uit de hand dat hij in 1445 als stadhouder moest worden vervangen. In
2 CONC  het kader van de financiële afwikkeling van zijn ambtsperiode trof hij een regeling met een belangrijke schuldeiser, de Hoekse edelman Reinoud van Brederode, heer van Brederode en Vianen. Willem schonk hem zijn 23-jarige dochter 
2 CONC Yolande.
2 CONT
2 CONT See more at: http://www.historici.nl/Onderzoek/Projecten/DVN/lemmata/data/LalaingYolande#sthash.IF8x1kEN.dpuf
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT De Brederodekroniek voor Yolande van Lalaing (The Brederode Chronicle for Yolande van Lalaing)
2 CONT https://hcommons.org/deposits/item/hc:21485/
2 CONT
2 CONT The publication "De Brederodekroniek voor Yolande van Lalaing" (by Thijs Porck, published in the 2009 volume Yolande de Lalaing (1422–1497), kasteelvrouwe van Brederode, edited by E. den Hartog and H. Wijsman) is a crucial modern 
2 CONC scholarly study for late-medieval Dutch nobility, history, and codicology.
2 CONT
2 CONT While titled "an old source" in a reference list, it actually represents a modern, foundational piece of historiographical research examining how Yolande de Lalaing, Chatelaine of Brederode, used history, manuscripts, and patronag
2 CONC e to solidify her family's rank.
2 CONT
2 CONT Key Value of the Document for Historical & Genealogical Research
2 CONT 1. Proof of Female Noble Patronage & Political Strategy
2 CONT The paper focuses on the Brederode Chronicle (Brederodekroniek), commissioned from the Carmelite friar Johannes a Leydis (Jan van Leiden).
2 CONT The Insight: Following the death or captivity of her husband, Reinoud II van Brederode, during the Hook and Cod conflicts, Yolande de Lalaing actively commissioned historiographical works.
2 CONT Why it matters: It demonstrates that late-medieval noblewomen were not passive figures; Yolande intentionally used family chronicles as political propaganda to project ancestral prestige, protect property claims, and assert her fa
2 CONC mily's legitimacy under Burgundian rule.
2 CONT 2. Redating and Contextualizing Late 15th-Century Manuscripts
2 CONT Thijs Porck’s chapter performs a detailed codicological and textual analysis of the surviving Middle Dutch and Latin manuscripts of the chronicle:
2 CONT The Insight: Porck re-dates the composition of both the Dutch and Latin versions of the Brederodekroniek.
2 CONT Why it matters: Knowing when a manuscript was authored helps historians separate contemporary 15th-century facts from back-dated ancestral legends created to glorify the House of Brederode.
2 CONT 3. Untangling Family Lineages & Ideology
2 CONT The chronicle traces the ancestral line of the Lords of Brederode (and their connections to the Counts of Holland and Hainaut noble families like Lalaing).
2 CONT The Insight: It analyzes how noble genealogical collections were structured during the last quarter of the 15th century.
2 CONT Why it matters: It helps researchers see where the medieval author relied on solid court archives versus where they fabricated or embellished connections to ancient heroes (such as Trojan descent myths or exaggerated feudal ties) 
2 CONC to satisfy their patron's prestige.
2 CONT 4. Insight into Cultural and Book History
2 CONT Published as part of the Kastelenstichting Holland en Zeeland monograph on Yolande, this research links:
2 CONT The literary culture of the Holland/Hainaut borderlands.
2 CONT The specific library holdings and manuscript commissions under Yolande's household at Batestein / Santpoort.
2 CONT How French-speaking Hainaut noblewomen (like the Lalaings) integrated into Dutch-speaking regional politics in Holland.
2 CONT Summary Recommendation
2 CONT If you are evaluating this work for research on Yolande de Lalaing, the House of Brederode, or 15th-century Netherlands nobility:
2 CONT Use it to understand context and intent: It explains why late-15th-century genealogical claims were written the way they were.
2 CONT Primary vs. Secondary: While Johannes a Leydis’s underlying chronicle is a 15th-century source, Porck's study is a modern 21st-century critical filter that helps you separate historical genealogical truth from 15th-century politic
2 CONC al spin.
2 CONT
2 CONT ___________
2 CONT
2 CONT Stamboom nr. :  209.383.
2 CONT
2 CONT Generatie :  18.
