1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Henry I of England
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Illegitimate children
2 CONT
2 CONT King Henry is famed for holding the record for the largest number of acknowledged illegitimate children born to any English king, with the number being around 20 or 25. He had many mistresses, and identifying which mistress is the
2 CONC  mother of which child is difficult. His illegitimate offspring for whom there is documentation are:
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert, 1st Earl of Gloucester. Often, said to have been a son of Sybil Corbet.
2 CONT
2 CONT Maud FitzRoy, married Conan III, Duke of Brittany
2 CONT
2 CONT Constance FitzRoy, married Richard de Beaumont
2 CONT
2 CONT Mabel FitzRoy, married William III Gouet
2 CONT
2 CONT Aline FitzRoy, married Matthieu I of Montmorency
2 CONT
2 CONT Gilbert FitzRoy, died after 1142. His mother may have been a sister of Walter de Gand.
2 CONT
2 CONT Emma, born c. 1138; married Gui de Laval, Lord Laval. [Uncertain, born 2 years after Henry died.][1]
