1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Adelaide de Maurienne ([1092]-Montmartre 18 Nov 1154, bur Montmartre, Église Abbatiale de Saint-Pierre).
2 CONT
2 CONT Parents: Comte Humbert II  (son of Amadee II Comte de Savoie & his wife Jeanne [de Genève] ([1072]-Moûtiers 19 Oct 1103, bur Moûtiers)  & Gisele  de Bourgogne (daughter of Guillaume I Comte Palatin de Bourgogne, Comte de Vienne et
2 CONC  de Mâcon & his wife Etiennette --- ([1075]-after 1133))
2 CONT
2 CONT x (Paris [25/30] Mar 1115) Louis Vi “Le Gros" King of France (son of Philippe I King of France & his first wife Bertha of Holland (Paris end 1081-Château Bethizy, near Paris 1 Aug 1137, bur église de l'Abbaye royale de Saint-Denis
2 CONC ).
2 CONT * Philip of France (1116–1131).
2 CONT * Louis VII (1120 – 18 November 1180), King of France.
2 CONT * Henry (1121–1175), Archbishop of Reims.
2 CONT * Hugues (b. c. 1122).
2 CONT * Robert (c. 1123–11 October 1188), Count of Dreux.
2 CONT * Constance (c. 1124–16 August 1176), married first Eustace IV, Count of Boulogne and then Raymond V of Toulouse.
2 CONT * Philip (1125–1161), Bishop of Paris. Not to be confused with his elder brother.
2 CONT * Peter (c. 1125–1183), married Elizabeth, Lady of Courtenay.
2 CONT * a daughter, whose name is not known, who died in infancy and was interred at the Abbey of Saint-Victor, Paris.
2 CONT
2 CONT xx ([1138]), Mathieu [I] Seigneur De Montmorency (son of Bouchard [III] Seigneur de Montmorency & his first wife Agnès de Beaumont Dame de Conflans (-[2 Aug/31 Dec] 1160).)
2 CONT * Adèle (or Aelis or Alix) of Montmorency.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Sources:
2 CONT * http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SAVOY.htm
2 CONT *https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Adelaide_of_Maurienne
2 CONT *https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ad%C3%A9la%C3%AFde_de_Savoie
2 CONT
2 CONT ------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT ==In Medlands:http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SAVOY.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT Comte Humbert II m ([1090]) as her first husband, GISELE de Bourgogne, daughter of GUILLAUME I Comte Palatin de Bourgogne, Comte de Vienne et de Mâcon & his wife Etiennette --- ([1075]-after 1133).
2 CONT [They had [seven] children, the eldest being]:
2 CONT >1.         '''ADELAIDE de Maurienne ([1092]-Montmartre 18 Nov 1154, bur Montmartre, église abbatiale de Saint-Pierre).'''  Her first marriage is recorded by Orderic Vitalis, who also names her father and her four oldest sons[165]
2 CONC . The De Genere Comitum Flandrensium, Notæ Parisienses records "filiam Humberti comitis Morienne" as wife of "Ludovicum regem Grossum"[166].   The Chronicle of Alberic de Trois-Fontaines names "regina Alaydis…soror Amadei comitis 
2 CONC Sabaudie" as wife of "Ludovici Grossi"[167].  She exercised considerable influence over her husband, playing an active part in the downfall of Etienne de Garlande, Chancellor of France.  After the accession of her son as King Loui
2 CONC s VII in 1137, Adelaide conspired against Suger, Abbé de Saint-Denis, triggering a quarrel with her son who exiled her and her second husband to her lands in Compiègne.  Her second marriage is confirmed by an undated charter which
2 CONC  records a donation to the priory of Saint-Nicolas d´Acy, near Senlis made in the presence of "dominæ Adelæ reginæ et domini Mathei mariti eius"[168].  In 1153, she retired to the church of the Abbaye de Saint-Pierre at Montmartre
2 CONC , which she had founded[169].  The necrology of the abbey of Saint-Denis records the death "XIV Kal Dec" of "Adelaidis regina"[170].  m firstly (Paris [25/30] Mar 1115) LOUIS VI "le Gros" King of France, son of PHILIPPE I King of 
2 CONC France & his first wife Bertha of Holland (Paris end 1081-Château Bethizy, near Paris 1 Aug 1137, bur église de l'Abbaye royale de Saint-Denis).  m secondly ([1138]) as his second wife, MATHIEU [I] Seigneur de Montmorency, son of 
2 CONC BOUCHARD [III] Seigneur de Montmorency & his first wife Agnès de Beaumont Dame de Conflans (-[2 Aug/31 Dec] 1160). 
2 CONT * http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SAVOY.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT -------------------------
