2 CONT ** 3.         MILON de Courtenay (-after 1138, bur Fontaine-Jean). … m [secondly] (before [1110/16]) ELISABETH de Nevers, daughter of RENAUD [II] Comte de Nevers et d'Auxerre & his first wife [Ita Raymonde] de Forez et de Lyon (be
2 CONC fore 1085-after [1120/39]). Milon & his [second] wife had three children: 
2 CONT *** c)         RENAUD de Courtenay ([1105/20]-[27 Sep 1194]).  The Continuator of Aimon of Fleury names “Willermum, Ioscelinum et Rainaldum” as the children of “Milonem de Cortinaco” and his wife “sorore comitis Nivernensis”[124].
2 CONC   Seigneur de Courtenay. [144] … m firstly ([1135/40]) [HELVISE], daughter of [FERRY de Donjon & his [first] wife ---] ([1120/25]-[after 1155?]).  … m secondly ([1150/55]) HAWISE d’Avranches, daughter of ROBERT d’Avranches & his w
2 CONC ife Mathilde Avenill ([after 1132]-1 Aug 1209). … Renaud & his first wife had four children: 
2 CONT ****1.         ELISABETH de Courtenay ([1140/45]-14 Sep after 1205).  …  m (before 24 Nov 1160) PIERRE de France, son of LOUIS VI King of France & his wife Adélaïde de Maurienne ([1126]-Palestine 10 Mar [1180/10 Apr 1183]).  He su
2 CONC cceeded as Seigneur de Courtenay, de Montargis, de Châteaurenard, de Champignelles, de Tanlay, de Charny et de Charenton, by right of his wife. -        SEIGNEURS de COURTENAY (CAPET). 
2 CONT **** 2.         ADELINE de Courtenay ([1142/48?]-after 1190).  m AVALON [III] Seigneur de Seignelay, son of DAIMBERT [I] Seigneur de Seignelay & his wife Alpazia --- ([1140/45?]-[1200]). 
2 CONT **** 3.         GUILLAUME de Courtenay ([1140/45]-after [1167/68], maybe before 1170)   m MATILDA, daughter of ROBERT FitzEdith [illegitimate son of Henry I King of England] & his [second] wife Mathilde d’Avranches (-1224).
2 CONT **** 4.         [RENAUD] de Courtenay (-[1194]).  … m (1178 or before) HAWISE Lady of Okehampton, daughter of [GEOFFROY de Crimes/GUILLAUME de Curcy] & his wife Mathilde d'Avranches (-31 Jul 1219). 
2 CONT
