3 CONT Original undifferenced Coat of Arms of Courtenay: Or, three torteaux. Apparently adopted by Renaud de Courtenay before his death in 1190 and before the split of the family into French and English branches, as the arms are used bot
3 CONC h in France and England. These are therefore very early arms as heraldry came into widespread use from about 1200 to 1215
