2 CONT Hedwige de Donjon1
2 CONT
2 CONT F, #3775
2 CONT
2 CONT Last Edited=23 Oct 2007
2 CONT
2 CONT Hedwige de Donjon is the daughter of Frederick de Donjon, Seigneur de Donjon. She married Renaud de Courtenay, Seigneur de Courtenay, son of Miles de Courtenay, Seigneur de Courtenay and Ermengarde de Nevers.1
2 CONT
2 CONT Hedwige de Donjon was living in 1158.1
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Hedwige de Donjon and Renaud de Courtenay, Seigneur de Courtenay
2 CONT
2 CONT Renaud de Courtenay+ d. 27 Sep 11941
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert de Courtenay+ d. 12091
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth de Courtenay+ d. a 12051
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT
2 CONT [S37] Charles Mosley, editor, Burke's Peerage, Baronetage & Knightage, 107th edition, 3 volumes (Wilmington, Delaware, U.S.A.: Burke's Peerage (Genealogical Books) Ltd, 2003), volume 1, page 1122. Hereinafter cited as Burke's Peer
2 CONC age and Baronetage, 107th edition.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References 
2 CONT *Burke's Peerage & Baronetage, 106th Edition, Charles Mosley Editor-in-Chief, 1999, Page: 833. https://hammroots.com/getperson.php?personID=I24680&tree=Main Renaud de Courtenay, Lord of Courtenay; accompanied Louis VII of France o
2 CONC n the Second Crusade but quarreled with him so that Louis seized his French possessions and bestowed them, with Renaud's daughter (Elizabeth) in marriage, on his (Louis') own younger brother Pierre; [Renaud subsequently threw in h
2 CONC is lot with the English kings and was granted the Lordship of Sutton (now Sutton Courtenay), on the Berks-Oxon borders by Henry II 1161; accompanied Henry II to Wexford in the Irish expedition of 1172; - Disputed] married 1st Hedw
2 CONC ige (living 1148-58), sister of Guy du Donjon; [married 2nd Maud, Dame du Sap (dsp 1224), daughter of Robert Fitz Roy (illegitimate son of Henry I of England) by his wife Maud d'Avranches - Disputed].
