1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Not the daughter of https://www.geni.com/people/Reginald-I-de-Courtenay-1st-lord-of-Sutton/6000000188589299896
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT From Peter Stewart, post at SGM, 27 January 2003 < [https://groups.google.com/g/soc.genealogy.medieval/c/psv2U0Vkd-s/m/wERwaoKEHmMJ GoogleGroups] > “Parents of Elisabeth de Courtenay”
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT The following account of the first Courtenay family's last generations was given, largely from earlier secondary sources, in _Histoire généalogique et chronologique de la Maison royale de France..._ by Père Anselme (Pierre de Guib
2 CONC ours) & others, third edition, 9 vols (Paris, 1726-33), vol I pp 474 and 527-8:
2 CONT
2 CONT *1 Miles, seigneur de Courtenay, died after 1127 [NB actually in or after 1138 when he last occurs], married ca 1095 Ermengarde de Nevers
2 CONT **2 (their third son) Renaud, seigneur de Courtenay, allegedly married an unnamed sister of Guy du Donjon [who is stated wrongly to have been living in 1148], also described as daughter of Frederic, seigneur du Donjon
2 CONT ***3a Elisabeth, died 14 September in or after 1205, married Pierre de France (ancestors of the second French Courtenay line)
2 CONT ***3b ''Unnamed daughter, died sp, married Avalon, seigneur de Saillenay
2 CONT ''
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT From Peter Stewart, SGM, 8 November 2019:
2 CONT
2 CONT https://groups.google.com/g/soc.genealogy.medieval/c/psv2U0Vkd-s/m/wERwaoKEHmMJ
2 CONT
2 CONT The name of Elisabeth's sister who married Augalo II of Seignelay was either Adelina or Adelvia - her name was given in a charter for Saint-Jean de Sens abbey dated 1194, read as Adelvia by a copyist in 1729 but as Adelina by the 
2 CONC archivist of Auxerre in 1882. 
2 CONT
2 CONT A charter of her husband dated 1190 is not helpful about this, as he referred to her by initial only, "laudavit A., uxor mea". 
2 CONT
2 CONT They had sons named Dainbert and Frederic: it's interestig that the latter name doesn't appear before this in the Seignelay or Courtenay families and possibly came from the step-father of Adelina/Adelvia, Frederic of Donjon, seign
2 CONC eur of Yerres.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT https://groups.google.com/g/soc.genealogy.medieval/c/psv2U0Vkd-s/m/FBBej7hKAgAJ
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT The ordinal of her husband should be III, not II, and his name is variously given as Augalo[n], Argalo[n], Avalo[n], and perhaps other forms. It was clearly Agalo on his seal, see here: 
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.sigilla.org/fr/sgdb/empreinte/7092
