1 NOTE {geni:about_me} -http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/toulcentw.htm#BeatrixLautrecMPhilippeLautrec
2 CONT
2 CONT i)     '''     BEATRIX''' (-after 21 Mar 1336).  Vicomtesse de Lautrec.  The marriage contract between “Guidone de Levis dom. Mirapicis et...Mathei de Levis filii sui” and “domina Aladayssi relicta dom. Bertrandi condam vicecomiti
2 CONC s Lautric...Biatricis filie sue et filie et heredis dicti Bertrandi”, with the option to marry “Elitz filie dicti dom. Bertrandi” should Beatrix die, is dated 2/5 Jan 1295 (O.S.), ratified 18/20 Jan 1295 (O.S.)[389].  The marriage
2 CONC  contract between “Gui de Lévis sgr de Mirepoix...son fils Philippe de Levis” and “Beatrix vicomtesse de Lautrec...sa mère Aladays”, noting her previous betrothal to “Mathieu de Lévis” and subject to Papal dispensation, is dated 1
2 CONC 0 Sep 1296[390].  Pope Boniface VIII issued the dispensation for the marriage 3 Jun 1297, referring to her earlier contract to marry “quondam Matheus de Levis miles frater tuus fili Philippe”[391].  “Alazia fille de feu...Guill. B
2 CONC . de Najac veuve de Bertr. vic de Lautrec” granted her rights in “castrum nostrum de Savinhaco” to “Beatrix notre fille aînée et héritière universelle dud. Bertr.” by charter dated 30 Jun 1297[392].  The date of her second marriag
2 CONC e is estimated from the following document: a charter dated 11 Mar 1310 (O.S.) records a dispute between “Bertrandi de Guto militis vicecomitis Lautricensis” and “dominam A. de Monteforti comitissam Vindocinensem” concerning “loca
2 CONC  de Cabanesio”[393].  A charter dated Nov 1313 recorded payment by the convent of Avignon Sainte-Claire to “Bertr. de Guto vicomte de Lomagne et d’Auvillars et...sa demme Béatrix épouse de feu Phil. de Lévis”[394].  "Béatrix de La
2 CONC utrec" bequeathed money for her future marriage to her daughter Regine, by her testament dated 30 Jul 1315[395].  Jean I Comte d´Armagnac, acting for his wife "fille et heritière de feu Bertrand de Goth vicomte de Lomagne et d´Auv
2 CONC illars", assigned a pension to "Béatrix de Lautrec, veuve de Bertrand de Goth" by charter dated 10 Jun 1324[396].  "Regina de Gutto comitissa Armaniaci Fesenciaci et Ruthenensis vicecomitissaque Leomaniæ et Altavillaris", under he
2 CONC r testament dated 12 Aug 1325, appointed "dominæ Beatrici vice-comitissæ Lautricensi matri suæ…Rogerio de Armaniaco et Domino Amanevo de Lebreto" as her executors[397].  “Beatrix vicomtesse de Lautrec” promised not to dispose of h
2 CONC er assets without the consent of “ses fils...Philippe et Bertrand de Lévis”, with the consent of “...vicomte Guillaume cousin de lad. dame”, by charter dated 28 Nov 1326, and committed to pay certain sums to her sons “pro custodia
2 CONC  castri [de La Focz]” where she was living by charter dated 29 May 1327[398].  “Beatrix vic. de Lautrec” ordered her subjects to swear allegiance to “nos fils Philippe et à Bertrand” by charter dated 21 Mar 1335 (O.S.)[399].  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Betrothed '''(2/5 Jan 1296) to MATHIEU de Lévis, son of GUY [III] de Lévis Maréchal de Mirepoix & his wife Isabelle de Marly [Montmorency] (-[Jan/Sep] 1296).  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' firstly (contract 19 Sep 1296, before 28 Jul 1298) PHILIPPE de Lévis, son of GUY [III] de Lévis Maréchal de Mirepoix & his wife Isabelle de Marly [Montmorency] (-after 15 Mar 1305).  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''m''' secondly (before 11 Mar 1311) BERTRAND de Goth, son of ARNAUD GARSIE de Goth [later Vicomte de Lomagne et d´Auvillars] & his wife Miramonde de Mauléon (-[22 May/4 Jun] 1324).  He succeeded his father in 1311 as Vicomte de 
2 CONC Lomagne et d´Auvillars. 
