1 NOTE Robert de Bellomont, 2nd son, 2nd Earl of Leicester, Lord of Breteuil andPoci, in France, was born in 1104. This nobleman stoutly adhered to HenryI upon all occasions, was with him at his decease in 1135, and heafterwards as staun
2 CONC chly supported the interests of Henry's grandson,Henry II, upon whose accession to the throne his lordship was constitutedJustice of England. He married Amicia, daughter and heir of Robert deWaer, Earl of Norfolk, by whom he had a
2 CONC  son Robert and two daughters. TheEarl, who was a munificent benefactor of the church, and founder ofseveral religious houses, died in 1167, after having lived for fifteenyears a canon regular in the Abbey of Leicester. He was suc
2 CONC ceeded by hisson, Robert.
