2 CONT    2. Hadwisa/Avisa of Gloucester (circa 1152 – 1189). Married[1] Geoffrey FitzPiers, Earl of Essex de Mandeville, son of Piers de Lutegareshale and Lady Maud de Mandeville of Costow.
2 CONT
2 CONT    3. Mabel FitzRobert of Gloucester (b. 1155); married 1.Amaury V de Montfort 2.Gruffudd ap Ifor Bach.
2 CONT
2 CONT    4. Amice FitzRobert, Countess of Gloucester (b. 1160, Tewkesbury, Gloucestershire). Married Richard de Clare, 4th Earl of Hertford.
2 CONT
2 CONT    5. Isabel of Gloucester (b. 1170, Gloucester). She was married three times:
2 CONT
2 CONT          1. Prince John
2 CONT
2 CONT          2. Geoffrey FitzGeoffrey de Mandeville, 2nd Earl of Essex.
2 CONT
2 CONT          3. Hubert de Burgh, 1st Earl of Kent.
2 CONT
2 CONT The earl died on his birthday in 1183; his wife Hawise survived him. Since their only son, Robert, predeceased his father, their daughters became co-heirs to the Gloucester inheritance.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Geoffrey married Hawisa Fergant of Brittany (abt. 1105-?). They had two sons, Vicomte Eudes II Porhoet (1122-?) and Alan la Zouche(1132-?). 
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Porhoët
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT William Fitz Robert, 2nd Earl of Gloucester
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Family and children
2 CONT
2 CONT He was married Hawise de Beaumont of Leicester, daughter of Robert de Beaumont, 2nd Earl of Leicester and Amica de Gael and had children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert FitzRobert (1151, Cardiff, Glamorganshire – 1166 Unmd Vp, Cardiff, Glamorganshire).
2 CONT
2 CONT Hadwisa/Avisa of Gloucester (circa 1152 – 1189). Married[1] Geoffrey FitzPiers, Earl of Essex de Mandeville, son of Piers de Lutegareshale and Lady Maud de Mandeville of Costow.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mabel FitzRobert of Gloucester (b. 1155); married 1.Amaury V de Montfort 2.Gruffudd ap Ifor Bach.
2 CONT
2 CONT Amice FitzRobert, Countess of Gloucester (b. 1160, Tewkesbury, Gloucestershire). Married Richard de Clare, 4th Earl of Hertford.
2 CONT
2 CONT Isabel of Gloucester (b. 1170, Gloucester). She was married three times:
2 CONT
2 CONT Prince John
2 CONT
2 CONT Geoffrey FitzGeoffrey de Mandeville, 2nd Earl of Essex.
2 CONT
2 CONT Hubert de Burgh, 1st Earl of Kent.
2 CONT
2 CONT The earl died on his birthday in 1183; his wife Hawise survived him. Since their only son, Robert, predeceased his father, their daughters became coheirs to the Gloucester inheritance.
