2 CONT Robert de Quincy  Birth unknown  England Death 1217  London, City of London, Greater London, England Burial  Church of The Hospitallers  Clerkenwell, London Borough of Islington, Greater London, England Add to Map  Memorial ID 111
2 CONC 309627
2 CONT
2 CONT Eldest son of Saher de Quincy and Margaret de Beaumont. Grandson of Robert de Quincy and Orabilis of Leuchars, Sir Robert de Beaumont and Petronilla Grandmesnil.
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert married Hawise of Chester, the daughter of Hugh, the Earl of Chester and Bertrade de Montfort, the daughter of Simon,the Count of Evreux. They had one daughter, Margaret, who married John de Lacy, Walter Marshall, Earl of P
2 CONC embroke and Richard de Wiltshire.
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert died at London at an early age. After his death, Hawise granted a rent to the brethren of the Hospital of Jerusalem in England for the foundation of a chantry at the Hospitallers for the soul of her husband. A few years lat
2 CONC er, she received a charter from her brother, Ranulph, the Earl of Chester and Lincoln, presenting her with the Earldom of Lincoln. After Ranulph's death, King Henry III granted the 3rd penny of Lincolnshire to Hawise, and she beca
2 CONC me the Countess of Lincoln. She received the castle and manor of Bolingbroke, with the Earl's lands in Lindsey and Holland. She died shortly before 19 Feb 1243 when her son-in-law, Walter Marshall, restored Bolingbroke Castle to t
2 CONC he king.
2 CONT
