2 CONT Birth: 1174 in Winchester, County Hampshire, ENGLAND
2 CONT Death: 25 APR 1264 in ENGLAND but buried in Brackley, County Aberdeenshire, SCOTLAND Event: Note Coat of Arms, URL http://www.geog.port.ac.uk/webmap/hantsmap/hantsmap/topics/blazon06.htm Occupation: Constable of SCOTLAND 
2 CONT
2 CONT This City is governed by a Mayor, Aldermen, Burgesses, Recorder, and Common-Council. The Citizens had formerly the Privilege of overseeing the King or Queen's Kitchin and Laundry at the Coronation, as the Citizens of London had th
2 CONC e Care of the Wine-Cellar, as Holinshed, and other Chronicles tell us. Here are weekly two plentiful Markets on Wednesday and Saturday, and a Fair on the first Monday in Lent. It sends two Citizens to Parliament, who are in this S
2 CONC ession, George Rodney Bridges Esq; and Lord William Pawlet. This City has given a Title to many ancient and Noble families, of which our Histories give this Account, viz. Clito, a noble Saxon, at the Time of the Conquest, was Earl
2 CONC  of Winchester, but at the coming of the Normans he was deprived of his Estate and Honour. After him we find none bearing that Title, till K. John made Saer de Quincy, Earl of Winchester, whose Arms were a Fesse with a Label of Se
2 CONC ven, as appears from his Seal. He married Margaret, the youngest Sister and Coheir of Robert, Earl of Leicester, and by her had one Son and Heir.
2 CONT
2 CONT Roger de Quincy, who bore for his Arms, in a Field Gules, seven Mascles voided, Or: He married the eldest Daughter and Co-heir of Alan, Lord Galloway, in Scotland, but by her had three Daughters only, of whom the eldest was marrie
2 CONC d to William de Ferrariis, Earl of Derby, the second to Alan de Zouche, and the youngest to Comino, Earl of Buchan, in Scotland, whereupon the Honour was extinct, and so continued for a considerable Time, till .... (there is a ful
2 CONC l page with more names at the web site below)
2 CONT
2 CONT SOURCE: "Cox's Hampshire, 1738", URL http://www.geog.port.ac.uk/webmap/hantsmap/hantsmap/cox1/cox1tx42.htm
