2 CONT Hawise of Chester, Countess of Lincoln (1180- 6 June 1241/3 May 1243), was an Anglo-Norman noblewoman and a wealthy heiress. Her father was Hugh de Kevelioc, 5th Earl of Chester. She was the sister and a co-heiress of Ranulf de Bl
2 CONC ondeville, 6th Earl of Chester. She was created suo jure 1st Countess of Lincoln in 1232. She was the wife of Robert de Quincy, by whom she had one daughter, Margaret, who became heiress to her title and estates. She was also know
2 CONC n as Hawise of Kevelioc.
2 CONT
2 CONT Hugh de Kevelioc, 3rd Earl of Chester 
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1169 he married Bertrade de Montfort of Evreux, daughter of Simon III de Montfort. She was the cousin of King Henry, who gave her away in marriage. Their children were: 
2 CONT
2 CONT Ranulph de Blondeville de Meschines, 4th Earl of Chester 
2 CONT
2 CONT Maud of Chester (1171-1233), married David of Scotland, 8th Earl of Huntingdon 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mabel of Chester, married William d'Aubigny, 3rd Earl of Arundel 
2 CONT
2 CONT Agnes of Chester (died November 2, 1247), married William de Ferrers, 4th Earl of Derby 
2 CONT
2 CONT Hawise of Chester (1180-1242), married Robert II de Quincy 
