1 NOTE Regent of Jerusalem 1212-1225, Emperor of Constantinople 1228 - 1237.
1 NOTE He was also Regent of Jerusalem 1212-1225. And Emperor of Constantinople 1228-1237.
1 NOTE John, a French nobleman, became king by his marriage to Queen Marie de 
2 CONT Montferrat of Jerusalem. When Marie died, their young daughter Yolande 
2 CONT succeeded as queen under John's regency. After playing an important part 
2 CONT in the Fifth Crusade, John lived and traveled in western Europe, seeking 
2 CONT support for another Crusade. In 1222 he betrothed Yolande to the Holy 
2 CONT Roman emperor Frederick II. Upon their marriage in 1225, Frederick quickly 
2 CONT claimed the crown of Jerusalem. John, also claiming the crown, commanded 
2 CONT papal troops in an attack upon Frederick's possessions in Italy. In 1229 
2 CONT John became regent and coemperor with Baldwin II, the 12-year-old Latin 
2 CONT ruler of Constantinople. In this capacity, he defended the Latin Empire 
2 CONT against attacks by the Byzantines and their Bulgarian allies.
1 NOTE King of Jerusalem, Jean de Brienne
