2 CONT ====ThePeerage.com: [http://www.thepeerage.com/p10690.htm#i106893 Sir John de Beaumont, 2nd Lord Beaumont]
2 CONT * '''Vitals''': M, #106893, b. circa 1317, d. between 10 May 1342 and 25 May 1342 (Consanguinity Index=0.01%)
2 CONT * '''Last Edited'''=3 Jul 2022
2 CONT * '''Bio:''' [John] was born circa 1317.2 He was the son of Henry Beaumont, 1st Earl of Buchan and Alice Comyn.2 He married Lady Eleanor Plantagenet, daughter of Henry Plantagenet, 3rd Earl of Lancaster and Matilda de Chaworth, be
2 CONC fore June 1337.1,2 He died between 10 May 1342 and 25 May 1342.2 He was appointed Knight on 2 May 1338.2 He fought in the campaign in France in 1339.2 He succeeded as the 2nd Baron Beaumont [E., 1309] on 10 March 1339/40.2
2 CONT * '''Children of Sir John...and Eleanor:'''
2 CONT ** 1. Joan Beaumont1 d. a 1400 '''<—''' Either this is an error by Alison Weir, or another, reliable source is absolutely necessary to confirm a Joan being a daughter. Did Daryl Lundy include this assumed child without careful scr
2 CONC utiny first is unknown. (Ken Shelley, 21 Mar 2026)
2 CONT ** 2.Henry de Beaumont, 3rd Lord Beaumont+1 b. c 1340, d. 25 Jul 1369
2 CONT * '''Sources'''
2 CONT ** 1. Alison Weir, ''Britain's Royal Families: The Complete Genealogy'' (London, U.K.: The Bodley Head, 1999), p. 78.
2 CONT ** 2. G.E. Cokayne, et al, ''The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain and the United Kingdom, Extant, Extinct or Dormant,'' new ed., (1910-1959; reprint in 6 volumes, Gloucester, U.K.: Alan Sutton Publishi
2 CONC ng, 2000), Vol. 2, p. 60.
2 CONT ** 3. Charles Mosley, ed., ''Burke's Peerage and Baronetage,'' 106th ed., (Crans, Switzerland: Burke's Peerage (Genealogical Books) Ltd, 1999), Vol. 1, p. 228. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ====FMG: English Lords [https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/ENGLISHNOBILITYMEDIEVAL3.htm#JohnBeaumontdied1342 A–C].
2 CONT * 7. '''JOHN Beaumont''' (–[10/25] May 1342). He succeeded his father as Lord Beaumont. '''m''' (before Jun 1337) as her first husband, [https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/ENGLAND,%20Kings%201066-1603.htm#Eleanordied1372 '''ELEANOR 
2 CONC of Lancaster'''], daughter of HENRY Earl of Lancaster & his wife Matilda Chaworth ([1318]–Arundel Castle, Sussex 11 Jan 1372, bur Lewes Priory, Sussex).  While her first husband was still alive, and before Earl Richard's annulment
2 CONC  of his first marriage, she lived with her future second husband. She married secondly (Ditton Church, Stoke Poges, Bucks 5 Feb 1345, Papal dispensation 4 Mar 1345) as his second wife, Richard Fitzalan Earl of Arundel "Copped hat"
2 CONC . 
2 CONT * '''John & his wife had [one child]:'''
2 CONT ** a) '''HENRY Beaumont''' (Brabant [1339/40]–17 Jun 1368, bur Sempringham, Lincolnshire).  Lord Beaumont.  m as her first husband, '''MARGARET de Vere''', daughter of JOHN de Vere Earl of Oxford & his wife Matilda Badlesmere (-15
2 CONC  Jun 1398, bur Newgate Grey Friars). She married secondly Nicholas de Lorain of Penshurst, Kent. She married thirdly John Devereux, who was summoned to Parliament in 1384 whereby he is held to have become Lord Devereux. Henry & hi
2 CONC s wife had children: 
2 CONT *** i) '''JOHN Beaumont''' ([1359/60]–Stirling 9 Sep 1396, bur Sempringham). Lord Beaumont.  – see below.
2 CONT
2 CONT <nowiki>–––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––––</nowiki>
2 CONT
2 CONT John was invested as a Knight on 2 May 1338. He fought in the campaign in France in 1339. He succeeded to the title of 2nd Lord Beaumont on 10 March 1339/40.
2 CONT
