2 CONT ====Cracrofts Peerage: [http://www.cracroftspeerage.co.uk/beaumont1308.htm Beaumont, Baron (E, 1308/9)]
2 CONT *  '''Henry [de Beaumont], 1st Baron Beaumont later 1st Earl of Buchan'''
2 CONT * 2nd son of Louis of Brienne, called "of Acre", ''jure uxoris'' Vicomte of Beaumont (by his wife Agnes of Beaumont, dau. and eventual sole hrss. of Raoul, Vicomte of Beaumont), 2nd son of John of Brienne, King of Jerusalem 1210-2
2 CONC 9 and Emperor-Regent of Constantinople 1229-37, by his third wife Berengaria of Castile, 1st dau. of Alfonso IX, King of Leon 1188-1230, by his second wife Berengaria I, Queen of Castile 1217-46, through whom he was second cousin 
2 CONC to King Edward II
2 CONT * '''Mar.'''  bef. 14 Jul 1310 Alice Comyn (d. bef. 10 Aug 1349), niece and heir of line of John [Comyn], 3rd Earl of Buchan, and 1st dau. and hrss. of Sir Alexander Comyn (by his wife Joan le Latimer), 2nd son of Alexander [Comyn
2 CONC ], 2nd Earl of Buchan, by his wife Lady Elizabeth de Quincy, 2nd dau. of Roger [de Quincy], 2nd Earl of Winchester
2 CONT * '''Children'''
2 CONT ** '''1. John Beaumont, later 2nd Baron Beaumont
2 CONT ** 2. Richard Beaumont
2 CONT ** 3. John Beaumont
2 CONT ** 4. Thomas Beaumont, of Bolton Percy, co. York, mar., and had issue
2 CONT ** 1. Lady Elizabeth Beaumont (dsp. 27 Oct 1400; bur. in Hulton Abbey), mar. c. 1330 Nicholas [de Audley], 3rd Baron Audley of Heleigh
2 CONT ** 2. Lady Catherine Beaumont (d. 11 Nov 1368), mar. David of Strathbogie, 11th or 2nd Earl of Atholl, and had issue
2 CONT ** 3. Lady Isabel Beaumont (d. 1361), mar. c. 1335 Henry "of Grosmont", 1st Duke of Lancaster, and had issue
2 CONT ** 4. Lady Agnes Beaumont (d. after 1359), mar. about Jul 1343 as his second wife Thomas [de Lucy], 2nd Baron Lucy
2 CONT ** 5. Lady Joan Beaumont, mar. Fulk [FitzWarin], 3rd Baron FitzWarin, and had issue
2 CONT ** 6. Lady Beatrice Beaumont, mar. Count of Dammartin
2 CONT * '''Died:''' 10 Mar 1339/40
2 CONT * '''Created:''' by writ of summons 4 Mar 1308/9 Baron Beaumont – by writ of summons 22 Jan 1334 jure uxoris Earl of Buchan
2 CONT * '''Suc. by''' son
2 CONT * '''Note''': Joint Warden of Scotland 1308;  granted the Lordship of the Isle of Man 1310 for life;  fought on the side of King Edward II at the Battle of Boroughbridge 1321/2; Constable of England 1322;  supported Prince Edward 
2 CONC against his father, for which he was rewarded with a grant of Loughborough Castle 1334; Justiciar of Scotland 1338
2 CONT ** '''John [Beaumont], 2nd Baron Beaumont
2 CONT ** '''Born:'''  c. 1318
2 CONT ** '''Mar.''' bef. Jun 1337 Lady Eleanor Plantagenet (mar. (2) 1345 as his second wife Richard [FitzAlan], 10th or 3rd Earl of Arundel;  d. 11 Jan 1372; bur. at Lewes, co. Sussex), 5th dau. of Henry [Plantagenet], 3rd Earl of Lanc
2 CONC aster, by his wife Maud de Chaworth, dau. of Sir Patrick de Chaworth, of Kidwelly, co. Carmarthen, and Kempsford, co. Gloucester
2 CONT ** '''Only child''': Henry Beaumont, later 3rd Baron Beaumont
2 CONT ** '''Died'''    betw. 10 and 25 May 1342
2 CONT ** '''Suc. by''' son
2 CONT ** '''Note:''' Knighted 1338 and served in France 1339; neither he nor any of his successors were summoned to Parliament as Earl of Buchan
