1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =='''Isabel of Beaumont==
2 CONT '''Isabel de Beaumont, Duchess of Lancaster, of the House of Brienne (c. 1320 – 1361) was an English noblewoman, being the youngest daughter and child of Henry de Beaumont, Earl of Buchan and Alice Comyn.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Isabel was born in about 1320. She had nine older siblings, including John de Beaumont, 2nd Lord Beaumont. Isabel's paternal grandparents were Louis of Brienne, Viscount de Beaumont, and Agnes, Viscountess de Beaumont. Her mate
2 CONC rnal grandparents were Alexander Comyn, Sheriff of Aberdeen and Joan le Latimer.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''She married Henry of Grosmont, 1st Duke of Lancaster  in 1337. Isabel bore Henry two daughters who would eventually inherit their father's estates:
2 CONT **Maud, Countess of Leicester  (4 Apr 1339 – April 10, 1362), married William V, Count of Hainault. Died without surviving issue. 
2 CONT **Blanche, Countess of Lancaster  (25 March 1345 – September 12, 1369), married John of Gaunt , son of Edward III of England , by whom she had three surviving children. Blanche inherited all her father's estates after the death of
2 CONC  her sister. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Isabel died of the plague  in 1361 at Leicester Castle . She was buried in Newark Abbey, Leicester. Her husband also died of the plague in March 1361. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Through Blanche, '''Isabel was an ancestress of Englands's Royal House of Lancaster''' , with Henry IV of England  being '''her grandson'''. Philippa of Lancaster,  Queen consort of Portugal, was also '''her grandchild'''.
2 CONT
2 CONT From: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Isabel_de_Beaumont
2 CONT *_______________________
2 CONT *'''Isabel Beaumont1,2,3,4 
2 CONT *'''F, #16420, d. between 24 March 1361 and 6 July 1361
2 CONT *Father      Sir Henry Beaumont, Earl of Buchan & Moray, 1st Lord Beaumont, Constable of England & the Army, Justiciar of Scotland2,5,6,7 d. 10 Mar 1340
2 CONT *Mother     Alice Comyn8,2,5,6,7 d. 3 Jul 1349
2 CONT *'''     Isabel Beaumont married Sir Henry Plantagenet, 1st Duke & 4th Earl Lancaster, Derby, Lincoln, son of Sir Henry Plantagenet, Earl Lancaster & Leicester, Count of Provence, Lord of Monmouth and Maud de Chaworth, before 23 J
2 CONC une 1330; They had 3 daughters (Isabel, died young; Maud, wife of Sir Wilhelm, Duke of Bavaria; & Blanche, wife of Sir John 'of Gaunt', Earl of Derby, Lincoln, & Leicester).2,3,6,4 Isabel Beaumont died between 24 March 1361 and 6 
2 CONC July 1361.2,6
2 CONT *'''Family      Sir Henry Plantagenet, 1st Duke & 4th Earl Lancaster, Derby, Lincoln b. c 1309, d. 23 Mar 1361
2 CONT *Children
2 CONT **Maud Plantagenet9,2,6 b. 4 Apr 1335, d. 10 Apr 1362
2 CONT **Blanche Plantagenet+10,6 b. c 1341, d. 12 Sep 1369
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT * 1.[S4698] Unknown author, Lineage and Ancestry of HRH Prince Charles by Gerald Paget, Vol. I, p. 78.
2 CONT * 2.[S5] Douglas Richardson, Plantagenet Ancestry, p. 426-427.
2 CONT * 3.[S16] Douglas Richardson, Magna Carta Ancestry, 2nd Edition, Vol. I, p. 157.
2 CONT * 4.[S4] Douglas Richardson, Royal Ancestry, Vol. I, p. 309.
2 CONT * 5.[S16] Douglas Richardson, Magna Carta Ancestry, 2nd Edition, Vol. I, p. 154-155.
2 CONT * 6.[S16] Douglas Richardson, Magna Carta Ancestry, 2nd Edition, Vol. II, p. 529-530.
2 CONT * 7.[S4] Douglas Richardson, Royal Ancestry, Vol. I, p. 307-308.
2 CONT * 8.[S5] Douglas Richardson, Plantagenet Ancestry, p. 83.
2 CONT * 9.[S11575] The Lineage and Ancestry of H.R.H. Prince Charles, Prince of Wales, by Gerald Paget, Vol. I, p. 18.
2 CONT * 10.[S5] Douglas Richardson, Plantagenet Ancestry, p. 426-428.
2 CONT *From: http://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p547.htm#i16420
2 CONT *__________________
2 CONT *'''Isabella de Beaumont1 
2 CONT *'''F, #102142, b. circa 1320, d. 1361
2 CONT *Last Edited=23 May 2011
2 CONT *Consanguinity Index=0.02%
2 CONT *'''     Isabella de Beaumont was born circa 1320. She was the daughter of Henry Beaumont, 1st Earl of Buchan and Alice Comyn.2 She married Henry Grosmont of Derby Plantagenet, 1st Duke of Lancaster, son of Henry Plantagenet, 3rd 
2 CONC Earl of Lancaster and Matilda de Chaworth, circa 1337.2 She died in 1361 at Leicester, Leicestershire, England, the bubonic plague.1,3
2 CONT *'''Children of Isabella de Beaumont and Henry Grosmont of Derby Plantagenet, 1st Duke of Lancaster
2 CONT ** 1.Matilda Plantagenet, Countess of Leicester2 b. 4 Apr 1339, d. 10 Apr 1362
2 CONT ** 2.Blanche of Lancaster, Countess of Derby+2 b. 25 Mar 1345, d. 12 Sep 1369
2 CONT *Citations
2 CONT * 1.[S11] Alison Weir, Britain's Royal Families: The Complete Genealogy (London, U.K.: The Bodley Head, 1999), page 76. Hereinafter cited as Britain's Royal Families.
2 CONT * 2.[S8] Charles Mosley, editor, Burke's Peerage and Baronetage, 106th edition, 2 volumes (Crans, Switzerland: Burke's Peerage (Genealogical Books) Ltd, 1999), volume 1, page 228. Hereinafter cited as Burke's Peerage and Baronetag
2 CONC e, 106th edition.
2 CONT * 3.[S8] Charles Mosley, Burke's Peerage and Baronetage, 106th edition, volume 1, page 228, says after 23 Mar 1336.
2 CONT *From: http://www.thepeerage.com/p10215.htm#i102142
2 CONT *________________
2 CONT *'''Henry PLANTAGENET (1º D. Lancaster)
2 CONT *Died: 24 Mar 1360
2 CONT *Buried: Newark Church, Leicester, Leicestershire, England
2 CONT *Notes: Knight of the Garter. (Founder). Earl of Derby. Afterwards Duke of Lancaster. Served in the wars against the Scots, the Dutch, and French. Admiral of the Fleet and Steward of England.
2 CONT *Father: Henry PLANTAGENET (3º E. Lancaster)
2 CONT *Mother: Maud CHAWORTH
2 CONT *'''Married: Isabel BEAUMONT (dau. of Henry Beaumont and Alice Comyn)
2 CONT *Children:
2 CONT **1. Maud PLANTAGENET (C. Holland)
2 CONT **2. Blanche PLANTAGENET
2 CONT *From: http://www.tudorplace.com.ar/PLANTAGENET.htm#Henry PLANTAGENET (1º D. Lancaster)
2 CONT *____________
2 CONT *The Early House of Plantagenet (1154 - 1327)
2 CONT *   2a. Henry "of Lancaster", sum. to Parliament by writ 6 Feb 1298/9 as Baron Lancaster, restored as 3rd Earl of Leicester 1324 and 3rd Earl of Lancaster 1327, suc. yr. brother as Lord of Beaufort (b. c.1281; d. 22 Sep 1345), mar
2 CONC . (1) bef. 2 Mar 1297 Matilda de Chaworth (b. c. 1285; d. bef. 3 Dec 1322), dau. of Sir Patrick de Chaworth, of Kidwelly, co. Carmarthen, and Kempsford, co. Gloucester, by his wife Lady Isabella de Beauchamp, 1st dau. of William [
2 CONC de Beauchamp], 9th Earl of Warwick, and (2) aft. 1322 Alice de Joinville, widow of John, Seigneur of Arcis-sur-Aube and Chacenay, and dau. of John de Joinville, Seneschal of Champagne, by his wife Alice de Risnel, dau. of Gautier,
2 CONC  Seigneur de Risnel, and had issue by his first wife:
2 CONT **'''     1b. Henry "of Grosmont", 4th Earl of Lancaster and Leicester, cr. 16 Mar 1337 Earl of Derby, cr. 20 Aug 1349 Earl of Lincoln, cr. 6 Mar 1351 Duke of Lancaster, cr. 5 Apr 1359 Earl of Moray, Knight of the Garter 1348 (b. 
2 CONC c.1305; d. 23 Mar 1361), mar. c.1335 Lady Isabella de Beaumont (d. 1361), 4th dau. of Henry [de Beaumont], 1st Baron Beaumont and Earl of Buchan, by his wife Alice Comyn, dau. of Sir Alexander Comyn, and had issue:
2 CONT ***          1c. Lady Matilda Plantagenet, suo jure Countess of Leicester, Derby and Lincoln (b. 4 Apr 1340; dsp. 10 Apr 1362), mar. (1) 1 Nov 1344 Sir Ralph de Stafford, de jure 3rd Baron Audley (dvp. and sp. 1347), 1st son and h
2 CONC eir ap. by his second wife of Ralph [de Stafford], 1st Earl of Stafford, and (2) 1352 William V, Duke of Bavaria, Count of Holland, Hainault and Zeeland
2 CONT ***          2c. Lady Blanche Plantagenet, suo jure Countess of Lancaster (b. 25 Mar 1345; d. 12 Sep 1369), mar. 19 May 1359 as his first wife her third cousin John "of Gaunt", 1st Duke of Lancaster, 4th son of Edward III, King of
2 CONC  England, by his wife Philippa of Hainault, dau. of William V, Count of Holland and Hainault, and had issue.
2 CONT *From: http://www.cracroftspeerage.co.uk/online/
2 CONT *__________________
2 CONT *'''Historical Dictionary of the British Monarchy     By James Panton
2 CONT *http://books.google.com.br/books?id=BiyyueBTpaMC&pg=PA74&dq=Isabel+de+Beaumont,+Duchess+of+Lancaster&hl=pt-BR&sa=X&ei=K8zRU62LNcuwyASp0ILIBA&ved=0CCUQ6AEwAQ#v=onepage&q=Isabel%20de%20Beaumont%2C%20Duchess%20of%20Lancaster&f=false
2 CONT *Pg.74
2 CONT *BLANCHE, DUCHESS OF LANCASTER (1345-1369), As wife of John of Gaunt and mother of King Henry IV, Blanche (often known as Blanche of Lancster) had a considerable impact on the direction of English history despite her short lifespa
2 CONC n. She was born on 25 Mar 1345, the younger of two daughters in the family of '''Henry Grosmont, duke of Lancaster, and his wife, Isabella (or Isabel) de Beaumont. Lancaster died in 1361 (or, according to some sources, in 1360) le
2 CONC aving no heir, and his elder daughter''' (Matilda, or Maud) died in 1362 without any children, so Blanche inherited the vast family estates in northern England. These lands provided a power base for John of Gaunt, whom she had mar
2 CONC ried at Reading Abbey on 13 May 1359, and allowed him to maintain influential positions at the court of his father, King Edward III, and Edward's successor, Richard II.
2 CONT *   The marriage, although undoubtedly arranged for financial and political reasons ('''Henry Grosmont was one of King Edward's most senior advisors'''). was apparently a happy one, yielding three daughters and four sons. Four of 
2 CONC the children died before reaching adulthood, but Philippa (born in 1360) became queen consort of Portugal by marrying King John I; Elizabeth (born in 1363or 1364) married three times (one husband, John Holland, duke of Exeter, was
2 CONC  a half-brother of Richard II and remained loyal to him as other support dwindled); and Henry (born in 1366 or 1367) deposed King Richard in 1399. Blanche succembed to bugonic plague at Bolingbroke Castle, a Lancaster stronghold i
2 CONC n Lincolnshire, on 12 September 1369 and was interred in St. Paul's Cathedral, London. Thirty years later, her husband, who had taken two other wives, was buried beside her, but the locations of the graves are no longer known. See
2 CONC  also LANCASTER, HOUSE OF.
2 CONT *___________________________
2 CONT
2 CONT From 
2 CONT
2 CONT http://homepages.rootsweb.ancestry.com/~cousin/html/p425.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT Isabel de Beaumont1
2 CONT
2 CONT b. after 1311, d. 1361
2 CONT
2 CONT Father Henry, 1st Lord Beaumont1 b. circa 1270, d. 10 March 1340 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother Alice Comyn1 b. circa 1297, d. before 10 August 1349 
2 CONT
2 CONT      Isabel de Beaumont was daughter of Henry, Lord Beaumont, by Alice, suo jure Countess of Buchan.2 Also called Elizabeth.2 She died at blackdeath. She was born after 1311.1 She was the daughter of Henry, 1st Lord Beaumont and A
2 CONC lice Comyn.1 Isabel de Beaumont married Henry, "of Grosmont," Duke of Lancaster, son of Henry, styled "of Lancaster," 3rd Earl of Lancaster and Maud de Chaworth, between 1334 and 1337; 4th cousins.1,3 Isabel de Beaumont died in 13
2 CONC 61 at Leicester Castle, England. She died of the Black Death (bubonic plague).3 She married Nicholas, 3rd Lord Audley, son of James, 2nd Lord Audley and Joan de Mortimer, after 1361; Her 2nd.2 Black Death in England. Between 1361 
2 CONC and 1369. Isabel de Beaumont was buried in Newark Abbey, Leicester, England.3 
2 CONT
2 CONT Family 1 Henry, "of Grosmont," Duke of Lancaster b. between 1299 and 1314, d. 24 March 1360/61 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children Matilda, Countess of Leicester b. 4 Apr 1339, d. 10 Apr 13623
2 CONT
2 CONT Blanche, Baroness Lancaster+ b. 25 Mar 1345, d. 12 Sep 13694
2 CONT
2 CONT Family 2 Nicholas, 3rd Lord Audley b. circa 1332, d. July 1391 
2 CONT
