1 NAME Alain lll /de Beaufort-en-Plerguel/
2 GIVN Alain lll
2 _MARNM de Beaufort-en-Plerguel
2 NICK Alain de Beaufort
2 NICK sénéchal de Dol
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1200
2 PLAC France
2 ADDR
1 OCCU Sieur, de Beaufort
1 TITL Sir
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT From Lignages et châteaux de la baillie de Rennes avant la guerre de Succession (xie-xive siècles) by  Christophe Amio
2 CONT
2 CONT >The lineage of the Senechals of Dol ([https://books.openedition.org/pur/docannexe/image/141622/img-7.jpg genealogical table 7]) is established at the Château de Beaufort in Plerguer, on a steep site overlooking a deep valley. The
2 CONC  small quadrangular structure flanked by towers of which there are still some traces is preceded by a farmyard. This assimilation of the seneschals of Dol to the Beaufort lineage is made possible thanks to the investigation of the
2 CONC  bones of the Archbishop of Dol in 1226 81 . This lineage that can be traced from the last quarter of the xi th  century 82 , is originally from the abbey of Tronchet, between 1133 and 1147 83 . The last member, Alain de Beaufort,
2 CONC  becomes lord of part of the land of Dinan by alliance 84 . Died after 1247 85, he leaves only two daughters. The eldest, Clémence Dame de Dinan, married Alain d'Avaugour. The second brings the heritage land of Beaufort to Brient 
2 CONC de Châteaubriant, younger son of Geoffroy de Châteaubriant, and heir to the property of the elder branch of the du Guesclins. His descendants male preserve until the xvii th  century. Beaufort Castle appears to have been abandoned
2 CONC  in favor of Plessis-Bertrand at the union of the two lands in the middle of xiii th  century.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Havoise de Dinan''' (née vers 1200), dame héritière de Dinan-Nord, mariée en 1225 à Alain3 (1200 † après 1247), seigneur de Beaufort, et de Dinan-Nord, dont :
2 CONT * Clémence de Beaufort (vers 1230 † avant 1263), dame héritière de Dinan-Nord,  mariée vers 1246 à Alain II d'Avaugour (1224 † vers 1267), comte de Goëlo, seigneur de Dinan-Sud, 4e seigneur de Bécherel, seigneur de Mayenne et de L
2 CONC aigle,
2 CONT * Jeanne de Beaufort ( † après 1280), dame héritière de Beaufort, mariée en 1251 à Briand Ier de Châteaubriant-Beaufort ( † après 1301), seigneur de Beaufort, tige de la branche de Beaufort de la Famille de Châteaubriant,
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Origins 
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/brittcope.htm#HawiseDolMGeoffroyIIBoterel
2 CONT
2 CONT Alan & his wife had three children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT i)          JORDAN .  “Alani filii Jordani” confirmed the donation by his grandfather “Alan Flauudi” of the tithe of his demesne at Burton to Marmoutier, with the approval of his wife Johanna and son Jordan, by charter dated to th
2 CONC e reign of King Henry II[872].  m ---.  The name of Jordan’s wife is not known.  Jordan & his wife had one child: 
2 CONT
2 CONT (a)       ALAIN .  "Jodoinus de Dolo miles" confirmed donations made to le Tronchet by “Alanus filius Jordani senescallus Dolensis fundator” by charter dated Apr 1229[873]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References
2 CONT * http://data0.eklablog.com/lanvallayhistoire/mod_article6047440_4.doc fils d’alan fitzjordan sénéchal de dol
2 CONT *Lignages et châteaux de la baillie de Rennes avant la guerre de Succession (xie-xive siècles).  Christophe Amio https://books.openedition.org/pur/141622?lang=en
