1 NOTE When John duke of Brittany died in 1341 he left as his heir Jeanne de Penthievre and his half brother Jean comte de Montfort, who battled over Brittany.  Jeanne's husband, Charles of Blois led her battle, until he was captured in 
2 CONC 1346 and held by the English.  Nine years a prisoner, he was ransomed, and then renewed the struggle for his wife's claim and eventually killed in battle.
