2 CONC ter dated 1204[956].  The Scripta de Feodis of King Philippe II record “Johans sires de Neele” holding “Neele et les apartenances...” and name among his “home...Raous mis frères...”[957].  Seigneur de Falvy.  m ([1212/14]) as her 
2 CONC second husband, [https://www.geni.com/people/Ade%CC%80le-de-Roye/6000000000112112364?through=6000000000112131470#/tab/overview ALIX de Roye], widow of [https://www.geni.com/people/Jean-d-Alen%C3%A7on/6000000009305095491?through=60
2 CONC 00000000112112364 JEAN [III] Comte d'Alençon], daughter of [https://www.geni.com/people/Barthe%CC%81lemy-de-Roye-Chamberlain-Of-France/6000000000112088890?through=6000000000112112364 BARTHELEMY de Roye] & his wife [https://www.gen
2 CONC i.com/people/Perronelle-de-Montfort/6000000000112086823?through=6000000000112088890 Petronille de Montfort] (-26 Jan 1226).  A manuscript genealogy of the Lords of Beaumont records that “Joannem”, son of “Robertum comitem Alenchei
2 CONC i”, married “Aaliz filiam domini Bartholomæi de Roye” but died childless[958].  Her second marriage is confirmed by the necrology of Joyenval which records the death of [her son] "domini Joannis de Nigella filii dominæ Aelidis de 
2 CONC Roya” and his donation which was confirmed by his mother[959].  The necrology of Joyenval records the death “26 Jan“ 1226 of "dominæ Alidiæ de Roya filiæ domini Bartholomæi fundatoris” and the donation of revenue from “teloneum su
2 CONC um de Roya, detentum nunc a domino de Mouy”[960].  Raoul & his wife had one child: 
2 CONT >*1.         [https://www.geni.com/people/Jean-III-de-Nesle-seigneur-de-Falvy/6000000000112088056?through=6000000000112112364 JEAN] [I] de Nesle (-2 Dec 1292).  Seigneur de Falvy et de la Hérelle. 
2 CONT
