1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''RAOUL de Roye .  Goethals records his parentage without citing the source which confirms the information[894].  Seigneur de la Ferté en Ponthieu, de iure uxoris[895].  m MARIE de Ville, daughter of ---.  Père An
2 CONC selme names her as the wife of Raoul de Roye but cites no primary source[896].  Goethals says that her father was “seigneur de Ville-sur-Illon” without citing the source which confirms the information[897].  Raoul & his wife had t
2 CONC wo children:''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT >*i)          MATHIEU [I] de Roye (-after Jul 1280).  Seigneur de la Ferté en Ponthieu.  m as her first husband, JEANNE de Vendeuil, daughter of CLAREMBAUD Seigneur de Vendeuil & his wife --- (-after 1319).  She married secondly J
2 CONC ean [III] de Nesle Seigneur de Falvy.  “Mathieu de Roye chevalier Seigneur de la Ferté et de Vendeuil et…Jeanne sa femme dame de Vendeuil” settled a dispute with the convent of Saint-Nicolas or Bos in the bishopric of Laon concern
2 CONC ing rights over “Choegny” by charter dated Jul 1280 which names “messire Huon de Vendeuil et messire Clerembaut”[898].  A document dated 1310 records a settlement between “domicellam Margaretam de Pinquigniaco” and “Ioannam de Ven
2 CONC dolio relictam defuncti Mathei de Roya militis”, which names “defuncti Mathei de Roya iunioris filii procreati ex eis...domicellæ Mariæ filiæ dictæ Ioannæ et dicti defuncti Mathei quondam mariti eiusdem”[899].  Her second marriage
2 CONC  is confirmed by the charter dated May 1324 which named “Jeanne jadis Dame de Vendeuil mere Jehan de Fallevi chevalier hoir à present de ladite Dame” and required “[le]dit Iehan de Fallevi” to make payments to “Marie de la Freté s
2 CONC a suer et au Seigneur de Loques son mary”[900].  Mathieu & his wife had two children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT >*ii)         MARIE de Roye (-13 Mar -).  The executors of “domini Auberti de Hangesto” claimed against “comitem Vindocinensem” for “dotalicio comitisse uxoris sue” dated 1260[908].  Her third marriage is confirmed by the necrolog
2 CONC y of Saint-Nicolas de Courville which records the death “V Non Mai“ of "dominus Johannes de Veteriponte miles junior” and his donation for the anniversaries of “patris et matris eiusdem necnon et domini Yvonis condam fratris sui” 
2 CONC made “Curveville in castello...in presencia nobilis domine domine de Vindocino domine de Curvavilla uxoris eiusdem...anno LXXI die mercurii post Concepcionem beate Marie Virginis” [1270/71][909].  A charter dated 1272 records a ju
2 CONC dgment against “B. comitem Vindocinensem” and after his death “dominam Mariam comitissam Vindocinensem, ratione liberorum suorum” relating to the capture of four men in the land of Sentier priory[910].  The necrology of Vendôme La
2 CONC  Trinité records the death "V Non Mar" of "Maria comitissa"[911].  The necrology of Saint-Nicolas de Courville records the death “III Id Mar“ of "Marie domine de Curveville condam comitisse Vindocinensis et matris Yvonis domini Cu
2 CONC rveville militis” and the donation for whom of “annui redditus super preposituram Curveville, ad festum beati Remigii”[912].  m firstly AUBERT [IV] de Hangest Seigneur de Genlis, son of [AUBERT [III] Seigneur de Genlis & his wife 
2 CONC Beatrix de Châtillon] (-before 1259).  m secondly ([before 1259]) BOUCHARD [VIII] Comte de Vendôme, son of PIERRE Comte de Vendôme & his wife Jeanne de Mayenne (-[15 May 1271], bur St Georges de Vendôme).  m thirdly ([15 May/9 Dec
2 CONC ] 1271) JEAN de Vieuxpont Seigneur de Courville, son of ROBERT de Vieuxpont Seigneur de Courville & his wife Isabelle de Maillebois (-3 May ----).
2 CONT
2 CONT https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/nfravalver.htm#MathieuRoyediedafter1350B
