1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Georges_de_la_Tr%C3%A9moille
2 CONT
2 CONT Georges de la Trémoille (c. 1382 – 6 May 1446) was count of de Guînes from 1398 to 1446 and Grand Chamberlain of France to King Charles VII of France. He sought reconciliation between Philip, Duke of Burgundy and Charles VII durin
2 CONC g their estrangement in the latter part of the Hundred Years' War. La Trémoille was a political opponent of Joan of Arc and Arthur de Richemont within the French court. Most historians take a poor view of his career, assessing tha
2 CONC t he placed personal advancement before the public interest.
2 CONT
2 CONT La Tremoille was captured at Agincourt in 1415. He regained his freedom shortly afterward and dedicated the rest of his career to court life and diplomacy. He made an advantageous marriage to Joan II of Auvergne (1378–1424), count
2 CONC ess of Auvergne and Boulogne (1404–1424). La Trémoille served the Burgundian court for several years, then joined the Armagnac court of Charles VII.
2 CONT
2 CONT La Trémoille became a royal favourite in 1427. He gained the title of grand chamberlain and was instrumental in constable de Richemont's expulsion from the court that same year. Following Joan of Arc's successful campaign to Rheim
2 CONC s for the coronation of Charles VII, la Trémoille delayed a march on Paris with fruitless peace negotiations. He may have been responsible for the lack of royal support that doomed her military actions thereafter. The historical c
2 CONC onsensus is that personal jealousies led him to undermine France's two best military commanders during a low point in the war. In September 1432 he paid for Rodrigo de Villandrando and his routiers to hold Les Ponts-de-Cé against 
2 CONC the assaults of Jean de Bueil. That year de Richemont returned to court and imprisoned la Trémoille the following year. Charles VII did not intervene.
2 CONT
2 CONT The family of Georges de LA TREMOUILLE and .. [129126] LA TREMOUILLE (de), Georges (Guy VI & Marie de SULLY [129127])
2 CONT * married about 1410, from .. (France) .., .. (..)
2 CONT       1) Marguerite ou Marie, died 1457-12, married Sully (France, place to identify) 1441 Jean de SALAZAR
2 CONT
