1 OCCU Comte de Dreux, Vicomte de Tartas, Seigneur d'Albret
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Charles_II_d%27Albret
2 CONT
2 CONT Charles II d'Albret (died 1471) was a French magnate, administrator, and soldier.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the son of Charles d'Albret and Marie de Sully. His father died in 1415 at the Battle of Agincourt, leaving the younger Charles as lord of Albret and titular Count of Dreux, titular count since after Agincourt the lands of 
2 CONC the county of Dreux were in English hands. As a member of the Armagnac faction, Charles was a supporter of the Dauphin Charles, future Charles VII of France.
2 CONT
2 CONT His links to the Armagnacs were strengthened by his marriage in 1417 to Anne of Armagnac, daughter of Bernard VII, Count of Armagnac and Bonne of Berry, from whom the faction took its name.
2 CONT
2 CONT Charles served on the royal council of Dauphin Charles and in 1427 joined with Richemont and Yolande of Aragon in removing the Dauphin's unpopular favourite Pierre de Giac. De Giac was soon afterwards executed by drowning. He took
2 CONC  part in the campaigns of Joan of Arc, and was named lieutenant of the province of Berry. He was confirmed in possession of the county of Dreux in 1441 by King Charles VII.
2 CONT
2 CONT On his death Albret passed to his grandson Alain (called Alain the Great), Jean's son, but he left the county of Dreux to his third son, Arnaud Amanieu. Alain, however, seized control of the county. His fourth son, Charles, was ex
2 CONC ecuted for treason in 1472.
2 CONT
2 CONT Charles and Anne had seven children;
2 CONT
2 CONT Jean d'Albret(1420–1468)
2 CONT
2 CONT Louis d'Albret,Cardinal(1422–1465)
2 CONT
2 CONT Arnaud Amanieu d'Albret, d.1463
2 CONT
2 CONT Charles d'Albret, d.1473
2 CONT
2 CONT Gilles d'Albret, d.1479
2 CONT
2 CONT Marie d'Albret, d.1486
2 CONT
2 CONT Jeanne d'Albret, d.1444
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT contrat de mariage entre Anne d'Armagnac &  Charles d'Albret le 23 août 1418
