2 CONT Raoul Paynel, known as Tesson, his mother's patronymic which will be carried by all his descendants in the male line. The names of the father and mother of Raoul Paynel, who became Tesson, can be found in Polonovski Jacques and Le
2 CONC portier Paul and in the Complements: he is the son of Guillaume Paynel, lord of Grippon and Subligny, married in 1214 to Pétronille Tesson, lady of Percy and of La Roche-Tesson. He took his mother's name and was probably lord of S
2 CONC ubligny and la Roche-Tesson. His ancestry can be found in Polonovski Jacques and Leportier Paul. Anselmne names the husband of Petronille de Montfort "Raoul de la Roche-Tesson". Sources: Note: Polonovski Jacques and Leportier Paul
2 CONC  "La famille Paynel" Revue généalogique normande n'47, July-September 1993, p.256-259; p.257. Père Anselme Histoire généalogique et chronologique de la Maison royale de France..., continuée par M. Du Fourny, Paris (France), third 
2 CONC edition revised, corrected and enlarged by P. Ange and P. Simplicien, Augustins Déchaussés, 1726-1733, 9 volumes
2 CONT
