2 CONT  (-1212).  The Chronicon Savigniacensis Monasterii records the death "XVIII Kal Jul" in 1212 of "Gaufridus dominus Filgeriarum, filius Willelmi et Agathæ, filiæ Willelmi de Humeto"[1160].  He succeeded his grandfather in 1196 as S
2 CONC eigneur de Fougères.  m MATHILDE de Porhoët, daughter of EUDES Vicomte de Porhoët & his wife ---.  The primary source which confirms her parentage and marriage has not yet been identified.  She succeeded her father as Vicomtesse d
2 CONC e Porhoët.  Geoffroy & his wife had one child:  
2 CONT
2 CONT a)         RAOUL [III] de Fougères (-24 Feb 1256, bur Sauvigny).  His parentage is confirmed by his burial entry (see below).  He succeeded his father in 1212 as Seigneur de Fougères.  “Fulco Paganelli” gave security to Louis IX K
2 CONC ing of France on behalf of “Radulpho de Filgeriis nepoti meo” relating to “terram suam in Normannia” by charter dated Mar [1230/31][1161].  The Chronicon Savigniacense records the death "VI Kal Mar" in 1256 of "Radulphus Dominus F
2 CONC ilgeriarum filius Gaufridi Domini Filgeriarum" and his burial at Sauvigny[1162].  m ISABELLE de Craon, daughter of AMAURY [I] Sire de Craon & his wife Jeanne de Roche.  "Radulfum Fulgerium…et nobilis domina de Sabolio et Credone" 
2 CONC agreed the marriage of "dom. Fulgeriarum" and "Isabella filia bonæ memoriæ Amauritii quondam domini Credonii" by charter dated Feb 1233[1163].  Her name is confirmed by the Chronicon Savigniacense which records the birth of "Isabe
2 CONC lla uxorelicti Radulphi filium Iohannem" in 1230[1164].  Raoul [III] & his wife had two children:  
2 CONT
2 CONT i)          JEAN de Fougères (6 Dec 1230-6 Dec 1230).  The Chronicon Savigniacense records the birth "die sancti Nicolai" in 1230 of "Isabella uxorelicti Radulphi filium Iohannem" and his death the same day[1165].  
2 CONT
2 CONT ii)         JEANNE de Fougères (-after 1273, bur Sauvigny).  The Chronicon Savigniacense records the marriage "IV Kal Feb" in 1253 of "Hugues Comes Marchiæ" and "Iohannam unicam filiam Radulfi Domini Filgeriarum in dicto castro"[1
2 CONC 166].  Dame de Fougères.  m (Fougères 29 Jan 1254) HUGUES [XIII] Sire de Lusignan Comte de la Marche et d’Angoulême, son of HUGUES [XII] "le Brun" Sire de Lusignan, Comte de la Marche et d'Angoulême & his wife Yolande de Bretagne 
2 CONC (-shortly after 25 Aug 1270).  Sire de Fougères, by right of his wife.
2 CONT From Wikipedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Geoffrey of Fougères (died 1212) was Baron of Fougères from 1196 to 1212 .
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT Geoffroy is the son of Guillaume de Fougère († 1187), himself the son and pre-deceased heir of Raoul  II de Fougères . His mother Agathe du Hommet, from a great Norman family, having remarried with Foulque Paynel on the death of h
2 CONC is grandfather, the guardianship of the young child is entrusted to his great-uncle Guillaume dit L'Angevin (around 1130 - diedDecember 20, 1212), Lord of Coglès, brother of Raoul  II and the only surviving male of the lineage of 
2 CONC governing age 1 .
2 CONT
2 CONT Geoffroy had a lot of trouble freeing himself from William's guardianship. In order to be able to emancipate himself and marry a rich heiress, the eldest daughter of the Viscount of Porhoët, Geoffroy had to give up part of his est
2 CONC ates to his great-uncle. In 1204, William obtained a third of the land of Fougères in usufruct with the right to dispose of it in full ownership as well as the family property located in England. Having become a man, Geoffroy marr
2 CONC ied Mahaut, one of the daughters and co-heiresses of Eudon  III of Porhoët, transferring the expectation of part of the property of the rich house of Porhoët into his patrimony. The Baron of Fougères died in 1212 while still young
2 CONC  and was buried in the cloister of the Abbey of Savigny . His only son Raoul  III of Fougères succeeded him 2 .
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes and references
2 CONT Frédéric Morvan , The Breton Knights. Between Plantagenets and Captets from the middle of the 12th to the middle of the  13th century , Rennes , Presses Universitaires de Rennes, 2009, 293  p. ( ISBN  978-2-7535-0827-9 ) , p.  272
2 CONC  ??Genealogy of Fougères
2 CONT Abbot Amédée Guillotin de Corson , The Lordships of Upper Brittany , Paris, The Book of History, 1999, 463  pp. ( ISBN  2-84435-030-5 ) , p.  189
