1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/BRITTANY.htm#ConstanceBretagnedied1148 '''From Melands:''']
2 CONT
2 CONT c) ['''CONSTANCE de Bretagne''' (-1148). Constance is shown in ''Europäische Stammtafeln'' as the younger daughter of Duke Conan III, died 1148[239]. The primary source which confirms her parentage and marriage has not yet been id
2 CONC entified. The information has not therefore been verified. '''m''' as his first wife, [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/BRITTANY.htm#ConstanceBretagnedied1148 '''GEOFFROY de Mayenne'''], son of JUHEL Seigneur de Mayenne & his wife 
2 CONC Clémence de Ponthieu (-18 Feb or 25 Jul 1169).]
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/BRITTANY.htm#ConstanceDssBretagnedied1201 See also] 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''The following is questionable and needs to be either confirmed or removed:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Constance Princess Of was born about 1118 in , Bretagne, Indre, France and her baptism took place in Dsp.  Constance Princess Of's father was Conan III "le Gross" Duke Of BRETAGNE and her mother is Maud, Princess Of ENGLAND.  Her 
2 CONC paternal grandparents are Alan IV FERGENT and Hermengarde Countess Of BRETAGNE; her maternal grandfather was Henry I "Beauclerc" King Of ENGLAND and her maternal grandmother is Mrs-Henry I, Concubine Of ENGLAND. She had a brother 
2 CONC and two sisters, named Hoel IV Count Of, Berthe De and Bertha Princess Of.  She died in Sp.
2 CONT
2 CONT Constance de Bretagne (Maud FitzRoy of England , Henry I "Beauclerc" of , William I the Conqueror of ) was born about 1114 in Bretagne, Indre, France.
2 CONT
2 CONT Constance married Alan la Zouche about 1123. Alan was born about 1093 in Rohan, Brittany, France.
2 CONT
2 CONT They had the following children:www.celtic-casimir.com
2 CONT
2 CONT Constance DE BRETAGNE
2 CONT 	Died: 1148
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage Information:
2 CONT Constance married Geoffroy IV DE MAYENNE Sire de Mayenne, son of Juhel I DE MAYENNE and Clemence DE MONTGOMERY. (Geoffroy IV DE MAYENNE Sire de Mayenne was born about 1133 and died on 18 Feb 1170.)
2 CONT
