2 CONT
2 CONT  Sherriff of Devonshire Roger la Zouche   
2 CONT
2 CONT Roger was born about 1185 in Molton, Devonshire, England.1   Roger's father was Earl of Brittany Alan la Zouche and his mother was Alice de Belmeis.  His paternal grandparents were Geoffrey la Zouche and Hawise of Brittany. He had
2 CONC  two brothers named William and Philip.  He was the youngest of the three children.  He died on May 14th, 1238 in North Melton, Devonshire, England.2 
2 CONT
2 CONT  Sherriff of Devonshire Roger la Zouche & Margaret de Beaumont 
2 CONT
2 CONT They had two sons and three daughters, named William, Alan, Eon, Loretta and Alice.
2 CONT
2 CONT Personal Details
2 CONT
2 CONT  Sherriff of Devonshire Roger la Zouche
2 CONT
2 CONT Roger was born about 1185 in Molton, Devonshire, England.1   He died on May 14th, 1238 in North Melton, Devonshire, England.2 
2 CONT
2 CONT  Margaret de Beaumont
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret was born in 1154 in Hampshire, England.3   She died at the age of 81 on January 12th, 1235.4 
2 CONT
2 CONT Death Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT Children
2 CONT
2 CONT   Eon la Zouche
2 CONT
2 CONT Eon was born about 1207.5 
2 CONT
2 CONT   William la Zouche
2 CONT
2 CONT William was born about 1209.5 
2 CONT
2 CONT   Loretta la Zouche
2 CONT
2 CONT Loretta was born about 1211 in North Melton, Devonshire, England.6   She died after 1273.7 
2 CONT
2 CONT   Alice la Zouche
2 CONT
2 CONT Alice was born in 1213.5 
2 CONT
2 CONT   Sir Alan la Zouche
2 CONT
2 CONT Alan was born in 1217.1   He died at the age of 53 on August 10th, 1270.1 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Roger la Zouche, Sheriff of Devonshire, was a younger brother of William--and was his heir in 1199.
2 CONT
2 CONT Roger married Margaret (?) before 1203. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was Sheriff of Devonshire between 1228 and 1231.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a witness to Henry III's confirmation of the Magna Charta.
2 CONT
2 CONT He died before 14 May 1238.
2 CONT
2 CONT Roger was our ancestor through two distinct descent lines--through his son Eudo and through his son Alan, each of whom was independently our ancestor.
2 CONT
