2 CONT
2 CONT '''MATHILDE de Blois.''' [1133/34]-before 1141, bur Priory of Holy Trinity, [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/St_Botolph_without_Aldgate Aldgate Without], London).  Daughter of King Stephen, Orderic Vitalis records her betrothal when
2 CONC  she was "two years old" but does not name her[303].  The Chronicon Valassense names "comes Mellenti Gualerannus" and "uxore sua regis Stephani familia"[304].  William of Newburgh records her burial, together with that of her brot
2 CONC her Baudouin, as "children of King Stephen and Queen" and wife of "comitis de Medlint", quoting the records of Holy Trinity[305].  King Stephen donated property to Holy Trinity Priory, London, for the souls of "Mathildis filie mee
2 CONC  et Bald[wini] filii mei", by charter dated to [1139/46][306].  Betrothed (Easter 1136303) WALERAN de Beaumont Comte de Meulan, son of ROBERT de Beaumont Comte de Meulan, Earl of Leicester & his second wife Elisabeth de Vermandois
2 CONC  (1104-Préaux 9/10 Apr 1166 bur Préaux).  
2 CONT
