2 NOTE This image is a portrait of Catherine de' Medici (1519–1589), the Queen of France. She was a highly influential figure in the 16th century, serving as queen consort to King Henry II and later as queen mother and regent for three o
3 CONC f her sons: Francis II, Charles IX, and Henry III. 
3 CONT
3 CONT Wikimedia Commons
3 CONT  +2
3 CONT Key Facts About Catherine de' Medici
3 CONT Powerful Regent: Between 1559 and roughly 1576, she was arguably the most powerful woman in France and possibly all of Europe.
3 CONT Italian Roots: Born into the prominent Medici family of Florence, she was the daughter of Lorenzo de' Medici.
3 CONT Artistic Legacy: The original portrait of her seen in the image is attributed to the court painter François Clouet.
3 CONT Historical Reputation: She is often remembered for her involvement in the political and religious turmoil of her time, including the French Wars of Religion. 
3 CONT
3 CONT World History Encyclopedia
3 CONT  +3
