2 NOTE This image is a portrait of Françoise d'Aubigné, Marquise de Maintenon (1635–1719), who was the second wife of King Louis XIV of France.Known as Madame de Maintenon, she had a remarkable rise from an impoverished background to one
3 CONC  of the most powerful positions in the French court.Key Facts About Madame de MaintenonEarly Life & First Marriage: Born into a family with little means, she first entered high society as the wife of the poet Paul Scarron, during 
3 CONC which time she was known as Madame Scarron.Royal Governess: After her first husband's death, she was appointed as the governess for the illegitimate children of King Louis XIV and his mistress, Madame de Montespan.Marriage to the 
3 CONC King: Following the death of Queen Marie-Thérèse, she married Louis XIV in a private, secret ceremony around 1683. While never officially recognized as Queen, she held significant political and social influence at Versailles.Legac
3 CONC y: In 1686, she founded the Maison royale de Saint-Louis, a pioneering school for girls from impoverished noble families.
