1 OCCU was one of Henry I's favorite mistresses., 15th Concubine of Henry I
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Do not confuse with her neice, Isabella (Elizabeth) de Beaumont, who married  Simon De Saint Liz, Gervase Paynel, and, William.  
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Henry_I_of_England#With_Isabel_de_Beaumont]
2 CONT
2 CONT Isabel (Elizabeth) de Beaumont (after 1102 – after 1172), daughter of Robert de Beaumont, sister of Robert de Beaumont, 2nd Earl of Leicester. She married Gilbert de Clare, 1st Earl of Pembroke, in 1130. She was also known as Isab
2 CONC ella de Meulan.
2 CONT
2 CONT Illegitimate children with Henry I:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1) Isabel Hedwig of England 
2 CONT
2 CONT 2) Matilda FitzRoy, abbess of Montvilliers, also known as Montpiller 
2 CONT
2 CONT ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
2 CONT
2 CONT  [http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/ENGLISH%20NOBILITY%20MEDIEVAL1.htm '''Gilbert de Clare from Medlands''']
2 CONT
2 CONT GILBERT de Clare "Strongbow", son of GILBERT FitzRichard de Clare & his wife Adelisa de Clermont ([1100][1032]-6 Jan 1148 or 1149, bur Tintern Abbey).  “Adeliz, uxor Gilberti filii Ricardi, et Gillebertus et Walterus et Baldewinus
2 CONC  et Rohaisia pueri Gilberti” donated property to Thorney Monastery, by undated charter witnessed by “Gilberto filio Gilberti, Galterio, Hervæo, Baldwino fratribus eius et Rohaisia sorore eorum”[1033].  Guillaume de Jumièges names 
2 CONC (in order) "Richard…Gilbert et Gautier" as the three sons of Gilbert[1034].  He inherited the estates of his paternal uncles Roger de Clare (after 1131, in the baronies of Bienfaite and Orbec, Normandy) and Walter de Clare (in 113
2 CONC 8, as lord of Nether Gwent with the castle of Strigoil, later known as Chepstow)[1035].  He was created Earl of Pembroke in 1138 by King Stephen.  The Annales Cambriæ record the death in 1149 of "Gilbertus comes, qui Strangboga di
2 CONC ctus est"[1036].  
2 CONT
2 CONT m ISABEL de Beaumont, daughter of ROBERT de Beaumont-le-Roger Comte de Meulan [Earl of Leicester] & his wife Isabelle de Vermandois ([1102/07]-after 1172), previously mistress of Henry I King of England.  Guillaume de Jumièges nam
2 CONC es "la sœur de Galeran comte de Meulan…Elisabeth" as wife of Gilbert[1037].  Henry II King of England confirmed the donations to the nuns of Saint-Saens by "Isabel comitissa qui fuit uxor Gilleberti comitis" by charter dated to [1
2 CONC 172/1182][1038].  “Badero de Momuta et uxor sua Rohes” donated revenue in Monmouth to Monmouth Priory by undated charter witnessed by "Galterus frater Gilleberti consulis, qui ipsa die loco consulis uxorem meam michi dedit…comitis
2 CONC sa Ysabel, Robertus filius Baderonis, Johannes filius Roberti, Thomas filius Pagani…"[1039].  
2 CONT
2 CONT Earl Gilbert & his wife had two children
2 CONT
2 CONT ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
2 CONT
2 CONT Strongbow's mother was Isabel (Elizabeth) de Beaumont, sister to Robert earl of Leicester and Waleran count of Meulan. Isabel had been the youngest mistress of King Henry I, and their liaison resulted in a natural daughter, Isabel
2 CONC  (Elizabeth), born c.1129/30. When Isabel de Beaumont married Gilbert in 1130, she took this daughter with her. Strongbow was born before the end of 1130; thus he was raised with the natural half-sister of the Empress Matilda,
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Robert de Beaumont, 1st Earl of Leicester''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''From Wikipedia''', the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1096 Robert de Beaumont, 1st Earl of Leicester married (Isabel) Elizabeth de Vermandois, daughter of Hugh Magnus and a scion of the French royal family. Their children were: 
2 CONT
2 CONT Emma de Beaumont (born 1102) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert de Beaumont, 2nd Earl of Leicester (born 1104) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Waleran IV de Beaumont, Count of Meulan (born 1104) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Hugh de Beaumont, 1st Earl of Bedford (born c. 1106) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Adeline de Beaumont, married two times: 
2 CONT
2 CONT Hugh IV of Montfort-sur-Risle; 
2 CONT
2 CONT Richard de Granville of Bideford (d. 1147) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Aubree de Beaumont, married Hugh II of Château-neuf-Thimerais. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Maud de Beaumont, married William Lovel. (b. c. 1102) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Isabel de Beaumont, a mistress of King Henry I of England. Married two times: 
2 CONT
2 CONT Gilbert de Clare, 1st Earl of Pembroke; 
2 CONT
2 CONT Hervé de Montmorency, Constable of Ireland
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT http://thepeerage.com/p10466.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT  Isabella of Meulan was born between 1102 and 1107.1 She was the daughter of Robert de Meulan, 1st Earl of Leicester and Elizabeth de Vermandois.2 She married Gilbert de Clare, 1st Earl of Pembroke, son of Gilbert fitz Richard and
2 CONC  Adeliza de Clermont. She died after 1172.2
2 CONT
2 CONT      As a result of her marriage, Isabella of Meulan was styled as Countess of Pembroke.1
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Isabella of Meulan and Henry I 'Beauclerc', King of England
2 CONT
2 CONT Matilda of Montvilliers2
2 CONT
2 CONT Isabella (?)2 b. c 1120
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Isabella of Meulan and Gilbert de Clare, 1st Earl of Pembroke
2 CONT
2 CONT Basilea de Clare2
2 CONT
2 CONT Richard FitzGilbert de Clare, 2nd Earl of Pembroke+2 b. c 1130, d. 20 Apr 1176
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT
