1 NOTE
2 CONT It is unclear without further research just what Isabel's birth date is. I have seen it as late as 1110. Also, it is unclear whether her mother was Elizabeth Vermandois or Amice de Montfort. I am leaving this as is for the time be
2 CONC ing. I think, though, that somebody confused Robert the first earl with Robert the second earl, as the sources seem to be virtually unanimous that the second earl had a wife named Amice de Montfort.
2 CONT
2 CONT Isabel was either a wife or (more likely) a concubine of Henry I "Beauclerc". It is well attested that Isabel Hedwig was their daughter. Many sources also list Maud; so I have put these two on this family card. A few sources also 
2 CONC list Constance Maud, Vicomtesse de Maine, b. 1128, as their daughter. I have added her to the family, as she is a Motteler ancestor. Henry I's other children are Stanford ancestors.
