1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Hugh de Bedford'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===From Medlands:===
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/NORMAN%20NOBILITY.htm#Walerandied1166A
2 CONT
2 CONT "Hugo pauper" (-after 1140).  His parentage is recorded by Orderic Vitalis[2291].  A favourite of King Stephen who gave him the castle and barony of Bedford in 1138, thereby creating him Earl of Bedford.  The Gesta Stephani Regis 
2 CONC records that "Hugo cognomina Pauper", who was granted "comitatum Bedefordiæ" after the expulsion of "Milone de Bellocampo", lost the castle, dated to [1140/41][2292].  He left England whereupon his earldom reverted to the crown[22
2 CONC 93].  He was ejected from Bedford by the sons of Robert Beauchamp.  He appears to have lapsed into poverty and was probably degraded from his peerage[2294].  m --- de Beauchamp, daughter of SIMON de Beauchamp & his wife ---.  Orde
2 CONC ric Vitalis records that "Hugoni cognomento Pauperi" married "filiam Simonis de Bello Campo"[2295].  Hugh & his wife had one child:  
2 CONT
2 CONT a)         HUGH of Bedford .  The primary source which confirms his parentage has not yet been identified.  m AMICIE de l'Isle, daughter of ---.  The primary source which confirms her parentage and marriage has not yet been identi
2 CONC fied.  Hugh & his wife had one child:  
2 CONT
2 CONT i)          ABEL of Bedford .  The primary source which confirms his parentage has not yet been identified.  
