1 NOTE {geni:about_me} HENRI II Duke of Brabant.   (c1207-Louvain 1/2 Feb 1248, bur Villers). 
2 CONT s/o  HENRI I "le Guerroyeur" Duke of Brabant & Mathilde de Flandre 
2 CONT x <22 Aug 1215 MARIA von Staufen, d/o PHILIPP King of Germany Duke of Swabia & Maria née Eirene Angelina of Byzantium ([1199/1200]-Louvain before 1235). 
2 CONT 1.         MATHILDE de Brabant (1224-29 Sep 1288, bur Abbey of Cercamp, Artois).  
2 CONT 2.         BEATRIX de Brabant (1225-11 Nov 1288, bur Abbaye de Marquette, near Lille). 
2 CONT 3.         HENRI de Brabant (-Louvain 28 Feb or 1 Mar 1261, bur Leeuwen Dominican 
2 CONT 4.         MARIE de Brabant (-beheaded Donauwörth 18 Jan 1256, bur Donauwörth Heilige Kreuz-Stift). 
2 CONT 5.         MARGUERITE de Brabant (-[4 Jun] 1277)
2 CONT 6.         PHILIPPE de Brabant (-young, bur Leeuwen St Pieter).  
2 CONT xx  (1241) SOPHIE von Thüringen, d/o LUDWIG IV "der Heilige" Landgraf of Thuringia & Erszébet of Hungary (Wartburg 20 Mar 1224-[Marburg] 29 May 1275, bur Villers).
2 CONT 1. ELISABETH de Brabant (1243-17 Apr or 9 Oct 1261, bur Braunschweig)
2 CONT 2. HENRI de Brabant (24 Jun 1244-Marburg 21 Dec 1308, bur Marburg Elisabethkirche)
2 CONT https://fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/BRABANT,%20LOUVAIN.htm#Mariedied1260
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------------
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Henry_II,_Duke_of_Brabant
2 CONT
2 CONT http://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Henri_II_de_Brabant
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.genealogics.org/getperson.php?personID=I00008759&tree=LEO
2 CONT
2 CONT Henri I was born circa 1165, probably in Leuven, in the Landgraviate of Brabant.  Henri I was Duke of Brabant from 1183 to his death, and Duke of Lower Lotharingia from 1190 to his death.  He was installed in 1180 as Duke of Lower
2 CONC  Lotharingy, which he held until 1222. He was Duke of Louvain 1183-1198. He returned property to Aachen St Maria, in the presence of "filiis meis Heinrico milite, Alberto clerico", by charter dated Sep 1185. He was installed as Du
2 CONC ke of Brabant in 1191. He agreed to divide "terram de Mussal" if "comes de Dasborc" died without heirs by charter dated 1197. He was one of the leaders of a crusade planned by Emperor Heinrich VI King of Germany, arriving in Pales
2 CONC tine in mid-1197. He was marching to relieve Jaffa, captured by the Muslims in Sep 1198, when he heard news of the death of Henri de Champagne, King of Jerusalem. He returned to Acre and took interim charge of the government until
2 CONC  the arrival of Amaury de Lusignan, King of Cyprus in Jan 1198. He recaptured Beirut from the Muslims in Oct 1197. After the murder of Philipp von Hohenstaufen, King of Germany in 1208, Philippe II "Auguste", King of France promot
2 CONC ed the candidacy of Duke Henri for the German throne. Duke Henri joined his son-in-law Emperor Otto IV against France, and was defeated at the battle of Bouvines in 1214. Markgraaf van Antwerpen 1211. [1]  He died on 5 September 1
2 CONC 235 in Köln (English: Cologne) in the Kingdom of Germany. He was buried in St. Peter's church in Leuven.  ROYAL ANCESTRY by Douglas Richardson Vol. I page 501  ↑ Medieval Lands, 2nd Edition  https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/User:Hr
2 CONC ishikes/sandbox#/image/File:Descent_of_U.S._Presidents_from_English_Royalty_3.png  Wikipedia:Henry I, Duke of Brabant 
2 CONT
2 CONT Henri II de Brabant, né en 1207, mort à Louvain le 1er février 1248, fut duc de Brabant de 1235 à 1248. Il était fils d'Henri Ier, duc de Brabant, et de Matilde de Boulogne.
2 CONT
2 CONT A peine né, il fut fiancé à une fille de Philippe de Souabe, roi des Romains et compétiteur d'Othon IV de Brunswick. Son père le donna en otage à plusieurs reprises, et il apparait dans les chartes et diplômes au côtés de son père
2 CONC  à partir de 1221. Il fut armé chevalier en 1226. En 1228, il se signala dans une campagne contre l'archevêque de Cologne.
2 CONT
2 CONT Il succède à son père en 1235. En 1237, il fut impliqué dans la guerre entre l'évêque de Liège et la famille de Limburg, puis dans les luttes d'influence qui se déchénèrent à la mort de l'évêque pour l'élection de son successeur. 
2 CONC La guerre ne se termina qu'en 1243. Après cette date, il n'intervint plus dans les affaires de l'Empire, se consacrant à la gestion de son duché.
2 CONT
2 CONT Henri II et Sophie de Thuringe furent inhumés dans un mausolée situé dans le choeur de l'église de l'abbaye cistercienne de Villers-en-Brabant.
2 CONT
2 CONT Il épousa en premières noces avant 1215 Marie de Hohenstaufen (1201 † 1235), fille de Philippe de Souabe, roi des Romains et d'Irène Ange. Ils eurent :
2 CONT
2 CONT #Henri III († 1261), duc de Brabant
2 CONT
2 CONT #Philippe, mort jeune
2 CONT
2 CONT #Mathilde (1224 † 1288), mariée en 1237 à Robert Ier de France (1216 † 1250), comte d'Artois, puis en 1254 Guy III de Châtillon († 1289), comte de Saint-Pol
2 CONT
2 CONT #Béatrice (1225 † 1288), mariée en 1241 à Henri Rapse († 1247), landgrave de Thuringe puis roi des Romains, puis en 1247 Guillaume III de Dampierre (1224 † 1251), comte de Flandre
2 CONT
2 CONT #Marie (1226 † 1256), mariée en 1254 à Louis II de Wittelsbach (1229 † 1294), duc de Bavière
2 CONT
2 CONT #Marguerite († 1277), abbesse de Herzogenthal
2 CONT
2 CONT Veuf, il se remarie vers 1240 à Sophie de Thuringia (1224 † 1275), fille de Louis IV, landgrave de Thuringe, et d'Elisabeth de Hongrie. Ils eurent :
2 CONT
2 CONT #Henri Ier (1244 † 1308), landgrave de Hesse, tige de la maison de Hesse.
2 CONT
2 CONT #Elisabeth (1243 † 1261), mariée en 1254 à Albert Ier (1236 † 1279), duc de Brunswick
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry II, Duke of Brabant
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry II of Brabant (French: Henri II de Brabant, Dutch: Hendrik II van Brabant, 1207 – February 1, 1248 in Leuven) was Duke of Brabant and Lothier after the death of his father Henry I in 1235.
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry II supported his sister Mathilde's son, William II, Count of Holland, in the latter's bid for election as German King.
2 CONT
2 CONT Family and children
2 CONT
2 CONT His first marriage was to Marie of Hohenstaufen (1201–1235, Leuven), daughter of Philip of Swabia and Irene Angelina. They had six children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry III, Duke of Brabant (d. 1261)
2 CONT
2 CONT Philip, died young
2 CONT
2 CONT Matilda of Brabant (1224 – September 29, 1288), married: 
2 CONT
2 CONT in Compiègne June 14, 1237 to Robert I of Artois;
2 CONT
2 CONT before May 31, 1254 to Guy II of Châtillon, Count of Saint Pol.
2 CONT
2 CONT Beatrix (1225 – November 11, 1288), married: 
2 CONT
2 CONT at Kreuzburg March 10, 1241 Heinrich Raspe Landgrave of Thuringia;
2 CONT
2 CONT in Leuven November 1247 to William III of Dampierre, Count of Flanders (1224 – June 6, 1251).
2 CONT
2 CONT Marie (c. 1226 – January 18, 1256, Donauwörth), married Louis II, Duke of Upper Bavaria. She was beheaded by her husband on suspicion of infidelity.
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret (d. March 14, 1277), Abbess of Herzogenthal.
2 CONT
2 CONT His second marriage was to Sophie of Thuringia (March 20, 1224 – May 29, 1275), daughter of Ludwig IV of Thuringia and Elisabeth of Hungary by whom he had two children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry (1244–1308, created Landgrave of Hesse in 1263.
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth (1243 – October 9, 1261), married in Braunschweig July 13, 1254 to Albert I, Duke of Brunswick-Lüneburg
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Henry_II,_Duke_of_Brabant
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry II of Brabant (French: Henri II de Brabant, Dutch: Hendrik II van Brabant, 1207 – February 1, 1248 in Leuven) was Duke of Brabant and Lothier after the death of his father Henry I in 1235. His mother was Mathilde of Flanders
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry II supported his sister Mathilde's son, William II, Count of Holland, in the latter's bid for election as German King.
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit] Family and children
2 CONT
2 CONT His first marriage was to Marie of Hohenstaufen (April 3, 1201–1235, Leuven), daughter of Philip of Swabia and Irene Angelina. They had six children:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.Henry III, Duke of Brabant (d. 1261)
2 CONT
2 CONT 2.Philip, died young
2 CONT
2 CONT 3.Matilda of Brabant (1224 – September 29, 1288), married: 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.in Compiègne June 14, 1237 to Robert I of Artois;
2 CONT
