1 NOTE In 1278, John was questioned as to his title to the lands. He brought to court an ancient rusty sword saying,Here, my Lord, is my warrant. My ancestors coming with William the Bastard won their land with this sword, and with the s
2 CONC word I will hold them against all comers.' With this plea he won his case." - "Royal Ancestors of Magna Charta Barons," Carr P. Collins (Dallas, 1959), p. 253. John was 7th Earl of Surrey, Sussex and Warren.
