1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==concerns==
2 CONT '''Seeing that this Blanche's husband William de la Planche appears to be the same as https://www.geni.com/people/William-de-la-Plaunchez/6000000000641960170 and her son James de la Planche appears to be the same as https://www.ge
2 CONC ni.com/people/James-de-la-Plaunche-of-Haversham/6000000004850154363, she appears to be the same as https://www.geni.com/people/Alice-NN/6000000022321536530.  Are they supposed to be the same person?  Further research is warranted.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==brief biography and family==
2 CONT Baroness Tingry
2 CONT
2 CONT Lady of Louplande
2 CONT
2 CONT ==comments==
2 CONT Given name has also been reported to be '''Madeleine'''.
2 CONT
2 CONT Date and place of birth have also been erroneously reported to be between circa 1245 and circa 1252 at Courtrain (probably a misspelling of ''Courtrai'', the French name for Kortrijk), Mynn (maybe a misspelling of ''Maine''), Fran
2 CONC ce.
2 CONT
2 CONT Date and place of marriage to William/Guillaume de Fiennes have also been erroneously reported to be:
2 CONT
2 CONT * February 1267 at Wigmore, Herefordshire, England
2 CONT * February 1268 at Wigmore, Herefordshire, England
2 CONT
2 CONT Date and place of death have been (erroneously?) reported to be June 11, 1302 (the date of her 2nd husband's death) at Louplande, Sarthe, (now Pays de la Loire), France.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==content to clean up==
2 CONT ===References
2 CONT # Roberts, Gary Boyd. ''The Royal Descents of 600 Immigrants''. Baltimore, MD, USA: Genealogical Publishing Co., (2004). Section: Immigrant Descendants of High Medieval Kings. Page 385. < [https://www.ancestry.com/imageviewer/coll
2 CONC ections/49324/images/FLHG_RoyalDescentsof600Immigrants-0489?ranMID=50138&ranEAID=4026539&ranSiteID=Xib7NfnK11s-OX.rA2C0xPEjs.87ueVoQw&o_xid=4026539&o_lid=4026539&o_sch=Affiliate+External&pId=93946 Ancestry.com] >; ([https://www.ge
2 CONC ni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000212566386836 document attached.]) "Descent from https://www.geni.com/people/Alfonso-IX-king-of-Leon-and-Galicia/6000000008477543238 & https://www.geni.com/people/Berenguela-I-la-Grande-reina-de-
2 CONC Castilla/6000000001412951572?through=6000000008477543238." 
2 CONT #https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blanche_de_Brienne,_Baroness_Tingry
2 CONT #https://stirnet.com/genie/data/continent/bb/brienne1.php#dau1 (membership required in order to view without interruption)
2 CONT #https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Brienne-2
2 CONT #https://www.familysearch.org/tree/person/details/9CHH-WJS
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ----
2 CONT '''Blanche de Brienne, Baroness Tingry is a direct descendant of Charlemagne.
2 CONT This is her Capetian lineage:
2 CONT '''
2 CONT # Hugues Capet, roi des Francs [First Capet] [A direct descendant of Charlemagne, via both parents]
2 CONT # Robert II Capet, "the Pious" king of the Franks
2 CONT # Robert I le Vieux, duc de Bourgogne
2 CONT # Constance de Bourgogne, Queen consort of Castile and Leon
2 CONT # Urraca I, reina de Castilla y León
2 CONT # Alfonso VII the Emperor, King of Castile and Leon
2 CONT # Fernando II, rey de León 
2 CONT # Alfonso IX, king of Leon and Galicia
2 CONT # Berenguela de León, emperatriz consorte de Constantinopla
2 CONT # Jean (John) de Brienne
2 CONT # Blanche de Brienne, Baroness Tingry
