2 CONT a)         GEOFFROY [V] (-after Nov 1218).  "Hugo Castriduni vicecomes" sold "terram nemoris Vindocinensis...inter Romilliacum et Calviniacum" to Marmoutier, with the consent of “Johannes de Lavardin, Gaufridus de Lavardin, Hugo d
2 CONC e Sancto Agilo, Dometa uxor eius et filius ipsius, Gaufredus Vogrin, Ursio de Fracta Valle et Nevelo filius eius et eorum uxores et liberi...eorum...Johanna vicecomitissa uxor mea et Gaufredus filius noster”, by charter dated to [
2 CONC 1175/84][988].  Vicomte de Châteaudun.  "Gaufridus vicecomes Castriduni" confirmed the foundation of "la chapelle de la Chauvelière", with the consent of "Adelicia uxore mea et Philippo et Hugone filiis meis", by charter dated to 
2 CONC [1190][989].  "Gaufridus vicecomes Castriduni" donated property to Hôtel-Dieu, Châteaudun with the consent of "Adelicia uxore mea, Philippo filio meo et Agnete sorore mea" by charter dated Feb 1200[990].  "Gaufridus Castriduni vic
2 CONC ecomes et dominus Montis Dublelli et domina Adelicia uxor mea" granted letters of immunity relating to Cormenon by charter dated 1 Mar 1202[991].  "Gaufridus vicecomes Castriduni" freed a serf, with the consent of "Adelicia uxore 
2 CONC mea et heredibus meis Gaufrido et Isabella", by charter dated 1202[992].  "Gaufridus vicecomes Castriduni" donated property to Hôtel-Dieu, Châteadun with the consent of "Adelicia uxore mea et Gaufrido filio meo et filiabus meis Is
2 CONC abella, Adelicia, Iohanna et Agnete" by charter dated Oct 1209[993].  "G comes Castriduni et A uxor mea" donated property to the abbey of Bécheron with the consent of "Gaufrido filio nostro, et Ysabella, Adelicia, Johanna, Agneta 
2 CONC filiabus nostris" by charter dated 1212 in which he names "dominus Jobertus de Guerchia avus meus et Johanna mater mea filia ipsius, comitissa d'Alençon"[994].  "Gaufridus vicecomes Castriduni et…Adelicia vicecomitissa" donated a 
2 CONC fair to the priory of Mondoubleau, with the consent of "Gaufrido filio nostro, filiabus nostris Ysabella, Adelicia, Johanna et Agnete", by charter dated May 1213[995].  [Seigneur de la Guerche]: a charter dated 1217 records that “
