2 CONC ires dou chastel de Neeles chevaliers et...Climence sa femme“ settled disputes about “la justice des bois de Perty” with Igny abbey by charter dated May 1259[1024].  The necrology of Braine Saint-Yved records the death “IX Kal Jul
2 CONC “ of “Roberti de Drocis militis filii...Roberti comitis Drocarum et domini Branæ” and his donation for the soul of “quondam uxore sua Clementia vicecomitissa Castriduni“[1025].  Clémence must have died before 1260, when her patern
2 CONC al aunt Agnes claimed her rights against Clémence’s husband and their daughter (see below).  m (before 1253) as his first wife, ROBERT de Dreux Seigneur de Beu, son of ROBERT [III] "Gasteblé" Comte de Dreux & his wife Aliénor dame
2 CONC  de Saint-Valéry ([1217]-23 Jun 1264).  Vicomte de Châteaudun by right of his wife. 
