1 OCCU Countess of Ponthieu and Montreuil 1221 - 1251
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marie_de_Ponthieu
2 CONT
2 CONT http://genealogics.org/getperson.php?personID=I00013719&tree=LEO
2 CONT
2 CONT Marie de Ponthieu (av.1199 † 1250), fut comtesse de Ponthieu de 1221 à 1250. Elle était fille de Guillaume II, comte de Ponthieu, et d'Adèle de France.
2 CONT
2 CONT Probablement sous l'influence de Philippe II Auguste, elle épousa en septembre 1208 Simon de Dammartin (1180 † 1239), déjà comte d'Aumale. Vers 1211, Simon de Dammartin et son frère Renaud trahirent Philippe Auguste et s'allièrent
2 CONC  à Jean sans Terre, roi d'Angleterre. Ils combattirent tous deux à Bouvines, Renaud fut fait prisonnier et Simon s'enfuit et s'exila. Le roi de France s'empara des biens de Simon, ainsi que du Ponthieu lorsque Marie en hérita. Ce 
2 CONC n'est qu'en 1220 que Simon fit sa soumission et que les époux purent récupérer leurs domaines[1]. Les deux époux sont cités le 2 mai 1230 lorsqu'il confirment la donation d'une propriété à l'abbaye Notre Dame d'Ourscamp. De ce pre
2 CONC mier mariage naquirent :
2 CONT
2 CONT #Jeanne (v. 1220 † 1279), comtesse de Ponthieu et d'Aumale ;
2 CONT
2 CONT #Philippe († 1278/81), mariée à Raoul de Lusignan († 1246), comte d'Eu, puis à Raoul († 1250), sire de Coucy, et à Otton II († 1271), comte de Gueldre ;
2 CONT
2 CONT #Marie, mariée à Jean II de Pierrepont († 1251), comte de Roucy ;
2 CONT
2 CONT #Agathe, mariée à Aymery II, vicomte de Châtellerault.
2 CONT
2 CONT Veuve, Marie se remarie vers 1240 avec Mathieu de Montmorency († 1250 Mansourah), seigneur d'Atichy, fils de Mathieu II, baron de Montmorency, et de Gertrude de Soissons.
2 CONT
2 CONT Elle meurt en septembre 1250.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Marie was the daughter of William IV of Ponthieu and Alys, Countess of the Vexin, and granddaughter of King Louis VII of France by his second wife Constance of Castile. As her father's only surviving child, Marie succeeded him, ru
2 CONC ling as Countess of Ponthieu and Montreuil from 1221 to 1251.
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit]Marriages and children
2 CONT
2 CONT She married Simon de Dammartin before September 1208. He was the son of Alberic II de Dammartin and Maud de Clermont, daughter of Renaud de Clermont, Count de Clermont-en-Beauvaisis and Clemence de Bar.[2] Simon and Marie had four
2 CONC  daughters but only two are recorded. The eldest was Joan of Dammartin (1220- 16 March 1279), second wife of Ferdinand III of Castile. Through her granddaughter Eleanor of Castile she is an ancestor of the British royal family. Th
2 CONC e other daughter was Philippa of Dammartin (died 1277/81) who married firstly Raoul II d' Issoudun, secondly Raoul II de Coucy, and thirdly Otto II, Count Geldern.
2 CONT
2 CONT Marie married secondly sometime between September 1240 and 15 December 1241, Mathieu de Montmorency, Seigneur d'Attichy, who was killed in battle at Mansurrah on 8 February 1250 during the Seventh Crusade, led by King Louis IX of 
2 CONC France.[
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Marie of Ponthieu (17 April 1199[1]-1251) was the Countess of Ponthieu and Countess of Montreuil, ruling from 1221 to 1251.
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit] Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Marie was the daughter of William IV of Ponthieu and Alys, Countess of the Vexin, and granddaughter of King Louis VII of France by his second wife Constance of Castile. As her father's only surviving child, Marie succeeded him, ru
2 CONC ling as Countess of Ponthieu and Montreuil from 1221 to 1251.
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit] Marriages and children
2 CONT
2 CONT She married Simon de Dammartin before September 1208. He was the son of Alberic II de Dammartin and Maud de Clermont, daughter of Renaud de Clermont, Count de Clermont-en-Beauvaisis and Clemence de Bar.[2] Simon and Marie had four
2 CONC  daughters but only two are recorded. The eldest was Jeanne of Dammartin (1220- 16 March 1279), second wife of Ferdinand III of Castile. Through her granddaughter Eleanor of Castile she is an ancestor of the British royal family. 
2 CONC The other daughter was Philippa of Dammartin (died 1277/81) who married firstly Raoul II d' Issoudun, secondly Raoul II de Coucy, and thirdly Otto II, Count Geldern.
2 CONT
2 CONT Marie married secondly sometime between September 1240 and 15 December 1241, Mathieu de Montmorency, Seigneur d'Attichy, who was killed in battle at Mansurrah on 8 February 1250 during the Seventh Crusade, led by King Louis VII of
2 CONC  France.[3]
