1 NOTE Marie, Countess of Ponthieu and Montgomerie, succeeded her father inthese counties. She married Simon de Dammartin, Count d'Aumale, whohaving followed the party of Ferrand, Count of Flanders, against PhilipAugustus, her uncle, was
2 CONC  proscribed for this in 1214 and withdrew toEngland. The King of France in his vengeance took extreme measure of thelaw and seized also all the possessions of the wife, his niece, includingthe County of Ponthieu. Her husband was n
2 CONC ot pardoned until the reign ofLouis IX, called the Saint, in March, 1230, who returned his possessions,and he died Sept. 21, 1239. Marie died in 1251, leaving three daughters:Jeanne, Phillipette and Marie.
