1 NAME Jean /Rochefoucauld-Marsillac/
2 GIVN Jean
2 _MARNM Rochefoucauld-Marsillac
1 NAME Jean I, seigneur de La Rochefoucauld
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1430
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1472
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://genealogics.org/getperson.php?personID=I00050819&tree=LEO
2 CONT
2 CONT BIOGRAPHY Jean was the son of Foucaud III de La Rochefoucauld, seigneur et baron de La Rochefoucauld, and Jeanne de Rochechouart, dame de Paransay. On 27 February 144 6 he married his cousin Marguerite de La Rochefoucauld, dame de
2 CONC  Barbezieux, daughter of Jean de La Rochefoucauld, seigneur de Barbezieux et de Verteuil, and Jeanne Sanglier, dame de Château-Guibert. They had a son François who would have progeny. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Jean was counsellor and chamberlain to kings Louis XI and Charles VIII, and governor of Bayonne. The most powerful vassal of Jean d'Orléans, comte d'Angoulême, he became guardian and tutor of Jean's son Charles (the future father 
2 CONC of King François I), who was only eight on the death of his father. Jean died in 1472.
