1 CONT He was also known as Regnault de Morelet both sources specifically mention that Morelet is a surname.328,329 He was also known as Renaud de Bettencourt.330 He was also known as Reinaldo de Bettencourt.331,332 He was also known as 
1 CONC Reynault de Béthencourt.333,334 He was also known as Reynaldo Bitancur.335 He was also known as Renault de Bethencourt.336 He was also known as Regnault de Moreau.337,338 In 1385 Jean gave to his brother Regnault, as part of his p
1 CONC aternal inheritance, the manor of Grand Quesnay and the lands of Huqueleu and Mauquenchy.339 He was aknight.340 He was Lord chamberlain of the Duke of Burgundy and of the King between 1400 and 1401.341 In 1402 Regnault was sent as
1 CONC  Ambassador to Spain to persuade King Henry III to render obedience to the Pope at Avignon.342 In Feb 1405 he visited his brother Jean de Bethencourt at Grainville-la-Teinturière when he was home on a short visit from the Canary I
1 CONC slands.343 He was put in charge of the supply of bread in 1410 in Paris.344 In 1411 Regnault de Bethencourt (IV) was named captain of the guard of the castle of Longueville.345 In 1412 he received, in payment for his services, a h
1 CONC ouse in Paris.346 
1 CONT
1 CONT He pledged fealty to King Henry V of England after the English had conquered most of Normandy in 1419.347 On 11 May 1421 Regnault's goods were increased by the gift which Jean (IV) made him of all his personal fortune.348 As vassa
1 CONC l of the Kings of England and of France, he performed the duties of Chief Treasurer of Normandy (1423) and Commander of the night watch of the streets of Paris (1424), a duty which he lost when the city returned to the possession 
1 CONC of the French in 1436.349 On 6 Apr 1426 Regnault was granted the fief of Béthencourt as well as 500 libras from the revenues of the lands of Granville which were awarded to Aldonce de Bracquemont and her husband Pierre de Rouville
1 CONC .350 In 1428 Regnault (IV) ceded the lands of Béthencourt to Regnault (V) who was creditor of Jean (IV).351
