1 CONC Drincourt (now Neufchatel-en-Bray), in the 1173-4 revolt of Henry II of England's sons, under the leadership of Philip of Flanders. Wounded by a crossbow bolt, he did not recover.
1 CONT He forcefully eloped with his wife, then a nun at Romsey. She afterwards left him and became its Abbess.
