0 @N6000000003615765622@ NOTE (1) MAUD, whose mother was Edith, of whom nothing is known (b).  She m. in 1103, Rotrou, COUNT of Perche, styled the Great, s. and h. of Geoffrey, Count of Perche, by Beatrice, da. of Hilduin, Count of Montdidier and  (jure uxoris
1 CONC ) Count of Roucy.  Rotrou had gone on the 1st Crusade in 1096.  In 1105 and 1114 he went to Spain, to help his cousin Alfonso I, King of Navarre and Aragon, against the Moors.  In 1114 he assisted Henry I at the siege of Belleme, 
1 CONC which he had long before claimed as his hereditary right. The King granted him the Belleme fiefs. He was present at the death of his royal father-in-law in 1135. In 1137 Stephen gave him Moulins; but in 1141 he made terms with Geo
1 CONC ffrey Plantagenet.  Maud was drowned in the wreck of the White Ship, 25 Nov. 1120, leaving 2 daughters. Rotrou m., 2ndly, before 1127, Hawise, da. of Walter de Salisbury, and sister of Patrick, 1st EARL OF Salisbury. He d. in 1144
1 CONC  at the siege of the Tower of Rouen (20 Jan. to 23 Apr.) by Geoffrey Plantagenet, and his widow m., as his 2nd wife, Robert, 1st Count of Dreux, 3rd s. of Louis VI (Le Gros), King of France; which Robert styled himself Count of Pe
1 CONC rche and lord of Belleme during the minority of his stepson.
1 CONT
1 CONT  (b) As her daughter married in 1103, she cannot be the daughter of Forn.
