1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT    Louis VI (1081-1137), king of France (1108-1137). Almost his entire
1 CONT reign
1 CONT   was spent in subduing the robber barons, who preyed on the environs of
1 CONT   Paris but were finally forced to yield to royal authority. For some
1 CONT 20 years
1 CONT    during the period from 1109-1135, Louis waged war against Henry I,
1 CONT the
1 CONT   Norman king of England, and against Henry's son-in-law, Holy Roman
1 CONT  Emperor Henry V. Louis greatly strengthed the royal power in France.
