0 @N6000000000269776088@ NOTE Robert I of Dreux, (Robert I Capet) nicknamed the Great (c. 1123 – October 11, 1188), was the fifth son of Louis VI of France and Adélaide de Maurienne. Through his mother he was related to the Carolingians and to the Marquess Wil
1 CONC liam V of Montferrat.
1 CONT
1 CONT In 1137 he received the County of Dreux as an appanage from his father. He held this title until 1184 when he granted it to his son Robert II.
1 CONT
1 CONT In 1139 he married Agnes de Garlande. In 1145, he married Hawise d'Evreux (Devereux). By his third marriage to Agnes de Baudemont in 1152, he received the County of Braine-sur-Vesle, and the lordships of Fère-en-Tardenois, Pontarc
1 CONC y, Nesle, Longueville, Quincy-en-Tardenois, Savigny, and Baudemont.
1 CONT
1 CONT Robert I participated in the Second Crusade and was at the Siege of Damascus in 1148. In 1158 he fought against the English and participated in the Siege of Séez in 1154.
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] Marriages and children Agnes de Garlande (1122–1143), daughter of Anseau de Garlande, count of Rochefort Simon (1141 – bef. 1182), lord of La Noue Hawise d'Evreux (1118–1152), daughter of Walter (FitzEdward) d'Evreux of Sal
1 CONC isbury, Sheriff of Wiltshire Adèle (1145 – aft. 1210), married firstly Valéran III, count of Breteuil, secondly Guy II, lord of Châtillon-sur-Marne, thirdly Jean I de Thorotte, fourthly Raoul I of Nesle, count of Soissons Alice or
1 CONC  Adelheid (1144–?) Agnes de Baudemont, Countess of Braine (1130 – c. 1202) Robert II (1154–1218), count of Dreux and Braine Henry (1155–1199), bishop of Orléans Alix (1156 – aft. 1217), married Raoul I, lord of Coucy Philippe (115
1 CONC 8–1217), bishop of Beauvais Isabella (1160–1239), married Hugh III of Broyes Peter (1161–1186) William (1163 – aft. 1189), lord of Braye, Torcy, and Chilly John (1164 – aft. 1189) Mamilie (1166–1200) Margaret (1167–?), nun The Sic
1 CONC ilian chancellor Stephen du Perche may also have been a son (legitimate or not) of his.
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] Source Title: Ancestral Roots of Certain American Colonists Who Came to America Before 1700 by Frederick Lewis Weis, Lines 50-25, 135-27 & 273-28
