0 @N6000000002187840745@ NOTE Robert I of Dreux
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Robert I of Dreux, nicknamed the Great (c. 1123 – October 11, 1188), was the fifth son of Louis VI of France and Adélaide de Maurienne. Through his mother he was related to the Carolingians and to the Marquess William V of Montfer
1 CONC rat.
1 CONT
1 CONT In 1137 he received the County of Dreux as an appanage from his father. He held this title until 1184 when he granted it to his son Robert II.
1 CONT
1 CONT In 1139 he married Agnes de Garlande. In 1145, he married Hawise d'Evreux (Devereux). By his third marriage to Agnes de Baudemont in 1152, he received the County of Braine-sur-Vesle, and the lordships of Fère-en-Tardenois, Pontarc
1 CONC y, Nesle, Longueville, Quincy-en-Tardenois, Savigny, and Baudemont.
1 CONT
1 CONT Robert I participated in the Second Crusade and was at the Siege of Damascus in 1148. In 1158 he fought against the English and participated in the Siege of Séez in 1154.
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit]
1 CONT Marriages and children
1 CONT Agnes de Garlande (1122–1143), daughter of Anseau de Garlande, count of Rochefort 
1 CONT Simon (1141 – bef. 1182), lord of La Noue 
1 CONT Hawise d'Evreux (1118–1152), daughter of Walter (FitzEdward) d'Evreux of Salisbury, Sheriff of Wiltshire 
1 CONT Adèle (1145 – aft. 1210), married firstly Valéran III, count of Breteuil, secondly Guy II, lord of Châtillon-sur-Marne, thirdly Jean I de Thorotte, fourthly Raoul I of Nesle, count of Soissons 
1 CONT Agnes de Baudemont, countess of Braine (1130 – c. 1202) 
1 CONT Robert II (1154–1218), count of Dreux and Braine 
1 CONT Henry (1155–1199), bishop of Orléans 
1 CONT Alix (1156 – aft. 1217), married Raoul I, lord of Coucy 
1 CONT Philippe (1158–1217), bishop of Beauvais 
1 CONT Isabella (1160–1239), married Hugh III of Broyes 
1 CONT Peter (1161–1186) 
1 CONT William (1163 – aft. 1189), lord of Braye, Torcy, and Chilly 
1 CONT John (1164 – aft. 1189) 
1 CONT Mamilie (1166–1200) 
1 CONT Margaret (1167–?), nun 
0 @N6000000005076750397@ NOTE Robert I de France, Comte de Dreux was born circa 1123. He was the son of Louis VI, Roi de France and Adelaide di Savoia. He married Agnes de Baudemont, Dame de Braine, daughter of Guido de Beaudement, Seigneur de Braine and Alice
1 CONC  (?), in 1152.1 He died on 11 October 1188.
1 CONT      Robert I de France, Comte de Dreux gained the title of Comte de Dreux.2
1 CONT Children of Robert I de France, Comte de Dreux and Agnes de Baudemont, Dame de Braine
1 CONT Robert II de Dreux, Comte de Dreux+ b. c 1154, d. c 1218
1 CONT Alice de Dreux+ b. c 1156/57, d. a 1217
1 CONT Citations
1 CONT [S16] Jirí Louda and Michael MacLagan, Lines of Succession: Heraldry of the Royal Families of Europe, 2nd edition (London, U.K.: Little, Brown and Company, 1999), table 64. Hereinafter cited as Lines of Succession.
1 CONT [S8] Charles Mosley, editor, Burke's Peerage and Baronetage, 106th edition, 2 volumes (Crans, Switzerland: Burke's Peerage (Genealogical Books) Ltd, 1999), volume 1, page 226. Hereinafter cited as Burke's Peerage and Baronetage, 1
1 CONC 06th edition.
0 @N6000000005598936573@ NOTE The location of the countship of Dreux was near the border of Normandi e and Ile-de-France, taking its name from the chief city.  Its histor y dates from the fifth century and was the scene of many changes of ru lers, including th
1 CONC at of Richard I, Duc of Normandie.
1 CONT
1 CONT Robert is styled as the head of a line of Counts of Dreux, and later B rittany.  In 1147, Robert took part in a crusade, and on reaching Cons tantinople refused, as a prince, to do homage to the Emperor Manuel fo r land he might a
1 CONC cquire in Palestine.  Later he proceeded to Antioch a nd Damascus.  While his older brother lingered in the Holy Land, Rober t was charged with escorting the barons and preletes back to France. In 1149 he became the focus of a feu
1 CONC dal revolt.  In 1150, he fought i n Normandie for Henry II, King of England. Robert received the county of Dreux from his father in 1152.
0 @N6000000009304845472@ NOTE #Générale#inhumation : Braîne sur Vesle St Yved 02
1 CONT
1 CONT Comte de Dreux et du Perche, Sgr de Savigny, de Torcy, de Brie-Comte-Robert, deCahilly et de Longjumeau, comte de Braine-sur-Vesle
1 CONT
1 CONT On a gravé sur sa tombe :
1 CONT " Princeps Robertus mira pietate refertus
1 CONT Hic jacet : heu ! noli plura rogare, tacet ".
1 CONT Accompagne Louis VII en 1147 à la 2ème croisade (1147-1149)  ;
1 CONT Fait la guerre à Henri Plantagenêt en 1158-1159 en Gascogne & Languedoc  ;
1 CONT En 1159, accorde une charte à la ville de Dreux et fonde à Paris l'égliseSaint-Thomas du Louvre  ;
1 CONT En 1170, dote sa ville de Brie-Comte-Robert d'un puissant château fort  ;
1 CONT Abandonne la direction de son comté en 1184.
1 CONT (Ribaldone Thierry)
1 CONT
