0 @N6000000008799929940@ NOTE [Jeremiah Brown.FTW]
1 CONT
1 CONT [from Ancestry.com 139798.GED]
1 CONT Robert de Bellomont, second Earl of Leicester, adhering to King Henry I upon all occasions, was with that monarch at his decease in 1135 and he afterwards as staunchly supported the interests of his grandson, Henry II, upon whose 
1 CONC accession to the throne he was constituted Justice of England. He married Godehilde, daughter of Raoul de Toeni II, who bore him no children, and from whom he was separated by 1090. When between fifty and sixty years of age, he ma
1 CONC rried Lady Elizabeth according to Crispin and Macary, and she, being young, was won over by WIlliam de Warren II, Earl of Warren and Surrey, so that she finally deserted him. Another source, Wurts, has him marrying Amicia Waer (Wa
1 CONC re), daughter of Ralph de Waer, Earl of Norfolk, by whom he had a son and two daughters.
