1 CONT  SAHER IV3 DE QUINCY, 1ST EARL OF WINCHESTER (Robert I2, Saher1), son of (2) Robert I2 and (X-2) Orabella (LOUCHERS) QUINCY, He married (1st) in England, before 1173, (AJ-53) LADY MARGARET DE BEAUMONT of Hampshire, daughter of (AJ
1 CONC -37) Robert III, 3rd Earl of Leicester and (PQ-4) Petronilla (de GRANTMESNIL), who was born circa 1154, was christened in 1235, and died on 12 Jan. 1234/5. 
0 @N6000000002247933528@ NOTE Magna Charta Surety, 1215
1 CONT
1 CONT He was active with Kings Richard and John in Normandy 1197-99, and in Oct 1200 he was appointed to conduct the King of Scotland to meet King John. In 1203, he was captured by the French, when he and his cousin Robert Fitz Walter, 
1 CONC surrendered the castle of Vendreuil, but had returned to England before 5 May 1204. By his marriage he became, in his wife's right, upon the death of her only brother, coheir to a moiety of the vast estates of the Honours of Leice
1 CONC stershire and Grandmesnil, of which he received custody 30 Mar 1205. He was created Earl of Winchester before 10 Feb 1206/07, and served in Scotland in 1209 and in Ireland in 1210, and was active in the work of the Exchequer, 1211
1 CONC -13, and justice in many counties. At Easter 1214/15, he was with the confederate barons against the King at Stamford, and in Jun 1215 he was one of the 25 chosen to enforce Magna Carta. Early the following year, with Robert Fitz 
1 CONC Walter, he went to invite Prince Louis to England, whereupon his lands were seized by the Crown. In Dec 1216, he defended the town of St. Albans from being sacked by Louis' army, and in the spring of 1217, lead an expedition to br
1 CONC ing relief to Mountsorrel Castle in Leicester, where he was defeated and captured by Henry III in May. Six months later he returned to his allegiance and his lands were restored. He joined the Crusaders and died at Damietta, and w
1 CONC as buried at Acre. His widow, Margaret, recognized as suo jure Countess of Winchester, died shortly before 12 Feb 1234/35, probably on 12 Jan.
