0 @N6000000005758036138@ NOTE Buried in Acre, Israel.  1st EARL OF WINCHESTER.Saer de Quincy, 1st Earl of Winchester (c. 1170?November 3, 1219) was one of the leaders of the baronial rebellion against King John of England, and a major figure in both Scotland a
1 CONC nd England in the decades around the turn of the twelfth and thirteenth centuries.    The family of de Quincy had arrived in England after the Norman Conquest, and took their name from Cuinchy in the Arrondissement of Bthune; the 
1 CONC personal name "Saer" was used by them over several generations. Both names are variously spelled in primary sources and older modern works, the first name being sometimes rendered Saher or Seer, and the surname as Quency or Quenci
1 CONC .    The first recorded Saer de Quincy (known to historians as "Saer I") was lord of the manor of Long Buckby in Northamptonshire in the earlier twelfth century, and second husband of Matilda of St Liz, stepdaughter of King David 
1 CONC I of Scotland. Their marriage produced two sons, Saer II and Robert de Quincy. It was Robert, th
