0 @N6000000004303398393@ NOTE WIKIPEDIA:
1 CONT
1 CONT Hugh de Kevelioc, 3rd Earl of Chester (1147 – June 30, 1181) was the son of Ranulph de Gernon, 2nd Earl of Chester and Maud of Gloucester, daughter of Robert, 1st Earl of Gloucester (otherwise known as Robert de Caen, the illegiti
1 CONC mate son of Henry I of England, making her Henry's granddaughter).
1 CONT
1 CONT He is thought by some to have taken his name from Kevelioc in Monmouth as his birthplace, but others think that instead he was born in, and took the name of, Cyfeiliog in Merionethshire or Meirionydd, Wales.
1 CONT He was underage when his father's death in 1153 made him heir to his family's estates on both sides of the channel. He joined the baronial Revolt of 1173-1174 against King Henry II of England, and was influential in convincing the
1 CONC  Bretons to revolt. After being captured and imprisoned after the Battle of Alnwick, he finally got his estates restored in 1177, and served in King Henry's Irish campaigns.
1 CONT
1 CONT In 1169 he married Bertrada de Montfort-l'Amauri, daughter of Simon III de Montfort. She was the cousin of King Henry, who gave her away in marriage. Their children were:
1 CONT 1.	Ranulph de Blondeville de Meschines, 4th Earl of Chester
1 CONT 2.	Maud of Chester (1171-1233), married David of Scotland, 8th Earl of Huntingdon
1 CONT 3.	Mabel of Chester, married William d'Aubigny, 4th Earl of Arundel
1 CONT 4.	Agnes of Chester (died November 2, 1247), married William de Ferrers, 4th Earl of Derby
1 CONT 5.	Hawise of Chester (1180-1242), married Robert de Quincy
1 CONT 6.	A daughter, name unknown, who was briefly married to Llywelyn Fawr
1 CONT He also had an illegitimate daughter, Amice of Chester, who married Ralph de Mainwaring.
1 CONT Hugh of Kevelioc died 30 June 1181 at Leek, Staffordshire, England.
1 CONT
1 CONT Sources
1 CONT •	Chronicle of the Abbey of St. Werburg at Chester (Lancashire and Cheshire Record Society)
1 CONT •	Chester, 3rd Earl, Hugh de Kevelioc, Oxford Dictionary of National Biography
1 CONT
1 CONT -------------------------
1 CONT
1 CONT AKA Hugh de Kevelioc.
1 CONT
1 CONT Third Earl of Chester, Vicomte d'Avranches in Normandy. He joined in the rebellion against King Henry II, was taken prisoner at Alnwick on July 13, 1174, and deprived of his Earldom. Though he was again in rebellion both in Englan
1 CONC d and Normandy, his Earldom was restored January 1177 (Complete Peerage, Vol III:167).
1 CONT
1 CONT Marriage 1 Spouse Unknown
1 CONT Children
1 CONT 1.	 Amicia le Meschine b: ABT 1178 in Chester, Cheshire, England
1 CONT
1 CONT Marriage 2 BERTRADE DE MONTFORT b: ABT 1155 in Montfort, Eure, France
1 CONT •	Married: 1169
1 CONT Children
1 CONT 1.	 HAWISE OF CHESTER b: 1180 in Chester, Cheshire, England
1 CONT 2.	 MABEL OF CHESTER b: ABT 1172 in Chester, Cheshire, England
1 CONT 3.	 Agnes of Chester b: ABT 1174 in Chester, Cheshire, England
1 CONT 4.	 Matilda (Maud) of Cheste b: 1171
1 CONT 5.	 Ranulf de Blundeville b: 1172 in Oswestry, Powys, Wales
1 CONT 6.	 Tanglust Kevelioc
1 CONT 7.	 Richard of Chester
1 CONT
1 CONT -------------------------
1 CONT
1 CONT FMG:
1 CONT
1 CONT HUGH "of Kevelioc" (Kevelioc, co. Monmouth 1147-Leek, Staffordshire 30 Jun 1181, bur Chester, Abbey of St Werburgh).  Robert of Torigny names "Hugonem filium suum" as successor of "Ranulfus comes Cestriæ"[70].  He succeeded his fa
1 CONC ther in 1153 as Earl of Chester, Vicomte d'Avranches, as a minor coming of age in 1158.  He joined the rebellion of Henry "the Young King" against Henry II King of England and was taken prisoner at Alnwick 13 Jul 1174.  He was dep
1 CONC rived of the earldom but restored in Jan 1177[71].  m (1169) BERTRADE de Montfort, daughter of SIMON de Montfort Comte d'Evreux & his wife Mahaut --- ([1155]-1227).  Robert of Torigny records the marriage arranged by Henry II King
1 CONC  of England in 1170 of "Hugoni comiti Cestriæ cognate suo" and "filiam comitis Ebroicensis cognatam suam ex parte patris sui"[72].  The primary source which confirms her name has not yet been identified.  Earl Hugh & his wife had 
1 CONC five children: 
1 CONT a)  MATILDA [Maud]
1 CONT b)  RANULF "de Blundeville
1 CONT c)  RICHARD 
1 CONT e)  AGNES [Alice]
1 CONT f)  HAWISE
1 CONT Earl Hugh had one illegitimate child by an unknown mistress:
1 CONT g)  AMICIA
