1 CONT himself to the internal security of his land and promoted domestic and
1 CONT foreign trade. Productivity doubled during his reign. He revolutionised
1 CONT the law system, and even sat over cases himself. He was a notable lawyer,
1 CONT and he built up the system of English Common Law, and began to develop
1 CONT the traditional jury system. He was a gifted administrator.
1 CONT Henry's notable failure was his attempt to curb the power and
1 CONT strength of the Church, particularly in the case of Thomas Beckett, who had been his wild pal until he was made Archbishop of Canterbury. His death did little for Henry's popularity.
1 CONT He was unfortunate in love, relentlessly and romantically pursuing the hand of his wife, Eleanor,
1 CONT who became a selfish spoilt lady, and who turned her sons against their own father.
1 CONT A rebellion by the eldest son, Henry was crushed, and Eleanor was placed under house arrest for fifteen years. The other brothers placed continual pressure on their father, in alliances with the King of France.
1 CONT Henry died a lonely and griefstricken man deserted by all of those he had loved and honoured.
1 CONT Father: *Geoffrey de Gatinais , of Anjou b: 24 Aug 1113 in Anjou, France
1 CONT Mother: *Matilda Alice , Emperess b: 5 Aug 1102 in Winchester, Hampshire, England
1 CONT Marriage 1 *Alice Capet , Princess b: 1170 in France
1 CONT Marriage 2 *Eleanor de Pointiers b: 1122
1 CONT Married: 11 May 1152 in Bordeaux, Gironde, France
1 CONT Children
