1 CONT Henry was born in 1133 and was married to 
1 CONT Eleanor, Duchess of
1 CONT Aquitaine immediately after her divorce from 
1 CONT Louis VII, King of France.
1 CONT They had nine children: William, Henry, 
1 CONT Matilda, Richard, Geoffrey,
1 CONT Philip, Eleanor, Joan and John. 
1 CONT Henry was the first of fourteen hereditary 
1 CONT kings, who were later refered to
1 CONT in the history oracles as Plantagenets. Henry 
1 CONT was the son of the Count of
1 CONT Anjou, whose family emblem was the 'plante 
1 CONT genet', a yellow flowering
1 CONT broom. 
1 CONT It was with the land bequeathed by the Count 
1 CONT to Henry and his auspicious
1 CONT marriage to Eleanor, which gained him a vast 
1 CONT amount of lands in France.
1 CONT These lands exceeded the lands owned in France 
1 CONT by the King of France,
1 CONT himself. In those times, the King of France ruled from Paris 
1 CONT and its surrounding areas. 
1 CONT Henry had lands reaching for 1000 miles, and it was this vast 
1 CONT domain, which was called the Angevin Empire. Henry was the first 
1 CONT king to demonstrate that he was truly a sovereign, and he ended all the 
1 CONT anarchy and demonstration of strengths throughout his lands. He devoted 
1 CONT himself to the internal security of his land and promoted domestic and 
1 CONT foreign trade. Productivity doubled during his reign. He revolutionised 
1 CONT the law system, and even sat over cases himself. He was a notable lawye
1 CONT and he built up the system of English Common Law, and began to develop 
1 CONT the traditional jury system. He was a gifted administrator. 
1 CONT Henry's notable failure was his attempt to curb the power and 
1 CONT strength of the Church, particularly
1 CONT in the case of Thomas Beckett, who had been his wild pal until he was 
1 CONT made Archbishop of Canterbury. His death did little for Henry's 
1 CONT popularity. 
1 CONT He was unfortunate in love, relentlessly and romantically 
1 CONT pursuing the hand of his wife, Eleanor,
1 CONT who became a selfish spoilt lady, and who turned her sons against their 
1 CONT own father. A rebellion by the eldest son, Henry was crushed, and Elean
1 CONT was placed under house arrest for fifteen years. The other brothers 
1 CONT placed continual pressure on their father, in alliances with the King of 
1 CONT France. Henry died a lonely and griefstricken man deserted by all of 
1 CONT those he had loved and honoured. 
