1 CONT
1 CONT Henry II (born 1133, ruled 1154-89). The grandson of Henry I was the
1 CONT first Plantagenet king of England. His mother was Matilda, daughter of
1 CONT Henry I. His father was Geoffrey of Anjou, whom Matilda married after
1 CONT the death of her first husband, Emperor Henry V. Geoffrey was called
1 CONT Plantagenet for his habit of wearing in his cap a sprig of the broom
1 CONT plant, which in Latin is called planta genista.
1 CONT    Henry II was born in Le Mans, France, in March 1133. During his
1 CONT mother's conflict with Stephen for the English throne he was brought to
1 CONT England. Stephen eventually recognized his claim, and Henry became king
1 CONT of England in 1154 after Stephen's death.
1 CONT    Henry II held England and Normandy by his mother's right. From his
1 CONT father he inherited, as French fiefs, the important counties of Anjou,
