1 CONT HIST HENRY II, WAS BORN IN 1133 TO GEOFFREY V PLANTAGENT AND MATILDA THEEMPRESS, DAUGHTER OF KING HENRY I OF ENGLAND.  HE GREW UP IN ANJOU,FRANCE, BUT VISITED ENGLAND AS EARLY AS 1142 TO DEFEND HIS
1 CONT  MOTHER'S CLAIM TO THE THRONE OF STEPHEN. EDUCATED
1 CONT HIST HENRY REVITALIZED THE BRITISH EXCHEQUER, ISSUING RECEIPTS FOR TAXPAYMENTS AND LOGGING ACCOUNTS ON ROLLED PARCHMENT.  HE REPLACEDINCOMPETENT SHERRIFFS, EXPANDING THE AUTHORITY OF ROYAL COURTS,
1 CONT  WHICH BROUGHT MORE MONEY TO HIM.  A BODY OF COMMON
1 CONT HIST THIS PROCESS OF STRENGTHENING ROYAL COURTS LED TO CONTROVERSY WITHCHURCH COURTS, WHERE MANY FUGITIVES FOUND A SAFE HAVEN AS AS MANY AS 1 IN50 ENGLISH SUBJECTS QUALIFIED AS CLERICS.  HENRY
1 CONT  WISHED TO TRANSFER SUCH CASES TO THE ROYAL COURTS, AS
1 CONT HIST THE SONS OF HENRY, HENRY THE YOUNG, RICHARD THE LION- HEART,GEOFFREY, AND JOHN LACK;AND, WERE NEVER SATISFIED AT THEIR FATHERS PLANSIN DIVIDING THE KINGDOM UPON HIS DEATH.  AT THE
1 CONT  ENCOURAGEMENT OF THEIR MOTHER, THE SON'S REBELLED SEVERAL
1 CONT DATE 24 MAY 2000
