0 @N6000000001783462577@ NOTE Basic Life Information
1 CONT Roger la Zouche, Sheriff of Devonshire was a younger son of Alan la Zouche and Alice de Belmeis. He was born circa 1182 at Ashby, Leicestershire, England. He was the heir of his brother William in 1199. He was Sheriff of Devonshir
1 CONC e at England between 1228 and 1231. Roger la Zouche was a witness to Henry III's confirmation of the Magna Charta.3 He died before 14 May 1238
1 CONT
1 CONT Roger la Zouche, brother of Alan later acquired possessed of Alan’s lands in Brittany and England.  He fought in France and later in Ireland for Henry III, often served as a royal messenger, and witnessed Henry’s confirmation of t
1 CONC he Magna Carta at Westminster in 1236/7.
1 CONT
1 CONT Marriage and Children
1 CONT He married Margaret (?) before 1203.  They had the following children:
1 CONT Alan, Lord Zouche, of Ashby+ b. c 1203, d. 1270
1 CONT Eudo la Zouche  b. c 1205, d. 1279
1 CONT Lora la Zouche  b. c 1206, d. a 1273
1 CONT <http://homepages.rootsweb.ancestry.com/~cousin/html/p392.htm>
