0 @N6000000000269706015@ NOTE Please find below a revised listing of the bastard children of King John.  The list has been augmented by many new references, corrections, and additions since my last posting of this listing.  The new listing includes Philip "Fiz
1 CONC  Le Rey" [i.e., Philip the king's son]) found in a 1263 Sussex fine as a possible bastard child of King John.
1 CONT
1 CONT Also, it appears there may be a link between Isabel, wife of Richard Fitz Ives, and another royal bastard, Eudes Fitz Roy.  I've learned that in 1245, Isabel's son and heir, William Fitz Ives, sued Giles de Chanceaux regarding pro
1 CONC perty in Cornwall.  This is surely the same man who was granted Eudes Fitz Roy's properties in Essex on his death without issue in 1242.  The Fitz Ives and Chanceaux link deserves further study.
1 CONT
1 CONT Comments are invited.
1 CONT
1 CONT Best always, Douglas Richardson, Salt Lake City, Utah
1 CONT
1 CONT - - - - - - - - - -
