1 CONT
1 CONT Clemence DAUNTSEY
1 CONT _______________________
1 CONT
1 CONT One source for the speculation that Agatha Ferrers was Joan's mother is Sir William Dugdale, in The Baronage of England (1675-6). He states his source to be Dr David Powel's History of Wales (1584). Powel's work is an enlarged edi
1 CONC tion of H Lhoyd's translation of The Historie of Cambria by the 12th century Saint Caradoc of Llancarfan.
1 CONT
1 CONT ___________________
1 CONT
1 CONT She and Richard FitzJohn of Dover were extremely close. She begged her father King John to spare her husband's life after his 2nd Welsh uprising in August of 1211. Joanna warned her father of
1 CONT baronial opposition when she overhead conversations in the Welsh court. Her husband erected the Friary of Llanfaes over her tomb. Her coffin is in the porch of the parish church.
1 CONT
1 CONT Web Site: "The Paternal Ancestry of Homer Beers James".
