1 CONT
1 CONT JOAN OF ENGLAND, born at Gloucester 22 July 1210.  In 1214 she was contracted to marry Geoffrey de Lusignan, son of Hugh de Lusignan, Count of la Marche, which marriage did not take place.  She married at York, Yorkshire 19 June 1
1 CONC 221 (as his 1st wife) ALEXANDER II, King of Scotland, Knt., son and heir of William the Lion, King of Scotland, by Ermengarde .... He was born at Haddington, East Lothian 24 August 1198.  They had no issue.  He was crowned at Scon
1 CONC e 6 Dec. 1214.  Joan died at York, Yorkshire 4 March 1237/8, buried at Tarrant Keynstan, Dorset.  Alexander II married (2nd) ... Mary de Coucy .... They had one son, Alexander (III) [King of Scotland].  Alexander II, King of Scotl
1 CONC and, died at Kerrera in the bay of Oban 8 July 1249, and was buried at Melrose Abbey.
