0 @N6000000002187840691@ NOTE Robert III of Dreux
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Arms of the Counts of DreuxRobert III of Dreux (1185–1234), Count of Dreux and Braine, was the son of Robert III, Count of Dreux, and Yolanda de Coucy. He was given the byname Gasteblé (lit. wheat-spoiler) when he destroyed a fiel
1 CONC d of wheat while hunting in his youth.
1 CONT
1 CONT Along with his brother Peter, Duke of Brittany he fought with future Louis VIII of France in 1212 at Nantes and was captured there during a sortie. Exchanged after the Battle of Bouvines for William Longsword, Earl of Salisbury, h
1 CONC e fought in the Albigensian Crusade, besieging Avignon in 1226. He was a supporter of Blanche of Castile during her regency after the death of Louis VIII in 1226.
1 CONT
1 CONT In 1210 he married Aénor of Saint-Valéry (1192–1250) and they had several children, including Yolande (1212–1248), who married Hugh IV, Duke of Burgundy, John I (1215–1249), later Count of Dreux, Robert (1217–1264), Viscount of Ch
1 CONC âteaudun, and Peter (1220–1250), a cleric.
1 CONT
1 CONT Preceded by:
1 CONT Robert II Count of Dreux
1 CONT 1218–1234 Succeeded by:
1 CONT John I 
0 @N6000000003949760252@ NOTE From: John Ravilious (Therav3@aol.com)  Subject: Re: Reginald de St. Valery and His Descendants
1 CONT Newsgroups: soc.genealogy.medieval  Date: 2002-09-30 09:39:35 PST 
1 CONT Monday, 30 September, 2002
1 CONT In 1210 or 1211 Annora had married Robert de Dreux, eldest son of Count Robert II of Dreux, and brother of Peter de Dreux later Duke of Brittany. Robert consistently supported Philip Augustus against King John, but made his peace 
1 CONC with Henry III in 1217. He became Count of Dress in 1218 and in February 1219 was awarded the lands that Thomas of St. Valery had held in England. By the end of 1226, as he had again chosen to side with France, Henry III seized al
1 CONC l his English lands.
1 CONT In 1227 Henry III granted all Robert de Dreux's English lands to his brother, Richard of Cornwall. The grant was confirmed by charter to 1231. Under Richard of Cornwall, Beckley, as a part of the honor of St. Valery, was the most 
1 CONC important of the five demesne manors of the honor in Oxfordshire-the others being Willaston, Blackthorn with Ambrosden, Asthall, and Yarnton; the honor was sometimes called 'of St. Valery of Beckley'; or simply `of Beckley'.' Rich
1 CONC ard's tenure at Beckley suffered one brief interruption after his capture by the Montfortiana at Lewes in 1264, but he recovered his lands in 1265 after Evesham Richard died in 1272 and was succeeded by his eldest surviving son, E
1 CONC dmund, who held the manor of St Valery, including Beckley and Horton for 28 years.
1 CONT He died in 1300, leaving no children, and his cousin, King Edward I, inherited his lands. Beckley and Horton were among the lands which Edward I granted for life to Roger Bigod, Earl of Norfolk. In 1302, on Roger's death in 1306 t
1 CONC hey reverted to the Crown.
1 CONT In 1308 Edward II gave Beckley to Hugh Despenser the elder, who later in the same year, leased the manor for life to his follower Sir John de Hadlow, who had been keeper of the manor and park in 1307. When the honor o£ St. Valery 
1 CONC was conferred upon Piers Gaveston in 1309, Beckley was excluded. ' [1]
1 CONT The authors used VCH Oxfordshire amongst their sources, but beyond this I have not yet read the entire webpage. Given that Beckley lands later wound up in Buckinghamshire, possibly VCH carries other details there as well.
0 @N6000000005076742514@ NOTE Comte de Dreux
1 CONT
1 CONT Robert III de Dreux, Comte de Dreux was born in 1185. He was the son of Robert II de Dreux, Comte de Dreux and Yolande de Courcy. He married Alianore de St. Valery, Dame de St. Valery, daughter of Thomas de St. Valery, Seigneur de
1 CONC  St. Valery and Adela de Ponthie, circa 1210. He died on 3 March 1234 at Braine, France.
1 CONT      Robert III de Dreux, Comte de Dreux gained the title of Comte de Dreux.
1 CONT Children of Robert III de Dreux, Comte de Dreux and Alianore de St. Valery, Dame de St. Valery
1 CONT Yolande de Dreux+ b. 1212, d. 1248
1 CONT Jean I de Dreux, Comte de Dreux+ b. 1215, d. c 1248
